      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"RENUM's body: ROM0's RAMRUN_C5D4 (its hidden entry $385F, RENUM's in the command table)\ncopies $0200 bytes from here ($C000-$C1FF) to $4F00 and runs them there, so its CALLs and\nJPs to $4Fxx/$50xx are to this code (RAM $4F00 = offset $0000).\n1. Reads the line range (FIRST, LAST), then LINE n (the new first number, default 10, kept\nin XCOORD's word) and STEP n (default 10, in AUTOSTEP); checking syntax ends there.\n2. Builds a table in the screen's page: at $8000 the old numbers of the lines from FIRST to\nLAST (high byte first, after the number of the line before FIRST), at $C000 + the same\noffset their new numbers. Error 33 when the table or a new number runs past $FFFF.\n3. Error 33 when the last new number reaches the line after LAST, or the first is below the\nline before FIRST.\n4. Renumbers PPC, the line references (RENUM_REFS), the lines themselves, EPPC and $5C6C\n(SDTOP), clears the screen and goes on at ROM0's $33D0 with PPC and SUBPPC stacked.\nEntry: the BASIC pointer past RENUM.\nError: 33 (no room for the numbers); 30 for a LINE or STEP number of 0.","comment":"New first number 10"},
        "3": {"comment":"XCOORD's word holds the new first number"},
        "6": {"comment":"AUTOSTEP holds the step"},
        "9": {"comment":"FIRST and LAST from the line range"},
        "12": {"comment":"The character after the range"},
        "13": {"comment":"LINE n: the new first number"},
        "16": {"comment":"LINE?"},
        "18": {"comment":"Read it (RENUM_READ_NUM)"},
        "21": {"comment":"STEP n: the step"},
        "24": {"comment":"STEP?"},
        "26": {"comment":"Read it (RENUM_READ_NUM)"},
        "29": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "32": {"comment":"Room for $18xx bytes? Error 1 if not"},
        "37": {"comment":"The screen's page at $8000 holds the table"},
        "40": {"comment":"HL' = the next new number"},
        "43": {"comment":"BC' = the step"},
        "47": {"comment":"DE' = the new numbers' half of the table"},
        "50": {"comment":"Back to the main registers"},
        "51": {"comment":"The old numbers' half starts at $8000"},
        "55": {"comment":"Line 0 to start"},
        "58": {"synopsis":"Stores the current line's old number in the table entry, stops past LAST, and steps to the\nnext line; lines before FIRST share the first entry.","comment":"The current entry"},
        "59": {"comment":"Old line number, high byte first"},
        "62": {"comment":"Back to the entry"},
        "64": {"comment":"Past LAST?"},
        "69": {"comment":"Yes: the table is done"},
        "71": {"comment":"DE = the next line's number; HL = FIRST"},
        "74": {"comment":"Still before FIRST?"},
        "77": {"comment":"Yes: overwrite the same entry"},
        "79": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "83": {"comment":"The new numbers"},
        "84": {"comment":"HL = the new half, DE = the new number"},
        "85": {"comment":"New number, high byte first"},
        "89": {"comment":"Table past $FFFF?"},
        "90": {"comment":"Yes: error"},
        "93": {"comment":"The next new number"},
        "94": {"comment":"Plus the step"},
        "95": {"comment":"Past 65535: error"},
        "97": {"comment":"Below $FF00?"},
        "99": {"comment":"A = the high byte + 1"},
        "100": {"comment":"Yes: the next line"},
        "102": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 33: the new numbers do not fit.","comment":"Stops with error code 33"},
        "104": {"synopsis":"The table is built: checks that the new numbers fit between the line before FIRST and the\nline after LAST, renumbers PPC, then the references and the lines.","comment":"Drop the table pointer"},
        "105": {"comment":"The first entry: the line before FIRST"},
        "108": {"comment":"TEMPW1 = it, bytes swapped"},
        "111": {"comment":"HMPR back from CURP"},
        "114": {"comment":"PPC: its new number"},
        "117": {"comment":"Map it (RENUM_MAP_WORD)"},
        "120": {"comment":"Kept for the restart at $33D0"},
        "121": {"comment":"SUBPPC"},
        "125": {"comment":"The line after LAST: none ($FFxx)?"},
        "129": {"comment":"Then the limit is $FF00"},
        "130": {"synopsis":"Compares the last new number with the line after LAST (or $FF00 when there is none): error\n33 when it is not below it.","comment":"No carry"},
        "131": {"comment":"The limit to DE'"},
        "132": {"comment":"HL' = the next new number"},
        "134": {"comment":"Less two steps: the last new number"},
        "138": {"comment":"Up to the line after the range?"},
        "140": {"comment":"Yes: error 33"},
        "142": {"comment":"The line before FIRST"},
        "145": {"comment":"DE = its number"},
        "147": {"comment":"The new first number"},
        "150": {"comment":"Below that line?"},
        "152": {"comment":"Yes: error 33"},
        "154": {"comment":"Renumber the references (RENUM_REFS)"},
        "157": {"comment":"FIRST"},
        "160": {"comment":"Find its line"},
        "163": {"synopsis":"Gives each line from FIRST on its new number (the line number is stored high byte first)\nuntil a line is past the table's range.","comment":"B, C = the line number, high byte first"},
        "167": {"comment":"Its new number (RENUM_LOOKUP)"},
        "171": {"comment":"Past the range: done"},
        "173": {"comment":"Store the new number"},
        "176": {"comment":"To the length word"},
        "178": {"comment":"BC = the line's length"},
        "182": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "183": {"comment":"Into the next page if past $BFFF"},
        "186": {"comment":"And on"},
        "188": {"synopsis":"Renumbers EPPC and the word at $5C6C (SDTOP), clears the screen and continues the program\nfrom the stacked PPC and SUBPPC through ROM0's $33D0.","comment":"EPPC: its new number"},
        "191": {"comment":"Map it (RENUM_MAP_WORD)"},
        "194": {"comment":"$5C6C (SDTOP) as well"},
        "196": {"comment":"Map it"},
        "199": {"comment":"The table spoiled the screen"},
        "202": {"comment":"Restart from PPC and SUBPPC on the stack"},
        "205": {"synopsis":"A hidden number not followed by TO, ',', ':' or CR (part of an expression): drops a\ncalculator value, then as RENUM_REF_SKIP.","comment":"Not a plain line number: drop a value"},
        "208": {"synopsis":"Leaves a reference alone: drops the three words RENUM_REF_NUMS stacked and goes on with the\nstatement (RENUM_REF_NEXT).","comment":"Drop the three saved words"},
        "211": {"comment":"On with the statement (RENUM_REF_NEXT)"},
        "214": {"synopsis":"Renumbers the line numbers written after the tokens of RENUM_TOKENS (IX walks the list\nthrough the copy at $50AB): for each token, searches the whole program from PROG for\nstatements that start with it (ROM0's FIND_STMT_E) and passes each to RENUM_REF_NUMS. LINE\ncounts only after a quote or a '$' (SAVE name LINE n). Called (at RAM $4FD6) by RENUM_CMD.\nEntry: the table built by RENUM_CMD.\nExit: at the end of the token list or of the program.","comment":"The token list (IX + 1 = RENUM_TOKENS)"},
        "218": {"synopsis":"The next token of the list: starts again at PROG, CLA and CHAD on its first line.","comment":"The next token"},
        "220": {"comment":"HL = PROG, paged in"},
        "223": {"comment":"The end of the program?"},
        "225": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "226": {"comment":"CLA = the line"},
        "229": {"comment":"Past the line number and length"},
        "233": {"comment":"CHAD = the line's text"},
        "236": {"synopsis":"Finds the next statement starting with the token at IX; returns at the list's end, moves on\nto the next token when there is none. Also the place each search goes on from.","comment":"The token"},
        "239": {"comment":"The end of the list?"},
        "241": {"comment":"E = the token"},
        "242": {"comment":"Find the next statement that starts with it"},
        "245": {"comment":"None: the next token"},
        "247": {"comment":"SUBPPC = its statement"},
        "250": {"comment":"CHADP = its page"},
        "255": {"comment":"The token again"},
        "258": {"comment":"LINE?"},
        "260": {"comment":"No: its numbers"},
        "262": {"comment":"The byte before the token"},
        "265": {"comment":"After a '$'?"},
        "267": {"comment":"Yes: SAVE name LINE n"},
        "269": {"comment":"After a quote?"},
        "271": {"comment":"No: not a line reference"},
        "273": {"synopsis":"Renumbers the line numbers after a token: skips TO, and for ON ($DE) everything up to the\n';'; counts the digits of the number's text, then takes the hidden number ($0E and 5 bytes)\nafter it. A number in the table gets its new value in the hidden number and its new digits\nin the text (the line's length changed by the difference, through ROM0's MAKE_ROOM or\nRECLAIM_BC); then a list goes on after each separator (RENUM_REF_NEXT).","comment":"The character after the token"},
        "274": {"synopsis":"RENUM_REF_NUMS after its RST $18: tests the character in A for TO. RENUM_REF_NEXT jumps here\n(at RAM $5012) for each number of a list.","comment":"TO?"},
        "276": {"comment":"No"},
        "278": {"comment":"Past TO"},
        "279": {"synopsis":"Keeps the number's place, B = -1 for the digit count, and skips to after the ';' when the\ntoken is ON ($DE).","comment":"Keep the number's place"},
        "280": {"comment":"B = -1: the digit count"},
        "282": {"comment":"ON?"},
        "284": {"comment":"No: count the digits"},
        "286": {"synopsis":"Steps through the text up to and past the ';' of ON.","comment":"Next character"},
        "287": {"comment":"Up to the ';'"},
        "291": {"comment":"Past the ';'"},
        "292": {"comment":"Drop the old place"},
        "293": {"comment":"The numbers start here"},
        "294": {"comment":"Hides $0127: INC HL / LD A,(HL)"},
        "297": {"synopsis":"Counts the digits of the number's text in B. The LD DE,$7E23 before it hides the loop's\nentry $0127 (INC HL, LD A,(HL)).","comment":"A digit?"},
        "300": {"comment":"Count it"},
        "301": {"comment":"Yes: the next character"},
        "303": {"comment":"B = the digit count"},
        "304": {"synopsis":"Skips spaces after the digits; anything but a hidden number ($0E) leaves the reference\nalone.","comment":"Skip spaces"},
        "310": {"comment":"Keep the place after it"},
        "311": {"comment":"A hidden number?"},
        "313": {"comment":"No: not a plain line number"},
        "315": {"comment":"The number to the calculator stack"},
        "318": {"comment":"CHAD past it"},
        "321": {"comment":"BC = the line number"},
        "324": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "325": {"comment":"TO, ',', ':' or CR?"},
        "328": {"comment":"No: an expression, skip it"},
        "330": {"comment":"BC = its new number (RENUM_LOOKUP)"},
        "333": {"comment":"Not renumbered: skip it"},
        "335": {"comment":"Stack the new number"},
        "338": {"comment":"HL = it on the stack"},
        "342": {"comment":"DE = the hidden number's 5 bytes"},
        "343": {"comment":"Copy the new value over them"},
        "346": {"comment":"Its text in PRNBUFF, C = its length"},
        "349": {"comment":"A = the old digit count"},
        "350": {"comment":"DE = the old digits"},
        "351": {"comment":"The line"},
        "354": {"comment":"The same length?"},
        "355": {"comment":"Yes: just copy the text"},
        "357": {"comment":"The line's length word"},
        "359": {"comment":"Keep the length"},
        "360": {"comment":"Keep the difference"},
        "361": {"comment":"BC = the line's length"},
        "365": {"comment":"HL = -difference, sign extended"},
        "371": {"comment":"The new length"},
        "374": {"comment":"Store it"},
        "378": {"comment":"The difference"},
        "381": {"comment":"Old text longer: shrink"},
        "383": {"comment":"Longer by A bytes"},
        "386": {"comment":"HL = the old digits"},
        "387": {"comment":"Open A bytes there"},
        "392": {"synopsis":"The old text is longer: reclaims the extra bytes at the old digits (ROM0's RECLAIM_BC).","comment":"C = the bytes too many"},
        "393": {"comment":"HL = the old digits"},
        "394": {"comment":"Reclaim them"},
        "397": {"synopsis":"The digits' room has the new length: C = the new length, then RENUM_COPY_TEXT.","comment":"DE = the digits"},
        "398": {"comment":"C = the new length"},
        "399": {"synopsis":"Copies the new digits from PRNBUFF over the old ones and moves CHAD past the hidden number.","comment":"From PRNBUFF"},
        "402": {"comment":"Copy the new digits"},
        "404": {"comment":"HL past them"},
        "405": {"comment":"Past the $0E and the 5 bytes"},
        "408": {"comment":"CHAD there"},
        "411": {"synopsis":"After a reference: at the end of the statement, or when no TO or separator follows, the\nsearch goes on (RENUM_FIND_STMT); otherwise past the separator to the next number\n(RENUM_REF_TO). Reached at RAM $509B.","comment":"At the end of the statement?"},
        "414": {"comment":"Yes: search on"},
        "417": {"comment":"TO, ',', ':' or CR?"},
        "420": {"comment":"No: search on"},
        "423": {"comment":"Past the separator"},
        "424": {"comment":"The next number of the list"},
        "427": {"synopsis":"The tokens followed by line numbers that RENUM_REFS renumbers, ended by 0: DELETE, ON ERROR,\nLINE, LLIST, LIST, RESTORE, GO TO, GO SUB, RUN. Read through IX (at RAM $50AB)."},
        "437": {"synopsis":"Reads the number after LINE or STEP for RENUM_CMD (called at RAM $50B5) and stores it at HL\nwhen running.\nEntry: HL = where it goes; the BASIC pointer on LINE or STEP.\nExit: carry when checking syntax; otherwise the word at HL set, A = the current character.\nError: 30 for 0.","comment":"Keep where it goes"},
        "438": {"comment":"A line number expression into BC"},
        "442": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "443": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "445": {"comment":"Yes: stops with error code 30"},
        "448": {"comment":"Store it"},
        "451": {"comment":"The current character"},
        "453": {"synopsis":"Gives the line number in the word at HL its new number when it is in the renumbered range\n(RENUM_LOOKUP). Called at RAM $50C5 for PPC, EPPC and SDTOP.\nEntry: HL = the word.\nExit: carry when it is not renumbered; BC = the new number otherwise.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC = the word"},
        "457": {"comment":"Its new number"},
        "461": {"comment":"Not renumbered"},
        "462": {"comment":"Store the new number"},
        "466": {"synopsis":"Finds the new number for line number BC: none (carry) when BC is below FIRST or past LAST;\notherwise the first table entry at or after BC (so a missing line takes the next line's\nnumber), read with the screen's page in HMPR. Called at RAM $50D2.\nEntry: BC = the old number.\nExit: no carry: BC = the new number; carry: not renumbered.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"Past LAST?"},
        "472": {"comment":"Yes: carry, not renumbered"},
        "473": {"comment":"FIRST"},
        "476": {"comment":"FIRST itself?"},
        "478": {"comment":"Yes: look it up"},
        "480": {"comment":"Below FIRST: carry"},
        "482": {"synopsis":"BC is in the range: pages the table in and searches it from $8002.","comment":"The table is in the screen's page"},
        "485": {"comment":"The first old number after the line before FIRST"},
        "488": {"synopsis":"Compares the entry at HL (high byte first) with BC.","comment":"High byte"},
        "489": {"comment":"Below, above or the same as B?"},
        "490": {"comment":"Not the same: decide on it"},
        "492": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "495": {"comment":"Compare it with C"},
        "496": {"synopsis":"Found when the entry is BC or above; otherwise the next entry.","comment":"This one or past: found"},
        "498": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "502": {"synopsis":"Reads the new number from the entry $4000 higher and puts HMPR back.","comment":"The new number's entry is $4000 higher"},
        "506": {"comment":"BC = the new number"},
        "509": {"comment":"HMPR back from CURP"},
        "512": {"synopsis":"GET's body: ROM0's GET_CMD copies $91 bytes from here to $4F00 and runs them there. Finds\nthe variable (ROM0's FIND_DEST), waits for a key, clicks and assigns it: a string variable\ngets the key as a one-character string (calculator operation $56), a numeric one the key's\nvalue as a digit ('0'-'9' 0-9, letters from 10 on, either case).\nEntry: the BASIC pointer at the variable.","comment":"The variable to assign"},
        "515": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "518": {"comment":"FLAGS"},
        "522": {"comment":"Clear bit 5"},
        "524": {"comment":"Wait for a key: A"},
        "528": {"comment":"A numeric variable?"},
        "530": {"comment":"Yes: the key's value"},
        "532": {"comment":"Stack the key's code"},
        "535": {"comment":"Operation $56 on it: a one-character string"},
        "538": {"comment":"Click and assign"},
        "540": {"synopsis":"A numeric variable: a digit's value, or a letter's value counted from 10.","comment":"A digit?"},
        "543": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "545": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "547": {"comment":"'A' to 10 and on"},
        "549": {"synopsis":"A digit: subtracts '0'.","comment":"'0' to 0"},
        "551": {"comment":"Stack the value"},
        "554": {"synopsis":"Clicks and assigns the value on the calculator stack (ROM0's ASSIGN_PAGE_CHAD).","comment":"The key click"},
        "557": {"comment":"Assign it, CHADP's page back"},
        "560": {"synopsis":"DELETE's body: ROM0's GET_CMD copies $91 bytes from here (its hidden entry $3885) to $4F00\nand runs them there. DELETE [n] TO [m]: deletes the program lines from n (default 1) to m\n(default $FEFF) with ROM0's RECLAIM_ABC, then prepares the program and continues (ROM0's\nPREP_CONTINUE). The first line's address and page are kept in FIRST's word and LAST's low\nbyte.\nEntry: the BASIC pointer past DELETE.\nError: 29 without TO.","comment":"Line 1 if no first number"},
        "563": {"comment":"Its address to FIRST's bytes"},
        "566": {"comment":"The current character"},
        "567": {"comment":"TO first?"},
        "569": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "571": {"comment":"The first line's number"},
        "574": {"comment":"Running: its address to FIRST's bytes"},
        "578": {"comment":"TO?"},
        "580": {"comment":"No: stops with error code 29"},
        "583": {"synopsis":"Past TO: the last line number, $FEFF when the statement ends here.","comment":"Past TO"},
        "584": {"comment":"The end of the statement?"},
        "587": {"comment":"Then up to $FEFF"},
        "590": {"comment":"Else the last line's number"},
        "593": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "596": {"comment":"No"},
        "598": {"comment":"Find the last line"},
        "601": {"comment":"Not there: HL is the line after it"},
        "603": {"comment":"DE = the line after it"},
        "607": {"synopsis":"HL = the line after the last one to delete; checking syntax ends here, running reclaims the\nbytes from the first line up to it.","comment":"Into the next page if past $BFFF"},
        "610": {"comment":"D = its page"},
        "613": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "616": {"comment":"The first line's page"},
        "620": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "623": {"comment":"A:HL = the end"},
        "624": {"comment":"C:DE = the first line"},
        "628": {"comment":"The length"},
        "631": {"comment":"Nothing to delete"},
        "632": {"comment":"BC = the bytes, A = the pages"},
        "634": {"comment":"HL = the first line"},
        "635": {"comment":"Reclaim the lines"},
        "638": {"comment":"Prepare the program, on with the next statement"},
        "641": {"synopsis":"Finds line HL and keeps its address in FIRST's word and its page in LAST's low byte (called\nat RAM $4F51), then puts CHADP's page back.\nEntry: HL = the line number.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Find line HL"},
        "644": {"comment":"Into the next page if past $BFFF"},
        "647": {"comment":"FIRST's word = its address"},
        "652": {"comment":"LAST's low byte = its page"},
        "655": {"comment":"CHADP's page back"},
        "658": {"synopsis":"KEYIN's body: ROM0's KEYIN_CMD copies $51 bytes from here to $4B00 and runs them there.\nKEYIN string: copies the string (at most $1FF bytes) into the emptied edit line, turns its\nkeywords into tokens (ROM0's RAMRUN_C533), checks its syntax and, without an error, enters\nit into the program when it starts with a line number or runs it otherwise; then empties the\nedit line and continues after the KEYIN (ROM0's $33D0 with PPC and SUBPPC stacked). An error\nin the check comes back here (ROM0's TRAP_NEXT_CALL).\nEntry: the BASIC pointer past KEYIN.\nError: 27 for a string that is too long; 29 for a line number that is too big.","comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "661": {"comment":"At most $1FF bytes"},
        "663": {"comment":"The string to the buffer at $4F00"},
        "666": {"comment":"Empty: nothing to do"},
        "667": {"comment":"PPC"},
        "671": {"comment":"SUBPPC"},
        "675": {"comment":"The text, $4F00"},
        "676": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "677": {"comment":"Empty the edit line"},
        "682": {"comment":"HL = ELINE"},
        "685": {"comment":"Room for the text"},
        "688": {"comment":"DE = the room"},
        "690": {"comment":"From the buffer"},
        "691": {"comment":"The text into the edit line"},
        "693": {"comment":"An error in the next call returns here"},
        "696": {"comment":"Turn keywords into tokens"},
        "699": {"comment":"Check the line's syntax"},
        "702": {"comment":"An error?"},
        "706": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "708": {"comment":"FLAGS: running"},
        "713": {"comment":"BC = the line number at the start"},
        "716": {"comment":"Too big: stops with error code 29"},
        "719": {"comment":"A line number: into the program"},
        "721": {"comment":"Statement 1"},
        "722": {"comment":"Run the edit line"},
        "725": {"comment":"No ENTER_LINE"},
        "726": {"synopsis":"Puts the edit line into the program (ROM0's ENTER_LINE) unless carry is set.","comment":"Put the line into the program"},
        "729": {"synopsis":"Puts ERRSP back, leaves the editor, empties the edit line and continues after the KEYIN.","comment":"ERRSP as it was"},
        "730": {"comment":"Leave the editor"},
        "733": {"comment":"Empty the edit line"},
        "736": {"comment":"Back to PPC and SUBPPC"},
        "739": {"synopsis":"POP's body: ROM0's GET_CMD copies $91 bytes from here (its hidden entry $3889) to $4F00 and\nruns them there. POP [variable]: takes the top entry off the BASIC stack (ROM0's BSTK_POP);\nwith a numeric variable, assigns it the number of the line the entry returns to (0 for an\naddress below $0100). A procedure's entry (type $40) also undoes its LOCALs (ROM0's\nUNWIND_LOCALS).\nEntry: the BASIC pointer past POP.\nError: 11 when the BASIC stack is empty; 29 for a string variable.","comment":"The end of the statement?"},
        "742": {"comment":"No: a numeric variable to assign"},
        "745": {"comment":"Keep Z: no variable"},
        "746": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "751": {"comment":"BSTKEND"},
        "754": {"comment":"The BASIC stack empty ($FF)?"},
        "756": {"comment":"No"},
        "758": {"comment":"Stops with error code 11"},
        "760": {"synopsis":"Takes the top entry off the BASIC stack; without a variable only checks its type.","comment":"Take the top entry off"},
        "763": {"comment":"B = its type and page"},
        "764": {"comment":"Z: no variable"},
        "765": {"comment":"Keep the type"},
        "766": {"comment":"No variable: only the stack"},
        "768": {"comment":"An address below $0100?"},
        "770": {"comment":"Then line 0"},
        "774": {"comment":"The line's page"},
        "778": {"comment":"DE = its line number"},
        "781": {"synopsis":"Stacks the line number in DE and assigns it to the variable."},
        "782": {"comment":"Stack it"},
        "785": {"comment":"Assign it to the variable"},
        "788": {"synopsis":"A procedure's entry (bits 7-5 = $40): undoes its LOCALs through ROM0's UNWIND_LOCALS.","comment":"The type"},
        "789": {"comment":"Bits 7-5"},
        "791": {"comment":"A procedure's entry?"},
        "793": {"comment":"Yes: undo its LOCALs too"},
        "797": {"synopsis":"INPUT's body: ROM0's RAMRUN_C5D4 (its hidden entry $385B, INPUT's in the command table)\ncopies $0200 bytes from here to $4F00 and runs them there (RAM $4F00 = offset $031D), so its\nCALLs and JPs to $4Fxx/$50xx are to this code. When running clears the lower window first;\nsets DFLAG to 1, runs the items (INPUT_ITEMS), clears FLAGE, ends a syntax check there; then\nclears the lower window again and sets SCRCT from SPOSNU's high byte and UWTOP.\nEntry: the BASIC pointer past INPUT.","comment":"Running?"},
        "800": {"comment":"Yes: clear the lower window"},
        "806": {"comment":"DFLAG = 1"},
        "810": {"comment":"The items (INPUT_ITEMS)"},
        "814": {"comment":"FLAGE = 0"},
        "817": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "820": {"comment":"Clear the lower window"},
        "823": {"comment":"SPOSNU's high byte"},
        "826": {"comment":"UWTOP"},
        "829": {"comment":"Rows from UWTOP to it"},
        "831": {"comment":"SCRCT"},
        "835": {"synopsis":"The INPUT items up to the end of the statement (called at RAM $4F26): separators are printed\n(ROM0's PRINT_SEPARATOR), anything else is an item (INPUT_ITEM); at the end a newline when\nDEVICE is the upper window.","comment":"The current character"},
        "836": {"comment":"The end of the statement?"},
        "839": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "841": {"comment":"A separator? Printed"},
        "844": {"comment":"The end follows: done"},
        "845": {"comment":"Not a separator: an item"},
        "848": {"comment":"And on"},
        "850": {"synopsis":"The end of the items: a newline (ROM0's PRINT_NEWLINE) when DEVICE is 0, the upper window.","comment":"DEVICE"},
        "853": {"comment":"The upper window?"},
        "854": {"comment":"Yes: a newline"},
        "858": {"synopsis":"One INPUT item (called at RAM $4F3D): '(' prints the items inside as a prompt, LINE reads a\nstring variable as typed, a letter reads a variable, anything else is printed (ROM0's\nPRINT_ITEM).\nEntry: A = the current character.","comment":"'('?"},
        "860": {"comment":"No"},
        "862": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "863": {"comment":"Print the items inside"},
        "867": {"comment":"')' must follow"},
        "870": {"synopsis":"Not '(': LINE, a variable, or an item to print.","comment":"LINE?"},
        "872": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "874": {"comment":"A letter?"},
        "877": {"comment":"No: print the item as a prompt"},
        "880": {"comment":"The variable"},
        "883": {"comment":"FLAGE bit 7 clear: not LINE"},
        "890": {"synopsis":"INPUT LINE: finds the variable after LINE, which must be a string (error 29), and sets FLAGE\nbit 7.","comment":"The variable after LINE"},
        "893": {"comment":"Running? Sign: numeric"},
        "896": {"comment":"A number: stops with error code 29"},
        "899": {"comment":"FLAGE bit 7: LINE"},
        "904": {"synopsis":"Reads a value for the variable found (ends a syntax check first): empties the workspace and\nputs a starting text in it, a CR for a number or LINE, \"\" and a CR for a string, with KCUR\non the CR (on the closing quote for a string); FLAGE bits 5 and 6 set (bit 6 cleared for a\nstring). Then edits it: LINE with ROM0's ED_START_CLR, otherwise with errors coming back to\nINPUT_RETRY until the text checks; and assigns the result.","comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "908": {"comment":"Empty the workspace"},
        "912": {"comment":"FLAGE bits 5 and 6"},
        "916": {"comment":"One byte for a number"},
        "919": {"comment":"Numeric?"},
        "922": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "925": {"comment":"Bit 6 clear: a string"},
        "927": {"comment":"LINE?"},
        "929": {"comment":"Yes: one byte"},
        "931": {"comment":"A string: two quotes and the CR"},
        "933": {"synopsis":"Opens C bytes in the workspace (1 or 3, reached at RAM $4F88 for a number) and writes the CR\nand the quotes.","comment":"Room in the workspace"},
        "936": {"comment":"CR at the end"},
        "938": {"comment":"A number or LINE?"},
        "939": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "941": {"comment":"The quote before the CR"},
        "944": {"comment":"And one at the start"},
        "946": {"synopsis":"KCUR and KCURP = the CR, or the closing quote for a string; LINE goes to the editor at once,\notherwise CHADP, CHAD and ERRSP are kept first.","comment":"KCUR = the CR, or the closing quote"},
        "949": {"comment":"KCURP = its page"},
        "954": {"comment":"FLAGE"},
        "957": {"comment":"LINE?"},
        "958": {"comment":"Yes: edit it"},
        "960": {"comment":"CHADP"},
        "964": {"comment":"CHAD"},
        "968": {"comment":"ERRSP"},
        "972": {"synopsis":"Where an error while the typed text is checked comes back to (the address $4FAF it stacks,\nwith ERRSP pointing at it for channels K and S): clears ERRNR, takes the hidden numbers out\nof the workspace, edits the text again (ROM0's ED_START), turns keywords into tokens and\nchecks the text (INPUT_EVAL with FLAGS bit 7 clear).","comment":"An error comes back here (RAM $4FAF)"},
        "976": {"comment":"ERRNR = 0"},
        "980": {"comment":"Channel K or S?"},
        "983": {"comment":"No"},
        "985": {"comment":"Errors return to $4FAF (INPUT_RETRY)"},
        "989": {"synopsis":"Takes the hidden numbers out of the workspace text, edits it, tokenises it and checks it.","comment":"The workspace"},
        "992": {"comment":"Take its hidden numbers out"},
        "995": {"comment":"Edit the line"},
        "998": {"comment":"Turn keywords into tokens"},
        "1001": {"comment":"FLAGS: checking syntax"},
        "1006": {"comment":"Check the text (INPUT_EVAL)"},
        "1009": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "1010": {"synopsis":"With carry (INPUT LINE): edits the workspace with ROM0's ED_START_CLR; then shows the text\non channels K and S (ROM1 $DC62 at OLDPOS) and assigns it.","comment":"LINE: edit with ED_START_CLR"},
        "1013": {"comment":"Channel K or S?"},
        "1016": {"comment":"No"},
        "1018": {"comment":"KCUR's high byte = CLET ('K' or 'S')"},
        "1021": {"comment":"Draw the line again ($F494)"},
        "1024": {"comment":"OLDPOS"},
        "1027": {"comment":"ROM1 $DC62"},
        "1030": {"comment":"Run it with ROM1 paged in"},
        "1033": {"synopsis":"Clears FLAGE bits 7 and 5; LINE assigns the workspace text up to its CR as a string,\nanything else is evaluated (INPUT_NUM_EVAL).","comment":"FLAGE"},
        "1037": {"comment":"Clear bit 7"},
        "1039": {"comment":"Clear bit 5"},
        "1041": {"comment":"LINE?"},
        "1042": {"comment":"No"},
        "1044": {"comment":"The workspace"},
        "1047": {"comment":"DE = the text"},
        "1049": {"comment":"BC = -1"},
        "1052": {"synopsis":"Counts the workspace text up to its CR in BC.","comment":"Count up to the CR"},
        "1059": {"comment":"Stack the text as a string"},
        "1062": {"comment":"Assign it"},
        "1065": {"synopsis":"Drops the error return, puts ERRSP back, keeps CHAD and CHADP in PRPTR and PRPTRP, evaluates\nand assigns the text when running (INPUT_EVAL), and puts CHAD back.","comment":"Drop the error return"},
        "1066": {"comment":"ERRSP as it was"},
        "1070": {"comment":"CHAD to PRPTR"},
        "1074": {"comment":"CHADP to PRPTRP"},
        "1078": {"comment":"FLAGS: running"},
        "1083": {"comment":"Evaluate and assign (INPUT_EVAL)"},
        "1086": {"comment":"CHAD's page back"},
        "1092": {"comment":"CHAD back"},
        "1099": {"synopsis":"Evaluates the text in the workspace (called at RAM $502E): CHAD and CHADP to WORKSP; STOP\nstops with error 17 when running; otherwise the expression is assigned to the variable of\nFLAGE's type (ROM0's LET_EXPR_ASSIGN after its first instruction) and must end the text.\nEntry: FLAGS bit 7 = running; FLAGE bit 6 = numeric.\nError: 17 for STOP; 29 when more follows.","comment":"WORKSP"},
        "1102": {"comment":"CHAD = it"},
        "1105": {"comment":"WORKSPP"},
        "1108": {"comment":"CHADP = it"},
        "1111": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "1112": {"comment":"STOP?"},
        "1114": {"comment":"No"},
        "1116": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "1119": {"comment":"No: fine"},
        "1120": {"comment":"Stops with error code 17"},
        "1122": {"synopsis":"Evaluates the text as a value of FLAGE's type and assigns it; anything after it is error 29.","comment":"FLAGE: the variable's type"},
        "1125": {"comment":"Evaluate and assign"},
        "1129": {"comment":"The end of the text?"},
        "1131": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "1132": {"comment":"Stops with error code 29"},
        "1134": {"synopsis":"DEF KEYCODE's body: ROM0's GET_CMD copies $91 bytes from here (its hidden entry $388D) to\n$4F00 and runs them there. DEF KEYCODE n, string (or ';') sets key n's text to the string;\nDEF KEYCODE n followed by the rest of the line takes that rest (up to its CR) and goes on\nwith the next line (the return address becomes ROM0's LINE_END); when checking syntax that\nform goes on through ROM0's STMT_END_STRIP. The key's old entry in the DKDEF list is\nremoved; an empty text only removes it.\nEntry: the BASIC pointer past DEF KEYCODE.\nError: 30 for a key number below $C0 or of $FF; 52 when the list would pass DKLIM.","comment":"The key number"},
        "1137": {"comment":"A comma or ';'?"},
        "1140": {"comment":"Yes: a string follows"},
        "1142": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "1145": {"comment":"No: check the rest of the line"},
        "1148": {"comment":"DE = the text's start"},
        "1149": {"comment":"NXTLINE"},
        "1153": {"comment":"Less the start, less 1"},
        "1155": {"comment":"BC = the length without the CR"},
        "1158": {"comment":"The text starts after the separator"},
        "1159": {"comment":"Return to LINE_END: on with the next line"},
        "1165": {"synopsis":"The text is a string expression: DE, BC = the string, paged in.","comment":"The string"},
        "1168": {"comment":"DE = it, BC = its length"},
        "1171": {"synopsis":"Takes the key number ($C0-$FE) and removes the key's entry from the DKDEF list when there is\none: the entries after it move down.","comment":"The text"},
        "1172": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "1173": {"comment":"A = the key number"},
        "1177": {"comment":"Below $C0 or $FF?"},
        "1179": {"comment":"Stops with error code 30"},
        "1183": {"comment":"Keep the key"},
        "1184": {"comment":"Is it defined?"},
        "1187": {"comment":"No"},
        "1189": {"comment":"Past its 3-byte head"},
        "1192": {"comment":"The text"},
        "1193": {"comment":"The next entry's text"},
        "1195": {"comment":"HL = the end marker's text"},
        "1200": {"comment":"The bytes from the next entry to the end"},
        "1205": {"comment":"HL = the next entry's text"},
        "1206": {"comment":"Back to its head"},
        "1209": {"comment":"DE = this entry's text"},
        "1210": {"comment":"Back to its head"},
        "1213": {"comment":"Move the rest down over it"},
        "1215": {"synopsis":"Adds the key's new entry at the end of the list (key, length word, text) and a new end\nmarker, unless the length is 0 or $FFxx.","comment":"The key"},
        "1216": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "1218": {"comment":"A length of $FFxx?"},
        "1221": {"comment":"Yes: only remove"},
        "1223": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "1224": {"synopsis":"Length 0 (or $FFxx): done through ROM0's POP_AF_HL_RET; otherwise the room check.","comment":"Yes: only remove (POP_AF_HL_RET)"},
        "1228": {"comment":"HL = the end marker's text"},
        "1232": {"comment":"Keep it"},
        "1233": {"comment":"The new end"},
        "1235": {"comment":"DKLIM"},
        "1238": {"comment":"Past it?"},
        "1240": {"comment":"Yes: stops with error code 52"},
        "1244": {"comment":"The new end marker"},
        "1246": {"comment":"The old marker's text"},
        "1247": {"comment":"The new entry's head"},
        "1250": {"comment":"The key"},
        "1251": {"comment":"The text"},
        "1252": {"comment":"The key"},
        "1254": {"comment":"The length"},
        "1260": {"comment":"The text"},
        "1263": {"synopsis":"DEF FN's body: ROM0's GET_CMD copies $91 bytes from here (its hidden entry $3891) to $4F00\nand runs them there. When running, skips the statement (ROM0's SKIP_STATEMENT). When\nchecking syntax: the name, an optional list of one-letter parameters (each with an optional\n'$') in brackets, each given a hidden number's place after it (ROM0's INSERT_NUM_SLOT), '='\nand an expression of the name's type.\nEntry: the BASIC pointer past DEF FN.\nError: 29.","comment":"Running?"},
        "1266": {"comment":"Yes: skip the statement"},
        "1269": {"comment":"The name"},
        "1270": {"comment":"A = 1 for a string name"},
        "1273": {"comment":"Keep it"},
        "1274": {"comment":"CHAD past the name"},
        "1278": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "1280": {"comment":"No"},
        "1283": {"comment":"')' at once?"},
        "1285": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "1287": {"synopsis":"One parameter: a letter, an optional '$', a hidden number's place; then ')' or a comma and\nthe next.","comment":"A parameter's letter"},
        "1290": {"comment":"Past the letter"},
        "1292": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "1294": {"comment":"No"},
        "1296": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "1297": {"synopsis":"Opens the hidden number's place after the parameter and moves CHAD there.","comment":"A hidden number's place after it"},
        "1300": {"comment":"CHAD there"},
        "1305": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "1307": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "1309": {"comment":"Else a comma"},
        "1312": {"comment":"The next parameter"},
        "1314": {"synopsis":"Steps past the ')'.","comment":"Past ')'"},
        "1315": {"synopsis":"Requires '=' and the expression; its type must be the name's (B = 1 for a string name, Z\nfrom ROM0's NEXT_EXPR for a string).","comment":"'='?"},
        "1317": {"comment":"No: error 29"},
        "1319": {"comment":"The expression: Z for a string"},
        "1322": {"comment":"B = 1 for a string name"},
        "1323": {"comment":"A string?"},
        "1325": {"comment":"A number: a numeric name?"},
        "1326": {"comment":"Yes: fine"},
        "1327": {"synopsis":"A string expression: fine when the name is a string's.","comment":"A string name?"},
        "1328": {"comment":"Yes: fine"},
        "1329": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 29.","comment":"Stops with error code 29"},
        "1331": {"synopsis":"Turns keywords typed in letters into tokens in a line of text: ROM0's RAMRUN_C533 (and\nRAMRUN_C533_X) copies $A1 bytes from here to $4D80 and runs them there (RAM $4D80 = offset\n$0533). Steps through the text from the caller's DE up to its CR: strings and the byte after\na $FF are skipped; a word starting with a letter, '<' or '>' is looked up in the keyword\nlist ($C5 entries from ROM1 $F8C9, through ROM0's JT_018A on a copy of 15 bytes at $4E23); a\nmatch is replaced by its token (keyword n: n + $3B, INK becoming PEN's $A1; below $4A: $FF\nand n + $3A), taking one space before and one after it; a word with no match goes to MTOKV\nwhen that is set (NZ from it counts as a match) and is otherwise skipped. A REM token ends\nthe work.\nEntry: the caller's registers in the alternates (RAMRUN_C533_X's EXX): DE = the text.\nExit: at the text's CR or after REM.","comment":"The caller's registers back"},
        "1332": {"comment":"HL = the text"},
        "1333": {"synopsis":"Goes on with the text at HL (reached at RAM $4D82 after each token)."},
        "1334": {"comment":"Look at it"},
        "1336": {"synopsis":"No keyword here: skips the rest of the name (letters and '_') when it starts with a letter.\nThe CP $23 hides the loop's entry $0540 (INC HL).","comment":"The word's start"},
        "1339": {"comment":"Below 'A'?"},
        "1341": {"comment":"Yes: on"},
        "1343": {"comment":"Hides $0540: INC HL"},
        "1346": {"comment":"A letter?"},
        "1349": {"comment":"Yes: skip it"},
        "1351": {"comment":"'_'?"},
        "1353": {"comment":"Yes: skip it"},
        "1355": {"synopsis":"Keeps CHAD on the character at HL and decides what it starts. The CP $E7 hides the entry\n$054F: RST $20, the next character.","comment":"CHAD = here"},
        "1358": {"comment":"Hides $054F: RST $20, the next character"},
        "1361": {"comment":"The end of the line?"},
        "1363": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "1364": {"comment":"A letter?"},
        "1367": {"comment":"Yes: a word"},
        "1369": {"comment":"'<'?"},
        "1371": {"comment":"Yes: maybe <> or <="},
        "1373": {"comment":"'>'?"},
        "1375": {"comment":"Yes: maybe >="},
        "1378": {"comment":"$FF, a function prefix?"},
        "1380": {"comment":"Yes: skip it and its code"},
        "1383": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "1385": {"comment":"No: the next character"},
        "1387": {"synopsis":"Skips a string up to its closing quote or the CR.","comment":"Skip the string"},
        "1389": {"comment":"The end of the line?"},
        "1391": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "1392": {"comment":"The closing quote?"},
        "1396": {"synopsis":"Steps past one more byte and goes on with the text.","comment":"Past it"},
        "1399": {"comment":"And on"},
        "1401": {"synopsis":"Copies 15 bytes of the text to $4E23 and matches them against the keyword list; with no\nmatch calls MTOKV when it is set.","comment":"Keep the word's start"},
        "1403": {"comment":"Copy 15 bytes to $4E23"},
        "1412": {"comment":"DE = the copy"},
        "1413": {"comment":"The keyword list, less 2"},
        "1416": {"comment":"$C5 keywords"},
        "1418": {"comment":"Match one: A = its number"},
        "1421": {"comment":"Found"},
        "1423": {"comment":"MTOKV"},
        "1426": {"comment":"Set?"},
        "1428": {"comment":"Yes: call it"},
        "1431": {"comment":"No match: skip the name"},
        "1433": {"synopsis":"A keyword matched: DE = past it in the text; writes its token (a function or operator as $FF\nand a code)."},
        "1435": {"comment":"The keyword's length"},
        "1437": {"comment":"The word's start"},
        "1439": {"comment":"DE = past the keyword in the line"},
        "1440": {"comment":"A function or operator?"},
        "1442": {"comment":"No: a statement"},
        "1444": {"comment":"Its code"},
        "1446": {"comment":"After the $FF prefix"},
        "1451": {"synopsis":"A statement keyword: token = A + $3B, $FF (INK) becoming $A1 (PEN).","comment":"The token"},
        "1453": {"comment":"INK ($FF)?"},
        "1455": {"comment":"No"},
        "1457": {"comment":"Then PEN's token"},
        "1459": {"synopsis":"Puts the token over a space just before the word.","comment":"The byte before the word"},
        "1460": {"comment":"Keep the token"},
        "1462": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "1464": {"comment":"Yes: the token goes over it"},
        "1467": {"synopsis":"Gets the token back from AF'.","comment":"The token"},
        "1468": {"synopsis":"Stores the token and skips one space after the keyword.","comment":"Store it"},
        "1470": {"comment":"HL = past the keyword"},
        "1471": {"comment":"A space after it?"},
        "1474": {"comment":"No"},
        "1476": {"comment":"Drop it too"},
        "1477": {"synopsis":"Reclaims the rest of the keyword's text; after REM returns, otherwise goes on after the\ntoken."},
        "1478": {"comment":"Reclaim the rest of the word"},
        "1482": {"comment":"HL = past the token"},
        "1484": {"comment":"The token"},
        "1486": {"comment":"REM?"},
        "1488": {"comment":"No: tokenise on"},
        "1491": {"comment":"REM: the rest is left as text"},
        "1492": {"synopsis":"MERGE's body: ROM0's RAMRUN_C5D4 copies $0200 bytes from here to $4F00 and runs them there\n(RAM $4F00 = offset $05D4; the copy reaches into the calculator's table, which is not used\nthere). Makes room for the file in the workspace before a $FF end marker (its size from the\n3-byte pointer at $4B72), loads it (ROM0's JLDVD), merges its lines (MERGE_LINES), its\nnumeric variables (MERGE_NUM_VARS), drops what is left of that part (the size from the\npointers at $4B60 and $4B66, probably the file's numeric variables), and merges each string\nand array variable, deleting the program's one of the same name first; then prepares the\nprogram and goes on (ROM0's PREP_CONTINUE).","comment":"Empty the workspace"},
        "1495": {"comment":"One byte in it"},
        "1501": {"comment":"An end marker, $FF"},
        "1504": {"comment":"C:DE = the pointer at $4B72: the size"},
        "1510": {"comment":"A:BC = the size"},
        "1513": {"comment":"Room for it before the $FF"},
        "1519": {"comment":"Load the file's data there"},
        "1522": {"comment":"Merge its lines (MERGE_LINES)"},
        "1525": {"comment":"Merge its numeric variables"},
        "1528": {"comment":"The pointer at $4B60"},
        "1531": {"comment":"C:DE = it"},
        "1536": {"comment":"And the one at $4B66"},
        "1541": {"comment":"A:HL = it"},
        "1545": {"comment":"The difference"},
        "1548": {"comment":"Plus 1"},
        "1556": {"comment":"At the workspace's start"},
        "1559": {"comment":"BC = the bytes"},
        "1560": {"comment":"A = the pages"},
        "1561": {"comment":"Reclaim them"},
        "1564": {"synopsis":"One string or array variable from the workspace (type/length byte, 10 name bytes, a 3-byte\nlength, the data): its type and name to $513F, the program's variable of that name deleted\n(ROM0's FIND_SAVARS, DELETE_STRVAR), room made at the end of the program's variables (ELINE\n- 1), the variable copied there (JFARLDIR's body at $2A5E) and deleted from the workspace.\nThe $FF end marker ends the merge.","comment":"The workspace"},
        "1567": {"comment":"The end marker?"},
        "1569": {"comment":"Yes: prepare the program and go on"},
        "1572": {"comment":"The type and name to $513F"},
        "1575": {"comment":"C = the name's length + 1"},
        "1577": {"comment":"BC = type byte and name"},
        "1580": {"comment":"A = the type byte"},
        "1581": {"comment":"Copy them"},
        "1583": {"comment":"The same variable in the program?"},
        "1586": {"comment":"Yes: delete it"},
        "1589": {"comment":"The workspace"},
        "1592": {"comment":"Past the type byte and name"},
        "1596": {"comment":"A = the length's pages"},
        "1598": {"comment":"DE = the length's bytes"},
        "1602": {"comment":"Plus the 14-byte head"},
        "1604": {"comment":"A:HL = the whole size"},
        "1609": {"comment":"The end of the variables, ELINE - 1"},
        "1616": {"comment":"Room there"},
        "1619": {"comment":"C:DE = the room"},
        "1624": {"comment":"The size's bytes, $0000-$3FFF"},
        "1626": {"comment":"MODCOUNT"},
        "1630": {"comment":"PAGCOUNT"},
        "1633": {"comment":"A:HL = the workspace"},
        "1638": {"comment":"Copy the variable into the room"},
        "1641": {"comment":"The workspace"},
        "1644": {"comment":"Delete the copy there"},
        "1647": {"comment":"The next variable"},
        "1649": {"synopsis":"Moves each line in the workspace into the program (called at RAM $4F9D): a program line of\nthe same number is deleted first (ROM0's RECLAIM_LINE), room is made where the line belongs,\nthe line is copied there and taken out of the workspace.\nEntry: none (the lines at WORKSP).\nExit: HL past the $FF that ends them.","comment":"The workspace"},
        "1652": {"synopsis":"The next line at HL (its number high byte first); $FF ends them.","comment":"B = the line number's high byte"},
        "1654": {"comment":"The end marker ($FF)?"},
        "1656": {"comment":"Yes: HL past it"},
        "1657": {"comment":"C = the low byte"},
        "1658": {"comment":"Find that line in the program"},
        "1661": {"comment":"Keep where it is"},
        "1662": {"comment":"And its page"},
        "1665": {"comment":"There already: delete it"},
        "1668": {"comment":"The workspace"},
        "1671": {"comment":"The length word"},
        "1673": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "1676": {"comment":"Plus the 4-byte head"},
        "1685": {"comment":"The program's page"},
        "1688": {"comment":"Room for the line"},
        "1691": {"comment":"The workspace"},
        "1695": {"comment":"Split the length into pages and bytes"},
        "1699": {"comment":"C = the program's page"},
        "1700": {"comment":"DE = the room"},
        "1701": {"comment":"Copy the line there"},
        "1704": {"comment":"The workspace"},
        "1707": {"comment":"Take the line out of it"},
        "1710": {"comment":"The next line"},
        "1712": {"synopsis":"Merges the loaded numeric variables (called at RAM $4FDC): for each letter a-z, the word at\nHL leads to its chain ($FFFF none); each variable that is neither hidden nor out of use is\nassigned by name into the program's variables (MERGE_NUM_CHAIN).\nEntry: HL = the 26 words, one per letter.","comment":"'a'"},
        "1714": {"synopsis":"Keeps the letter at $5140 and merges its chain when there is one.","comment":"The letter"},
        "1717": {"comment":"DE = the letter's first variable"},
        "1720": {"comment":"None ($FFFF)?"},
        "1721": {"comment":"No: merge the chain"},
        "1725": {"comment":"The next letter"},
        "1729": {"comment":"Past 'z'?"},
        "1731": {"comment":"No"},
        "1734": {"synopsis":"Merges one letter's chain of numeric variables (called at RAM $4FF2): each variable\n(type/length byte, a link word, the letters after the first, the 5-byte value) is assigned\nby its name, built at $513F-$5141 on, through ROM0's ASSIGN_NUM_TYPE; the link counts from\nits own high byte and $FFFF ends the chain.\nEntry: HL = the word before the first variable; DE = its link, D + 1.\nExit: HL as on entry."},
        "1735": {"synopsis":"The next variable of the chain: HL = the link's address + the link.","comment":"HL = the variable"},
        "1737": {"comment":"The type/length byte"},
        "1738": {"comment":"Hidden (bit 7) or no longer in use (bit 5)?"},
        "1740": {"comment":"Yes: skip it"},
        "1742": {"comment":"Keep the page"},
        "1747": {"comment":"C = the name's length less 1: the letters after the first"},
        "1751": {"comment":"Without the FOR-NEXT bit"},
        "1753": {"comment":"The type byte to $513F"},
        "1756": {"comment":"Past the type byte and the link"},
        "1759": {"comment":"A one-letter name"},
        "1763": {"comment":"The other letters to $5141, after the first at $5140"},
        "1768": {"synopsis":"Stacks the variable's value and assigns it by the name at $513F, then puts the page back.","comment":"The value to the calculator stack"},
        "1771": {"comment":"Assign it by the name at $513F"},
        "1775": {"comment":"The page back"},
        "1778": {"synopsis":"Reads the variable's link: $FFFF ends the chain.","comment":"The link"},
        "1782": {"comment":"The end of the chain ($FFFF)?"},
        "1783": {"comment":"No: the next variable"},
        "1787": {"synopsis":"The calculator's operation table: one word per operation code $00-$5D, the routine\nCALC_TABLE_OP returns to. Most are in ROM1; $06 ($1897), $1C ($187F), $1D ($1883) and $46\n($1877) are ROM0 routines, and $0B, $4E and $50 point to ROM0's STOP_ERR29."},
        "1975": {"synopsis":"The calculator: runs the operation bytes at IX (ROM0's CALC_ENTRY calls it). Each operation\nreturns to CALC_NEXT_OP, which keeps DE as STKEND. Before each operation RST28V is called\nwith A = the code when it is set. Codes $00-$1F take two values (DE = the top value, HL =\nthe one below), $20-$5F one (DE = STKEND, HL = the top value), both through CALC_OP_TABLE;\n$C8-$FF store, recall and stack constants (past this range); $60-$C7 stop with error code\n51.\nEntry: IX = the operation bytes.\nError: 51 for a code $60-$C7.","comment":"STKEND"},
        "1979": {"synopsis":"Where every operation returns ($C7BB): pushes its own address again as the next operation's\nreturn address, sets STKEND = DE and takes the next operation byte at IX.","comment":"The return address for every operation"},
        "1983": {"comment":"STKEND = DE"},
        "1987": {"comment":"The operation code"},
        "1992": {"synopsis":"Runs operation A: calls RST28V when set, then sorts the code into its group. ROM1 $C805\ncomes here with A from $5B87 (BCREG's high byte).","comment":"RST28V"},
        "1995": {"comment":"Set?"},
        "1997": {"comment":"Yes: call it, A = the code"},
        "2002": {"comment":"$00-$1F, two values?"},
        "2004": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "2006": {"comment":"$20-$5F?"},
        "2008": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "2010": {"comment":"$E0-$FF: stack constant n?"},
        "2012": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "2014": {"comment":"$D8-$DF: recall memory n?"},
        "2016": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "2018": {"comment":"HL = the top value"},
        "2022": {"comment":"$D0-$D7: store memory n?"},
        "2024": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "2026": {"comment":"$C8-$CF: store memory n and drop?"},
        "2028": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "2030": {"comment":"$60-$C7: stops with error code 51"},
        "2032": {"synopsis":"Codes $00-$1F: DE = the top value.","comment":"DE = the top value"},
        "2037": {"synopsis":"Codes $00-$5F: stacks the code's routine from CALC_OP_TABLE as the return address, HL = DE -\n5, and returns into it."},
        "2038": {"comment":"The code times 2"},
        "2040": {"comment":"The operation table"},
        "2044": {"comment":"BC = the routine"},
        "2047": {"comment":"Its address to return to"},
        "2048": {"comment":"HL = the value below the one DE points at"},
        "2052": {"comment":"Into the operation's routine"},
        "2053": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $24: carries out the operation whose code is the loop counter (BCREG's\nhigh byte, $5B87), by going back into the calculator's loop at its dispatch ($07C8).\nEntry: the loop counter = an operation code.\nExit: as that operation leaves the stack.","comment":"The loop counter is the operation code"},
        "2056": {"comment":"Dispatch it as if read from the stream"},
        "2058": {"synopsis":"Calculator operations $C8-$CF: copies the top value to memory n (n = code - $C8, at MEM +\n5n) and drops it. The CP $D5 hides the entry $080C (PUSH DE), where operations $D0-$D7 come:\nthey store the top in memory n and keep it.\nEntry: HL = the top value; DE = STKEND; A = n.\nExit: DE = the new STKEND (the top's address; at $080C, STKEND unchanged).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Keep the top's address: the new STKEND"},
        "2059": {"comment":"Hides $080C: PUSH DE (operations $D0-$D7)"},
        "2061": {"comment":"DE = the top"},
        "2062": {"comment":"HL = memory n; BC = 5"},
        "2065": {"comment":"Copy the top into memory n"},
        "2068": {"comment":"DE = the top's address (or STKEND at $080C)"},
        "2070": {"synopsis":"Calculator operations $D8-$DF: stacks a copy of memory n (n = code - $D8).\nEntry: DE = STKEND; A = n.\nExit: DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = memory n; BC = 5"},
        "2073": {"comment":"Copy it onto the stack"},
        "2076": {"synopsis":"Finds calculator memory n: MEM + 5n.\nEntry: A = n (0-7).\nExit: HL = the memory's address; BC = 5 (the length, ready for LDIR).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"MEM: the calculator's memories"},
        "2079": {"comment":"Times 5"},
        "2086": {"comment":"HL = MEM + 5n"},
        "2087": {"comment":"BC = 5"},
        "2090": {"synopsis":"Calculator operations $E0-$FF: stacks the 5 bytes at CALC_CONSTANTS + n (n = code - $E0).\nThe constants overlap: n is a byte offset, not an index.\nEntry: DE = STKEND; A = n; B = 0.\nExit: DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC = n"},
        "2091": {"comment":"CALC_CONSTANTS + n"},
        "2095": {"comment":"Copy 5 bytes onto the stack"},
        "2100": {"synopsis":"The calculator's constants, read by CALC_STK_CONST 5 bytes from offset n (operations $E0 +\nn). The ROM uses n = 0 (0.5), 1 (0, a small integer), 2 (16384), 6 (1.0), 9 (1, a small\ninteger), 12 (10) and 16 (pi/2, at $0844). The 21 bytes end at $0848; the byte after is the\ncode of CALC_END."},
        "2121": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $33: ends the calculation. Drops the loop's return address and returns\ninto CALC_ENTRY in ROM0, which returns past the operation bytes.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as CALC_ENTRY.","comment":"Drop the loop's return address"},
        "2122": {"comment":"Back into CALC_ENTRY"},
        "2123": {"synopsis":"Calculator operations $34-$38: end the calculation and return from the routine that used RST\n$28 as well: drops the loop's and CALC_ENTRY's return addresses, takes the LMPR and the\ncaller's IX that CALC_ENTRY pushed, and leaves through CALC_RESTORE (ROM0), whose RET then\nreturns to the caller's caller.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC restored from BCREG; LMPR put back; IX as before the RST $28.","comment":"Drop the loop's return address"},
        "2124": {"comment":"Drop CALC_ENTRY's return address"},
        "2125": {"comment":"A = the LMPR saved by CALC_ENTRY"},
        "2126": {"comment":"The caller's IX"},
        "2128": {"comment":"Restore BC and LMPR; return to the caller's caller"},
        "2131": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $25: stacks a copy of the top value.\nEntry: HL = the top; DE = STKEND.\nExit: DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Copy the top's 5 bytes to STKEND"},
        "2136": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $07 (the RET of CALC_DUP): drops the top value. For codes below $20, DE\nholds the top's address on entry, and the loop makes it the new STKEND.\nEntry: DE = the top's address.\nExit: DE = the new STKEND."},
        "2137": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $21: sets the loop counter (BCREG's high byte, $5B87) from the operand\nbyte.\nEntry: IX = the operand.\nExit: IX past it.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"The operand byte"},
        "2140": {"comment":"Z: always step past the operand"},
        "2143": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $22: decrements the loop counter and jumps by the offset byte unless it\nreached 0.\nEntry: IX = the offset (counted from its own address).\nExit: IX at the jump's target, or past the offset.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"The loop counter, less 1"},
        "2147": {"synopsis":"Stores the loop counter; at 0 (or for operation $21, always) steps past the operand,\notherwise jumps.","comment":"Store the loop counter"},
        "2150": {"comment":"Zero: no jump"},
        "2152": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $20: jumps by the signed offset byte, counted from the offset's own\naddress. Also the jump of the other jump operations.\nEntry: IX = the offset.\nExit: IX = the target.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"The offset byte"},
        "2156": {"comment":"BC = the offset, sign-extended"},
        "2159": {"comment":"IX = the target"},
        "2162": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $1F: drops the top value and jumps by the offset byte when it was 0;\notherwise steps past the offset.\nEntry: DE = the top's address; IX = the offset.\nExit: DE = the new STKEND; IX moved.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"Z: is the top 0?"},
        "2167": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $1E: drops the top value and jumps by the offset byte when it was a\ntrue result (1): it decrements the value's low byte and jumps when that gives 0. Meant for\nthe 0/1 results of the comparisons.\nEntry: DE = the top's address; IX = the offset.\nExit: DE = the new STKEND; IX moved.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"HL = the top's low byte"},
        "2171": {"comment":"1 becomes 0: true"},
        "2172": {"synopsis":"The common tail of the conditional jumps: Z jumps (CALC_JUMP's offset code), NZ steps past\nthe offset.","comment":"Jump?"},
        "2174": {"synopsis":"Steps IX past an operand byte.","comment":"Past the offset"},
        "2177": {"synopsis":"Calculator operations $28 and $27: copy bytes from the operation stream to the calculator\nstack. $28 takes a count byte first; $27 (the entry $0887, hidden in the LD HL,$0506: LD\nB,$05) copies exactly 5 bytes, one number. Several numbers in one $28 are stacked in order.\nEntry: IX = the operands; DE = STKEND.\nExit: IX past them; DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: AF, B, DE.","comment":"B = the count"},
        "2182": {"comment":"Hides $0887: LD B,$05 (operation $27)"},
        "2185": {"synopsis":"Copies the next byte from the operation stream to the stack.","comment":"Copy a byte from the stream"},
        "2192": {"comment":"Until all are copied"},
        "2195": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $29: stacks, as a small integer, the byte at the address given by the\noperand word.\nEntry: IX = the word; DE = STKEND.\nExit: IX past it; DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"C = the byte at the operand's address"},
        "2198": {"comment":"Stack it"},
        "2200": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $2A: stacks the word at the address given by the operand word (STK_BC).\nCALC_SVAR uses it on ROM1 $FE44.\nEntry: IX = the word.\nExit: IX past it; DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC = the word at the operand's address"},
        "2203": {"comment":"Stack it"},
        "2206": {"synopsis":"Reads the operand word from the operation stream and the word at that address.\nEntry: IX = the operand; DE = STKEND.\nExit: BC = the word read; HL = the address + 1; DE = STKEND; IX past the operand.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Keep DE"},
        "2207": {"comment":"DE = the operand word"},
        "2217": {"comment":"HL = the address; DE = STKEND"},
        "2218": {"comment":"BC = the word there"},
        "2222": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $23: stacks the loop counter as a small integer.\nEntry: DE = STKEND.\nExit: DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.","comment":"The loop counter"},
        "2226": {"comment":"Stack it"},
        "2228": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $26: stacks the operand byte as a small integer.\nEntry: IX = the byte; DE = STKEND.\nExit: IX past it; DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.","comment":"The operand byte"},
        "2233": {"comment":"Stack it"},
        "2235": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $2F: replaces the top value with 1 when it is 0 or more, 0 when it is\nnegative.\nEntry: HL = the top.\nExit: DE = STKEND.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.","comment":"Is it 0?"},
        "2238": {"comment":"HL = the top"},
        "2239": {"comment":"0: the result is 1"},
        "2241": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $2E: replaces the top value with 1 when it is above 0, else 0. (Zero is\ntested on bytes 0, 2 and 3, which covers a small integer 0.)\nEntry: HL = the top.\nExit: DE = STKEND.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.","comment":"The sign bit"},
        "2245": {"comment":"Negative: the result is 0"},
        "2247": {"comment":"Bytes 3, 2 and 0 all 0?"},
        "2256": {"comment":"Zero: the result is 0"},
        "2258": {"comment":"Above 0: the result is 1"},
        "2260": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $5C (NOT): replaces the top value with 1 when it is 0, else 0.\nEntry: HL = the top.\nExit: DE = STKEND.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.","comment":"Is it 0?"},
        "2263": {"comment":"HL = the top"},
        "2264": {"synopsis":"Puts 1 at HL when Z, else 0.","comment":"Z: 1"},
        "2266": {"comment":"Else 0"},
        "2268": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $2D: replaces the top value with 1 when it is 0 or less, else 0.\nEntry: HL = the top.\nExit: DE = STKEND.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.","comment":"Is it 0?"},
        "2271": {"comment":"HL = the top"},
        "2272": {"comment":"0: the result is 1"},
        "2274": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $2C: replaces the top value with 1 when it is negative (bit 7 of byte\n1, the sign in both forms), else 0.\nEntry: HL = the top.\nExit: DE = STKEND.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.","comment":"The sign bit"},
        "2278": {"synopsis":"Puts 1 at HL when carry, else 0.","comment":"No carry: 0"},
        "2280": {"synopsis":"Puts the small integer 1 at HL. The CP $0E after it hides the entry $08EB (LD C,$00), which\nputs 0 there; many routines jump to it. Both go on into CALC_STK_C_AT_DE with DE = HL.\nEntry: HL = the place.\nExit: DE = HL + 5 (the new STKEND).\nChanges: AF, C, DE.","comment":"C = 1"},
        "2282": {"comment":"Hides $08EB: LD C,$00 (a result of 0)"},
        "2285": {"comment":"Write at HL"},
        "2287": {"synopsis":"Writes C as a positive small integer (0, 0, C, 0) at DE and steps DE past the 5 bytes; the\nfifth byte is not written.\nEntry: DE = the place; C = the number.\nExit: DE += 5; A = 0.\nChanges: AF, DE.","comment":"Byte 0: 0 (a small integer)"},
        "2290": {"comment":"Byte 1: the sign, positive"},
        "2292": {"comment":"Byte 2: C"},
        "2294": {"comment":"Byte 3: 0"},
        "2298": {"comment":"DE past the 5 bytes"},
        "2300": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $0E (AND, numbers): x AND y gives 0 when y is 0, else x.\nEntry: HL = x; DE = y (the top).\nExit: DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.","comment":"y 0?"},
        "2303": {"comment":"Then 0"},
        "2305": {"comment":"Else x stays; y dropped"},
        "2306": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $0D (OR): x OR y gives 1 when y is not 0, else x.\nEntry: HL = x; DE = y (the top).\nExit: DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.","comment":"y 0?"},
        "2309": {"comment":"Not 0: the result is 1"},
        "2311": {"comment":"Else x stays; y dropped"},
        "2312": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $15 (AND with a string first): a$ AND y gives a$ when y is not 0, else\na$ with its length (bytes 3 and 4) set to 0, an empty string.\nEntry: HL = the string; DE = y (the top).\nExit: DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: AF, DE.","comment":"y 0?"},
        "2315": {"comment":"No: the string stays; y dropped"},
        "2316": {"comment":"The string's length bytes"},
        "2319": {"comment":"...both 0: an empty string"},
        "2320": {"comment":"DE = the new STKEND"},
        "2323": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $1A (= for strings): COMPARE_STRS (ROM0), then 1 when equal, else 0, in\nplace of the two strings.\nEntry: HL = the first string; the second on top.\nExit: DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"Compare the strings"},
        "2326": {"comment":"Equal: 1"},
        "2328": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $19 (< for strings): 1 when the first string sorts before the second\n(COMPARE_STRS gives carry), else 0.\nEntry: HL = the first string; the second on top.\nExit: DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"Compare the strings"},
        "2331": {"comment":"Carry: 1"},
        "2333": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $1B (> for strings): 1 when the first string sorts after the second,\nelse 0.\nEntry: HL = the first string; the second on top.\nExit: DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"Compare the strings"},
        "2336": {"comment":"Equal: 0"},
        "2338": {"comment":"No carry: 1"},
        "2340": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $17 (<= for strings): 1 when the strings are equal or the first sorts\nbefore the second, else 0.\nEntry: HL = the first string; the second on top.\nExit: DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"Compare the strings"},
        "2343": {"comment":"Equal: 1"},
        "2345": {"comment":"Else carry: 1"},
        "2347": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $18 (>= for strings): 1 unless the first string sorts before the\nsecond.\nEntry: HL = the first string; the second on top.\nExit: DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"Compare the strings"},
        "2350": {"synopsis":"Puts 1 at HL when no carry, else 0.","comment":"No carry: 1"},
        "2353": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $16 (<> for strings): 0 when the strings are equal, else 1.\nEntry: HL = the first string; the second on top.\nExit: DE = the new STKEND.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"Compare the strings"},
        "2356": {"comment":"Equal: 0"},
        "2358": {"comment":"Else 1"},
        "2360": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $13 (= for numbers): NOT (x - y), through the calculator.\nEntry: x and y on the calculator stack.\nExit: 1 or 0 in their place; returns from the calculator's caller as well ($34).","comment":"x - y, NOT"},
        "2364": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $12 (< for numbers): x - y below 0 (operation $2C).\nEntry: x and y on the calculator stack.\nExit: 1 or 0 in their place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"x - y, below 0?"},
        "2368": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $14 (> for numbers): x - y above 0 (operation $2E).\nEntry: x and y on the calculator stack.\nExit: 1 or 0 in their place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"x - y, above 0?"},
        "2372": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $10 (<= for numbers): x - y not above 0 (operation $2D).\nEntry: x and y on the calculator stack.\nExit: 1 or 0 in their place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"x - y, 0 or less?"},
        "2376": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $11 (>= for numbers): x - y not below 0 (operation $2F).\nEntry: x and y on the calculator stack.\nExit: 1 or 0 in their place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"x - y, 0 or more?"},
        "2380": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $0F (<> for numbers): NOT NOT (x - y).\nEntry: x and y on the calculator stack.\nExit: 1 or 0 in their place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"x - y, NOT, NOT"},
        "2385": {"synopsis":"Tests whether the value at DE is 0 (bytes 0, 2 and 3 all 0: the small integer 0).\nCALC_IS_ZERO_HL ($0952) tests the value at HL.\nEntry: DE = the value (at $0952: HL).\nExit: Z when it is 0; A = the bytes ORed; DE and HL as on entry (at $0952: exchanged).\nChanges: AF.","comment":"HL = the value"},
        "2386": {"synopsis":"Tests whether the value at HL is 0 (bytes 0, 2 and 3), then exchanges DE and HL.\nEntry: HL = the value.\nExit: Z when it is 0; DE = the value; HL = DE on entry.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"Byte 0 (the exponent)"},
        "2389": {"comment":"OR byte 2"},
        "2391": {"comment":"OR byte 3"},
        "2392": {"comment":"Back to byte 0"},
        "2395": {"comment":"Exchange back"},
        "2397": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $08 (MOD): x MOD y = x - y * INT (x / y). The quotient INT (x / y) is\nleft in calculator memory 3.\nEntry: x and y on the calculator stack.\nExit: the result in their place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"x MOD y = x - y * INT (x / y)"},
        "2409": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $09 (DIV): INT (x / y).\nEntry: x and y on the calculator stack.\nExit: the result in their place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"INT (x / y)"},
        "2413": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $0A (BOR): the bitwise OR of two numbers 0-65535.\nEntry: x and y on the calculator stack.\nExit: the result in their place.\nError: 30 when either is out of range (GET_UINT16).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC = x; HL = y"},
        "2416": {"comment":"Low bytes ORed"},
        "2418": {"comment":"High bytes ORed"},
        "2422": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $0C (BAND): the bitwise AND of two numbers 0-65535.\nEntry: x and y on the calculator stack.\nExit: the result in their place.\nError: 30 when either is out of range (GET_UINT16).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC = x; HL = y"},
        "2425": {"comment":"Low bytes ANDed"},
        "2427": {"comment":"High bytes ANDed"},
        "2429": {"synopsis":"Stacks BC with B = A (STK_BC): the tail of CALC_BOR and CALC_BAND.","comment":"BC = the result"},
        "2430": {"comment":"Stack it"},
        "2433": {"synopsis":"Takes two numbers 0-65535 off the calculator stack (GET_UINT16, ROM0).\nEntry: x and y on the calculator stack.\nExit: HL = y (the top); BC = x.\nError: 30 when either is out of range.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"y, 0-65535"},
        "2437": {"comment":"x, 0-65535"},
        "2440": {"comment":"HL = y"},
        "2442": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $39 (SIN):\n1. Reduces the angle to z in -1 to 1, with SIN x = SIN (z * pi/2) (CALC_REDUCE_ANG,\n   operation $2B).\n2. Puts z * z in memory 0 and evaluates z * (pi/2 + c1 z^2 + ... + c5 z^10) by Horner's\n   rule, the five coefficients stacked by one $28 and the loop counter at 5.\nEntry: x on the calculator stack.\nExit: SIN x in its place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"The reduced angle z; z * z to memory 0"},
        "2485": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $3A (COS): SIN (x + pi/2).\nEntry: x on the calculator stack.\nExit: COS x in its place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"SIN (x + pi/2)"},
        "2490": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $3B (TAN): SIN x / COS x.\nEntry: x on the calculator stack.\nExit: TAN x in its place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"SIN x / COS x"},
        "2497": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $2B: reduces an angle in radians for CALC_SIN.\n1. y = x / (2 pi) less its nearest whole number (INT (y + 0.5)), so y is -0.5 to 0.5; then w\n   = 4y, -2 to 2.\n2. |w| up to 1 gives z = w; otherwise z = 2 - w for w above 0, -w - 2 below (the tail at\n   $09DB).\nEntry: x on the calculator stack.\nExit: z in its place, -1 to 1, with SIN x = SIN (z * pi/2); returns from the calculator's\ncaller as well.","comment":"Times 1/(2 pi); less the nearest whole number"},
        "2523": {"synopsis":"Operation bytes of CALC_REDUCE_ANG reached by its $1E jump at $09D7 (|w| above 1): w - 2 or\n2 - w, then $34."},
        "2531": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $40 (EXP): multiplies x by 1/LN 2 (the 5-byte number at $09E6) and goes\non into CALC_POW2: EXP x = 2 ^ (x / LN 2).\nEntry: HL = x, the top.\nExit: as CALC_POW2.","comment":"Keep the value's address"},
        "2532": {"comment":"x / LN 2"},
        "2541": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "2542": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $32: 2 ^ x.\n1. n = INT x to memory 1, f = x - n (0 to 1) to memory 0.\n2. 2 ^ f by a polynomial in f: seven coefficients after 1.0, Horner's rule with the loop\n   counter at 7.\n3. Takes n off the stack (CALC_POP_BYTE) and adds it to the result's exponent byte.\nEntry: HL = x, the top.\nExit: 2 ^ x in its place; DE = STKEND (CALC_DE_STKEND).\nError: 28 when the exponent passes 255 (ERROR_28_STOP); a result too small for the exponent\nbecomes 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Keep the value's address"},
        "2543": {"comment":"n to memory 1; 2 ^ f by a polynomial; n on top"},
        "2596": {"comment":"A = n; Z: positive"},
        "2599": {"comment":"Positive: add it"},
        "2601": {"comment":"Negative and up to 255?"},
        "2603": {"comment":"Drop the value's address"},
        "2604": {"synopsis":"Makes the result 0 (an underflow) at FP_ZERO's routine $08EB.","comment":"The result is 0"},
        "2607": {"synopsis":"A negative n: BC = -magnitude, for the exponent.","comment":"BC = -magnitude"},
        "2611": {"synopsis":"Adds BC (n) to the result's exponent, checking the range.","comment":"HL = the value"},
        "2612": {"comment":"DE = its exponent"},
        "2615": {"comment":"Plus n"},
        "2618": {"comment":"Below 0: 0"},
        "2621": {"comment":"Above 255: error 28"},
        "2625": {"comment":"The new exponent"},
        "2627": {"comment":"0: the result is 0"},
        "2629": {"comment":"Store it"},
        "2630": {"comment":"DE = STKEND"},
        "2633": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $04 (^): x ^ y.\n1. When y is a whole number 0-63 (y minus its low byte ANDed with $3F is 0), multiplies 1 by\n   x y times (the operation bytes at $0A60, the loop counter = that byte, passed in B).\n2. Otherwise 0 when x is 0 (the bytes at $0A5D), else EXP (y * LN x).\nEntry: HL = x; DE = y, the top.\nExit: the result in their place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.\nError: as CALC_LN for a negative x.","comment":"y's byte 2"},
        "2636": {"comment":"B = it, 0-63: the loop counter"},
        "2639": {"comment":"y a whole number 0-63? x 0? EXP (y * LN x)"},
        "2653": {"synopsis":"Operation bytes of CALC_POWER reached by its $1F jumps: at $0A5D x is 0 (drop y, the result\nis 0); at $0A60 y is a whole number 0-63 (memory 0 = x, then 1 times x, the loop counter\ntimes)."},
        "2667": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $3F (LN):\n1. Makes x a floating-point number (operation $31) and stops when x is 0 or less (the 0/1\n   test left above STKEND is read back).\n2. Splits x into m * 2^k with m 0.5 to 1 (exponent set to $80); when m is 0.8 or less, m =\n   2m and k = k - 1.\n3. k * LN 2 plus (m - 1) times a 12-term Chebyshev series in 2.5 (m - 1) - 0.5\n   (CALC_CHEB_SUM).\nEntry: x on the calculator stack.\nExit: LN x in its place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.\nError: 27 when x is 0 or less (STR_BUF_ERR).","comment":"Floating point; 0 or less? (the test dropped)"},
        "2673": {"comment":"The dropped test's low byte, above STKEND"},
        "2676": {"comment":"1: x is 0 or less"},
        "2677": {"comment":"Error 27"},
        "2680": {"comment":"B = the exponent"},
        "2681": {"comment":"m = the mantissa, 0.5 to 1"},
        "2684": {"comment":"k = exponent - 128; series in 2.5 (m - 1) - 0.5"},
        "2792": {"comment":"Sum it"},
        "2794": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $3E (ATN):\n1. For |x| below 1, z = x and the base is 0; otherwise z = -1/x and the base is pi/2 with\n   the sign of x.\n2. The base plus z times a 12-term Chebyshev series in 2 z^2 - 1 (CALC_CHEB_SUM).\nEntry: x on the calculator stack.\nExit: ATN x in its place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"|x| below 1? Else z = -1/x, base pi/2"},
        "2885": {"synopsis":"Sums a 12-term Chebyshev series by the three-term recurrence b = c + 2t * b' - b''\n(Clenshaw's), shared by CALC_LN and CALC_ATN.\n1. Memory 0 = 2t (t was in memory 0); memory 1 = 0.\n2. For each of the 12 coefficients, from the top of the stack down, the recurrence, keeping\n   b' in memory 1 and b'' in memory 2.\n3. Multiplies b - b'' by the value below the coefficients and adds the value below that.\nEntry: the base, the multiplier and the 12 coefficients on the calculator stack; memory 0 =\nt.\nExit: the result in place of them; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"12 coefficients"},
        "2887": {"comment":"Clenshaw's recurrence with memories 0-2"},
        "2911": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $3C (ASN): 2 * ATN (x / (1 + SQR (1 - x * x))).\nEntry: x on the calculator stack.\nExit: ASN x in its place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"2 * ATN (x / (1 + SQR (1 - x * x)))"},
        "2926": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $3D (ACS): pi/2 - ASN x.\nEntry: x on the calculator stack.\nExit: ACS x in its place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"pi/2 - ASN x"},
        "2932": {"synopsis":"Multiplies two 16-bit unsigned numbers by shifts and adds. The multiplier is HL when its\nhigh byte is 0 (8 bits only), else DE (16 bits, exchanged into HL); its bits are taken from\nthe top, adding the other number for each set bit.\nEntry: HL, DE = the numbers.\nExit: HL = the product; carry when it passes 65535 (HL is then incomplete).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.\nKeeps: BC.","comment":"Keep BC"},
        "2933": {"comment":"8 bits"},
        "2935": {"comment":"HL's high byte 0?"},
        "2939": {"comment":"No: the multiplier is DE"},
        "2940": {"comment":"Its high byte"},
        "2942": {"synopsis":"C = the multiplier's low byte; a zero high byte skips the first 8 bits.","comment":"C = its low byte"},
        "2943": {"comment":"The product"},
        "2946": {"comment":"High byte 0: only the low byte"},
        "2948": {"synopsis":"Shifts the product and adds DE for each set bit of the multiplier's high byte.","comment":"Product * 2"},
        "2949": {"comment":"Overflow?"},
        "2951": {"comment":"The next bit"},
        "2954": {"comment":"Set: add the multiplicand"},
        "2955": {"comment":"Overflow?"},
        "2957": {"synopsis":"The next bit of the high byte."},
        "2959": {"comment":"8 more bits"},
        "2961": {"synopsis":"The multiplier's low byte, bit by bit.","comment":"The low byte"},
        "2962": {"synopsis":"Shifts the product and adds DE for each set bit of the low byte.","comment":"Product * 2"},
        "2963": {"comment":"Overflow?"},
        "2965": {"comment":"The next bit"},
        "2968": {"comment":"Set: add the multiplicand"},
        "2969": {"comment":"Overflow?"},
        "2971": {"synopsis":"The next bit of the low byte."},
        "2973": {"synopsis":"Puts BC back and returns, carry for an overflow.","comment":"BC back"},
        "2975": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $00 (*): x * y.\n1. Two small integers: multiplies their magnitudes (MUL16_HL_DE) and writes a small integer\n   with the combined sign, unless the product passes 65535.\n2. Otherwise floating point (MUL_FLOAT).\nEntry: HL = x; DE = y, the top.\nExit: the product in place of x; DE = the new STKEND.\nError: 28 when the result is too big.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; the alternates.","comment":"Either a floating-point number?"},
        "2977": {"comment":"Then floating point"},
        "2979": {"comment":"Keep y's and x's addresses"},
        "2981": {"comment":"DE = |x|; C = x's sign"},
        "2984": {"comment":"Keep |x|"},
        "2985": {"comment":"B = x's sign"},
        "2986": {"comment":"HL = y"},
        "2988": {"comment":"DE = |y|; C = y's sign"},
        "2991": {"comment":"HL = |x|"},
        "2992": {"comment":"C = the product's sign"},
        "2995": {"comment":"HL = |x| * |y|; carry: too big"},
        "2998": {"comment":"DE = x's address"},
        "2999": {"comment":"HL = x's address; DE = the product"},
        "3000": {"comment":"Too big: floating point"},
        "3002": {"comment":"Write it as a small integer"},
        "3004": {"synopsis":"Writes DE as a small integer at HL, negative when A is 1 (A = 0: positive). ROM1's arc\ndrawing ($EA4A, $EA53) calls it.\nEntry: HL = the place; DE = the magnitude; A = 0 or 1.\nExit: HL = the place + 3; DE kept.\nChanges: AF, C, HL.","comment":"A = 0: C = 0; A = 1: C = $FF"},
        "3010": {"comment":"Keep DE"},
        "3011": {"synopsis":"Writes DE as a small integer at HL with sign byte C ($FF negative); a zero DE is always\npositive.\nEntry: HL = the place; DE = the magnitude; C = the sign; the value to give back in DE\npushed.\nExit: HL = the place + 3; DE popped.\nChanges: AF, C, HL.","comment":"Zero?"},
        "3015": {"comment":"Then positive"},
        "3016": {"synopsis":"Writes 0 and the sign C, then the value, negated when C is $FF.","comment":"Byte 0: 0"},
        "3019": {"comment":"Byte 1: the sign"},
        "3021": {"comment":"Positive?"},
        "3024": {"comment":"Negative: DE = -DE"},
        "3031": {"synopsis":"Writes the low and high bytes.","comment":"The low and high bytes"},
        "3034": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "3036": {"synopsis":"Reads the small integer at HL as a sign and a magnitude.\nEntry: HL = the value.\nExit: C = the sign byte; DE = the magnitude; HL = the value + 3; Z when it is positive (or a\nnegative 0).\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.","comment":"C = the sign byte"},
        "3039": {"comment":"DE = the value"},
        "3042": {"comment":"Positive?"},
        "3044": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "3045": {"synopsis":"Negates DE (two's complement: 1 less, then complemented). FP_CPL_DE ($0BE6) only complements\nit.\nEntry: DE.\nExit: DE = -DE; Z when the result is 0.\nChanges: AF, DE.","comment":"DE - 1, then"},
        "3046": {"synopsis":"Complements DE (each bit inverted).\nEntry: DE.\nExit: DE = NOT DE; Z when the result is 0.\nChanges: AF, DE.","comment":"...each bit inverted"},
        "3052": {"comment":"Z: the result is 0"},
        "3054": {"synopsis":"Negates the 32-bit number DE' (high) : DE (low): the low word is negated; the high word is\nnegated when the low result is 0, else complemented.\nEntry: DE, DE'.\nExit: DE, DE' negated; the register sets exchanged (EXX), so the high word is in DE.\nChanges: AF, DE, DE'.","comment":"Negate the low word"},
        "3057": {"comment":"The high word"},
        "3058": {"comment":"Low not 0: complement only"},
        "3060": {"comment":"Low 0: negate"},
        "3062": {"synopsis":"The integer product passed 65535: drops the saved address and multiplies in floating point.","comment":"Drop y's address"},
        "3063": {"synopsis":"The floating-point multiplication.\n1. Both operands made floating point (FP_FLOAT_BOTH); 0 when either is 0.\n2. When either mantissa is 0.5 (a power of two), adds the exponents (FP_SCALE_EXP).\n3. Otherwise multiplies the mantissas (MUL_LONG).\nEntry: HL = x; DE = y.\nExit: the product at x; DE = the new STKEND.\nError: 28 when it is too big.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; the alternates.","comment":"Both floating point; x 0?"},
        "3066": {"comment":"x 0: the result is x"},
        "3067": {"comment":"y's flags"},
        "3068": {"comment":"y 0: the result is 0"},
        "3070": {"comment":"Keep x's address"},
        "3071": {"comment":"x's flags"},
        "3072": {"comment":"x a power of two?"},
        "3074": {"comment":"y's flags"},
        "3075": {"comment":"y not a power of two: the long way"},
        "3077": {"synopsis":"One operand is a power of two: exponent = x's + y's - 129.","comment":"y's exponent"},
        "3081": {"comment":"Plus x's"},
        "3084": {"comment":"Less 129"},
        "3087": {"synopsis":"Finishes a multiplication or division by a power of two: HL = the new exponent before the BC\nbias. Checks it (0 or below: the result is 0; above 255: error 28), writes it and XORs y's\nmantissa bytes into x's, which gives the other operand's mantissa with the combined sign.\nEntry: HL, BC = the exponent and its bias; DE = y; the address of x pushed.\nExit: DE = x + 5 (the new STKEND).\nError: 28 when the exponent passes 255.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "3088": {"comment":"Below 0: the result is 0"},
        "3091": {"comment":"Above 255: error 28"},
        "3095": {"comment":"The new exponent"},
        "3097": {"comment":"0: the result is 0"},
        "3099": {"comment":"HL = x"},
        "3100": {"comment":"Store the exponent"},
        "3101": {"comment":"Four mantissa bytes"},
        "3103": {"synopsis":"XORs the next mantissa byte of y into x."},
        "3105": {"comment":"XOR y's byte into x's"},
        "3110": {"comment":"DE = x + 5"},
        "3113": {"synopsis":"Takes the result's address off the stack and makes the result 0.","comment":"Drop x's address"},
        "3114": {"synopsis":"Makes the result at HL 0 (the routine at $08EB).","comment":"Write 0 at HL"},
        "3117": {"synopsis":"Multiplies the two 32-bit mantissas (FP_UNPACK_2), y's bytes from the lowest, by shifts and\nadds into HL' (high) : HL (low), a zero byte shifting 8 bits at once; then the exponent ex +\ney - 128 and FP_NORMALISE.\nEntry: HL = x; DE = y; the address of x pushed.\nExit: as FP_PACK.","comment":"Unpack x and y"},
        "3120": {"comment":"Keep the exponents"},
        "3121": {"comment":"The product HL' : HL = 0"},
        "3129": {"comment":"Four bytes of y"},
        "3131": {"synopsis":"The next byte of y's mantissa: 8 bits, or a byte shift when it is 0.","comment":"8 bits"},
        "3133": {"comment":"This byte 0?"},
        "3136": {"comment":"Then shift the product 8 bits at once"},
        "3147": {"synopsis":"Adds x's mantissa when the bit is set.","comment":"The next bit"},
        "3150": {"comment":"Set: add x's mantissa"},
        "3155": {"synopsis":"Shifts the 32-bit product right one bit.","comment":"Shift the product right"},
        "3165": {"comment":"Each bit"},
        "3167": {"comment":"The last bit out goes into B"},
        "3169": {"synopsis":"Takes y's next mantissa byte from the alternates.","comment":"y's next byte to A"},
        "3171": {"comment":"...the bytes move along"},
        "3176": {"comment":"Each byte"},
        "3179": {"comment":"A = the bits below the mantissa"},
        "3181": {"comment":"The mantissa's low word to DE"},
        "3182": {"comment":"H, L = the exponents"},
        "3185": {"comment":"Exponent = ex + ey"},
        "3186": {"comment":"...less 128"},
        "3189": {"synopsis":"Ends a multiplication or division: HL = the exponent less the bias in BC; the mantissa HL' :\nDE with the extra bits in A. Shifts the mantissa left once when its top bit is clear, rounds\non the next bit and packs (FP_PACK_POP).\nEntry: HL, BC = the exponent and its bias; HL' : DE = the mantissa; A = the bits below it;\nthe sign (A bit 7) and x's address pushed.\nExit: as FP_PACK.","comment":"Less the bias"},
        "3191": {"comment":"Top bit set?"},
        "3195": {"comment":"No: exponent - 1"},
        "3197": {"comment":"...and the mantissa shifted left"},
        "3205": {"synopsis":"Rounds the mantissa up when the next bit is set."},
        "3206": {"comment":"The next bit: round up?"},
        "3207": {"synopsis":"Rounds the mantissa HL' : DE on carry, carrying into the exponent when it overflows.\nCALC_ADD jumps here."},
        "3209": {"comment":"Add 1 to the mantissa"},
        "3225": {"comment":"All overflowed: exponent + 1"},
        "3227": {"comment":"...and the mantissa's high byte $80"},
        "3230": {"synopsis":"Takes the sign byte off the stack and packs the result.","comment":"A = the sign"},
        "3231": {"synopsis":"Packs a floating-point result at x: exponent L (H must be 0; below 1 gives 0, above 255\nerror 28), the sign from A bit 7 into the mantissa's top bit, then the mantissa HL' : DE.\nEntry: HL = the exponent; A bit 7 = the sign; HL' : DE = the mantissa; the address of x\npushed.\nExit: DE = x + 5 (the new STKEND).\nError: 28 when the exponent passes 255.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Exponent below 0?"},
        "3232": {"comment":"Then the result is 0"},
        "3235": {"comment":"Above 255: error 28"},
        "3239": {"comment":"Exponent 0?"},
        "3241": {"comment":"Then the result is 0"},
        "3244": {"comment":"BC = the mantissa's high word"},
        "3248": {"comment":"The sign into bit 7"},
        "3252": {"comment":"B = the exponent"},
        "3253": {"comment":"HL = x's address"},
        "3254": {"comment":"The exponent"},
        "3256": {"comment":"The sign and the mantissa"},
        "3263": {"comment":"DE = x + 5"},
        "3266": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $05 (/): x / y.\n1. Both made floating point; x = 0 gives 0; y = 0 is error 28.\n2. A power-of-two y: exponent = x's - y's + 129 (FP_SCALE_EXP).\n3. Otherwise long division (DIV_LONG).\nEntry: HL = x; DE = y, the top.\nExit: the quotient in place of x; DE = the new STKEND.\nError: 28 for a division by 0 or a result too big.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; the alternates.","comment":"Both floating point; x 0?"},
        "3269": {"comment":"x 0: the result is 0"},
        "3270": {"comment":"Keep x's address"},
        "3271": {"comment":"y's flags"},
        "3272": {"comment":"y 0: error 28"},
        "3275": {"comment":"y not a power of two: long division"},
        "3277": {"comment":"y's exponent"},
        "3281": {"comment":"x's exponent, less y's"},
        "3285": {"comment":"Plus 129"},
        "3291": {"synopsis":"Divides the mantissas: the dividend in HL' : HL, the divisor negated in DE' : DE, by trial\nadditions, 34 quotient bits (four bytes, then two for rounding), then the exponent ex - ey +\n$81 and FP_NORMALISE.\nEntry: HL = x; DE = y; the address of x pushed.\nExit: as FP_PACK.","comment":"Unpack x and y"},
        "3294": {"comment":"HL' : HL = x's mantissa; DE' : DE = y's"},
        "3298": {"comment":"The divisor negated"},
        "3302": {"comment":"Keep the exponents"},
        "3303": {"comment":"8 bits; C counts 4 bytes up to 0"},
        "3306": {"comment":"Try the first subtraction"},
        "3308": {"synopsis":"Keeps the quotient byte just made in the alternates and starts the next 8 bits.","comment":"8 more bits"},
        "3311": {"comment":"The quotient bytes move along"},
        "3317": {"synopsis":"Shifts the remainder left; a bit shifted out means the divisor surely goes in.","comment":"The remainder left one bit"},
        "3322": {"comment":"No bit out: try the subtraction"},
        "3324": {"comment":"A bit out: subtract surely"},
        "3328": {"comment":"A quotient bit of 1"},
        "3331": {"synopsis":"Subtracts the divisor (adds its negative); a borrow puts it back.","comment":"Remainder - divisor"},
        "3335": {"comment":"Fits: a quotient bit of 1"},
        "3337": {"comment":"Does not fit: add the divisor back"},
        "3343": {"synopsis":"Moves the quotient bit (carry) into A.","comment":"The quotient bit into A"},
        "3345": {"comment":"Each bit"},
        "3347": {"comment":"Another byte?"},
        "3351": {"comment":"Keep the byte"},
        "3352": {"comment":"Then 2 more bits, for the rounding"},
        "3356": {"comment":"Gather the quotient into H'L' and D"},
        "3365": {"comment":"The 2 extra bits"},
        "3366": {"comment":"...to the top of A"},
        "3368": {"comment":"The last quotient byte"},
        "3369": {"comment":"...to E"},
        "3370": {"comment":"B, C = the exponents"},
        "3371": {"comment":"x's exponent"},
        "3376": {"comment":"...less y's"},
        "3378": {"comment":"Plus $81"},
        "3383": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $03 (-): negates y (the routine at ROM1 $D18F, operation $5D) and adds\n(CALC_ADD).\nEntry: HL = x; DE = y, the top.\nExit: as CALC_ADD.","comment":"HL = y"},
        "3384": {"comment":"Keep x's address"},
        "3385": {"comment":"y = -y (operation $5D)"},
        "3388": {"comment":"HL = x; DE = y"},
        "3390": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $01 (+): x + y.\n1. Two small integers: adds them as 17-bit signed numbers; a sum out of range goes to\n   floating point, -65536 is written as $91 $80 0 0 0.\n2. Floating point: both made floating point and unpacked; the smaller is shifted right to\n   line up (SHIFT_R_DE32); same signs add (with a shift right on a carry, rounded by\n   FP_ROUND_A); different signs subtract (ADD_SUB_MANT).\nEntry: HL = x; DE = y, the top.\nExit: the sum in place of x; DE = the new STKEND.\nError: 28 when it is too big.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; the alternates.","comment":"Either a floating-point number?"},
        "3392": {"comment":"Then floating point"},
        "3394": {"comment":"Keep y's address"},
        "3396": {"comment":"Keep x's sign's address"},
        "3398": {"comment":"BC = x"},
        "3404": {"comment":"A = y's sign"},
        "3406": {"comment":"DE = y"},
        "3409": {"comment":"Add the 16 bits"},
        "3414": {"comment":"HL = x's sign"},
        "3415": {"comment":"The signs plus the carry"},
        "3416": {"comment":"Out of range?"},
        "3418": {"comment":"Then floating point"},
        "3420": {"comment":"The new sign: $00 or $FF"},
        "3422": {"comment":"The sum 0?"},
        "3426": {"comment":"With a negative sign?"},
        "3430": {"comment":"-65536: exponent $91"},
        "3434": {"comment":"...negative, mantissa 0.5"},
        "3436": {"synopsis":"Writes the sum's low and high bytes and a zero fifth byte.","comment":"The low byte"},
        "3438": {"comment":"The high byte"},
        "3440": {"comment":"Byte 4: 0"},
        "3442": {"comment":"DE = y's address, the new STKEND"},
        "3444": {"synopsis":"The integer sum is out of range: back to x and add in floating point.","comment":"Drop y's address"},
        "3445": {"comment":"HL = x"},
        "3446": {"synopsis":"The floating-point addition: unpacks both and lines up the exponents.","comment":"Keep x's address"},
        "3447": {"comment":"Both floating point"},
        "3450": {"comment":"Unpack them"},
        "3453": {"comment":"y's exponent less x's"},
        "3455": {"comment":"y's not below x's?"},
        "3457": {"comment":"C = x's exponent"},
        "3458": {"comment":"A = the difference"},
        "3460": {"comment":"Exchange the mantissas"},
        "3464": {"comment":"Shift y's right"},
        "3469": {"synopsis":"y's exponent is not below x's: shifts x's mantissa right by the difference, then exchanges\nthe two.","comment":"Shift x's right (when they differ)"},
        "3472": {"comment":"Exchange the mantissas"},
        "3476": {"comment":"BC = the exponent"},
        "3478": {"synopsis":"Same signs add the mantissas; different signs subtract (FP_ADD_SUB_M).","comment":"A = the sign of x XOR y"},
        "3479": {"comment":"Different signs?"},
        "3481": {"comment":"Then subtract"},
        "3482": {"comment":"Add the mantissas"},
        "3487": {"comment":"DE = the low word"},
        "3488": {"comment":"HL = x's address"},
        "3490": {"comment":"x's sign byte"},
        "3491": {"comment":"No carry out?"},
        "3493": {"comment":"Carry: exponent + 1"},
        "3494": {"comment":"...and shift the sum right"},
        "3504": {"synopsis":"The sign from x; rounds and packs (FP_ROUND_A).","comment":"x's sign"},
        "3506": {"comment":"HL = the exponent"},
        "3508": {"comment":"Round and pack"},
        "3511": {"synopsis":"Different signs: subtracts the mantissas; an exact 0 gives the result 0.","comment":"Subtract the mantissas"},
        "3517": {"comment":"High word not 0?"},
        "3519": {"comment":"Keep the borrow"},
        "3521": {"comment":"Low word 0 too?"},
        "3524": {"comment":"Then the result is 0"},
        "3528": {"synopsis":"The sign is x's, flipped (and the difference negated) when the subtraction borrowed.","comment":"DE = x's address"},
        "3530": {"comment":"x's sign byte"},
        "3532": {"comment":"No borrow: x's sign"},
        "3534": {"comment":"A borrow: the other sign"},
        "3537": {"comment":"...and the difference negated"},
        "3550": {"synopsis":"Shifts the mantissa left one bit and lowers the exponent.","comment":"Exponent - 1"},
        "3552": {"comment":"Mantissa left one bit"},
        "3556": {"synopsis":"Until the mantissa's top bit is set, then packs (FP_PACK).","comment":"Top bit set?"},
        "3558": {"comment":"No: again"},
        "3561": {"comment":"The mantissa's low word to DE"},
        "3562": {"comment":"HL = the exponent"},
        "3564": {"comment":"Pack it"},
        "3567": {"synopsis":"Shifts the 32-bit mantissa DE' (high) : DE (low) right A bits (at most 33), then rounds up\non the last bit shifted out.\nEntry: A = the count (not 0).\nExit: DE', DE shifted.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, DE'.","comment":"B = the count"},
        "3568": {"comment":"...at most 33"},
        "3574": {"synopsis":"Shifts the 32 bits right one place.","comment":"Shift the high word right"},
        "3580": {"comment":"Shift the low word right"},
        "3584": {"comment":"Each bit"},
        "3586": {"comment":"Last bit out 0: done"},
        "3587": {"comment":"Else round up"},
        "3595": {"synopsis":"Unpacks two floating-point numbers, x at HL and y right after it, for the long arithmetic.\nPushes, under the return address, AF with A bit 7 = the sign of the result of a\nmultiplication or division (x's sign XOR y's).\nEntry: HL = x; DE = y, right after it.\nExit: B = x's exponent; C = y's exponent; DE' : DE = x's mantissa, HL' : HL = y's, each with\nits top bit set; BC' = y's bytes 2 and 3; A = y's byte 4.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, the alternates; AF'.","comment":"y's sign byte"},
        "3597": {"comment":"B = x's exponent"},
        "3599": {"comment":"Bit 7: the signs XORed"},
        "3600": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "3601": {"comment":"Push the sign under it"},
        "3603": {"comment":"x's mantissa, the top bit set"},
        "3609": {"comment":"Keep its high word"},
        "3610": {"comment":"DE = its low word"},
        "3614": {"comment":"C = y's exponent"},
        "3617": {"comment":"y's byte 1, the top bit set"},
        "3622": {"comment":"y's byte 2"},
        "3624": {"comment":"HL' = y's high word; B' = byte 2"},
        "3631": {"comment":"y's byte 3"},
        "3634": {"comment":"C' = it"},
        "3635": {"comment":"DE' = x's high word"},
        "3637": {"comment":"HL = y's low word"},
        "3641": {"synopsis":"Makes both operands floating point (FP_FLOAT_DE on y, then on x), keeping y's flags in AF'.\nEntry: HL = x; DE = y.\nExit: HL = x; DE = y; flags for x, AF' for y: carry when it is 0; else Z when its mantissa\nis exactly 0.5 (a power of two).\nChanges: AF, AF', BC, DE, HL.","comment":"y first"},
        "3644": {"comment":"Keep y's flags"},
        "3645": {"synopsis":"Exchanges DE and HL and makes the number at HL floating point (CALC_TO_FLOAT).\nEntry: DE = the number.\nExit: as CALC_TO_FLOAT, with DE and HL exchanged.","comment":"HL = the number"},
        "3646": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $31: makes the number at HL floating point (a small integer is\nconverted by INT_TO_FLOAT).\nEntry: HL = the number.\nExit: HL = it; carry when it is 0 (left a small integer); else Z when its mantissa is\nexactly 0.5 (a power of two).\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"The exponent byte"},
        "3648": {"comment":"0: a small integer"},
        "3650": {"comment":"The mantissa's top byte"},
        "3653": {"comment":"...without the sign: not 0?"},
        "3656": {"comment":"Bytes 2-4 ORed: Z for a mantissa of 0.5"},
        "3666": {"synopsis":"Converts the small integer at HL to floating point: exponent $90 for a high byte, $88 for a\nlow byte only, lowered while shifting the magnitude left until its top bit goes out; the\nsign goes into the mantissa's top bit.\nEntry: HL = the number.\nExit: HL = it; carry when it is 0 (left as it is); else Z when the mantissa is 0.5.\nChanges: AF, BC.\nKeeps: DE.","comment":"Keep DE"},
        "3667": {"comment":"C = the sign; DE = the magnitude"},
        "3670": {"comment":"Bytes 3 and 4: 0"},
        "3676": {"comment":"Back to byte 1"},
        "3677": {"comment":"The high byte"},
        "3678": {"comment":"Exponent $90 for 16 bits"},
        "3681": {"comment":"High byte not 0?"},
        "3683": {"comment":"Low byte 0 too?"},
        "3684": {"comment":"Then the number is 0"},
        "3686": {"comment":"Only 8 bits: exponent $88"},
        "3690": {"synopsis":"Lowers the exponent for each shift.","comment":"Exponent - 1"},
        "3691": {"synopsis":"Shifts the magnitude left until a 1 goes out.","comment":"Shift the magnitude left"},
        "3694": {"comment":"Until a 1 goes out"},
        "3696": {"comment":"Carry = the sign bit"},
        "3698": {"comment":"The sign into the top"},
        "3701": {"comment":"Byte 1: the sign and the mantissa"},
        "3703": {"comment":"Byte 2"},
        "3706": {"comment":"Byte 0: the exponent"},
        "3707": {"comment":"Z for a mantissa of 0.5"},
        "3712": {"synopsis":"The number is 0: stays a small integer, carry set.","comment":"HL = byte 0"},
        "3714": {"comment":"Carry: 0"},
        "3716": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $54 (VAL); the LD A,$AF hides operation $53 (VAL$) at $0E85 (XOR A).\n1. Copies the string to the workspace with a CR after it (TEXT_TO_WKSP) and points\n   CHADP/CHAD at it.\n2. Calls RAMRUN_C533_X (ROM0) on it, then checks the syntax of one expression (EXPR_ANY),\n   which must end at the CR and be a number for VAL, a string for VAL$.\n3. Evaluates it (EVAL_EXPR) and puts CHAD, CHADP and HMPR back.\nEntry: the string on the calculator stack.\nExit: the value in its place; DE = STKEND (CALC_DE_STKEND).\nError: 29 for a bad expression or the wrong type.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX.","comment":"Hides $0E85: XOR A (operation $53, VAL$)"},
        "3718": {"comment":"Keep IX"},
        "3720": {"comment":"B = CHADP"},
        "3725": {"comment":"CHAD"},
        "3729": {"comment":"Z: VAL$"},
        "3731": {"comment":"The string"},
        "3734": {"comment":"One more for the CR"},
        "3735": {"comment":"Copy it to the workspace, CR at the end"},
        "3738": {"comment":"CHAD = the copy"},
        "3742": {"comment":"HMPR: its page"},
        "3744": {"comment":"CHADP"},
        "3747": {"comment":"Keep the copy's address"},
        "3748": {"comment":"RAMRUN_C533_X on it"},
        "3753": {"comment":"CHAD = the copy"},
        "3758": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7 off: check the syntax only"},
        "3763": {"comment":"An expression: Z for a string"},
        "3766": {"comment":"Keep its type"},
        "3767": {"comment":"At the CR?"},
        "3770": {"comment":"No: error 29"},
        "3772": {"comment":"HL = the copy"},
        "3773": {"comment":"Z: VAL$"},
        "3774": {"comment":"VAL?"},
        "3776": {"comment":"VAL$: a string?"},
        "3779": {"synopsis":"VAL: a string expression is an error.","comment":"The expression's type"},
        "3780": {"comment":"VAL with a string: error 29"},
        "3782": {"synopsis":"Evaluates the copy (FLAGS bit 7 set: running), then puts CHAD, CHADP and HMPR back.","comment":"CHAD = the copy"},
        "3785": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7 on: running"},
        "3790": {"comment":"Evaluate it"},
        "3793": {"comment":"CHAD back"},
        "3797": {"comment":"CHADP back"},
        "3801": {"comment":"HMPR back to CHADP's page"},
        "3804": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "3806": {"synopsis":"Loads DE from STKEND and returns: the calculator's loop expects DE = STKEND after an\noperation that changed the stack by ROM0's routines.\nEntry: none.\nExit: DE = STKEND.","comment":"DE = STKEND"},
        "3811": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 29.","comment":"Stops with error code 29"},
        "3813": {"synopsis":"Calculator operations $49 (DVAR), $4C (EOF) and $4D (PTR): handed to the DOS through RST $08\nhooks 139 (HVAR), 140 and 141. The entries $0EE8 and $0EEB are hidden in the two LD HL\ninstructions (RST $08 $8C and $8D); when the hook returns, the rest of those instructions is\nharmless and all go on at CALC_DE_STKEND.\nEntry: the argument on the calculator stack.\nExit: as the DOS leaves the stack; DE = STKEND.","comment":"DVAR: the DOS's hook 139"},
        "3815": {"comment":"Hides $0EE8: RST $08 $8C (EOF)"},
        "3818": {"comment":"Hides $0EEB: RST $08 $8D (PTR)"},
        "3821": {"comment":"DE = STKEND"},
        "3823": {"synopsis":"PATH$, function code $35 (EVAL_FN_ROUTINES in ROM0): steps past the token, returns at once\nwhen checking syntax ($3B14 in ROM0), else hands the work to the DOS (RST $08 hook 142,\nHPATH).\nEntry: CHAD at the token.\nExit: the DOS's result on the calculator stack; DE = STKEND.","comment":"Past the token; returns when checking syntax"},
        "3826": {"comment":"PATH$: the DOS's hook 142"},
        "3828": {"synopsis":"Ends a DOS function with DE = STKEND.","comment":"DE = STKEND"},
        "3830": {"synopsis":"RND, function code $22 (EVAL_FN_ROUTINES in ROM0). When running, SEED becomes (SEED + 1) *\n254 MOD 65537 - 1 (by simulating the code for all 65536 seeds) and the result is SEED /\n65536 (its exponent lowered by 16). A following '(' takes RND (n): operation $30 (ROM1\n$D1D6) of the result times (n + 1).\nEntry: CHAD at the token.\nExit: the number on the calculator stack (when running).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Past the token"},
        "3831": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "3834": {"comment":"No: only the syntax"},
        "3838": {"comment":"SEED"},
        "3841": {"comment":"SEED' = (SEED + 1) * 254 MOD 65537 - 1"},
        "3854": {"comment":"No borrow?"},
        "3857": {"synopsis":"Stores the new SEED and stacks RND as SEED / 65536.","comment":"The new SEED"},
        "3860": {"comment":"Stack it"},
        "3863": {"comment":"Floating point"},
        "3866": {"comment":"Exponent - 16: / 65536"},
        "3869": {"comment":"Too small: leave it"},
        "3872": {"synopsis":"An argument in brackets?","comment":"The current character"},
        "3873": {"comment":"A '('?"},
        "3876": {"comment":"The argument n and ')'; running?"},
        "3880": {"comment":"RND * (n + 1), operation $30"},
        "3886": {"synopsis":"ATTR, function code $27 (EVAL_FN_ROUTINES in ROM0): ATTR (row, column) with row 0-23 and\ncolumn 0-31 (GET_ROW_COL). Reads the attribute byte from the current screen: in MODE 1 at\n$9800 + row * 32 + column, in MODE 2 $2000 above the cell's first pixel byte; MODE 3 and 4\nhave none (MODE34_ERROR, error 34).\nEntry: CHAD at the token.\nExit: the byte on the calculator stack (when running).\nError: 32 when out of range; 34 in MODE 3 or 4; 29 for bad syntax.","comment":"(row, column); running?"},
        "3890": {"comment":"24 rows, 32 columns"},
        "3893": {"comment":"D = row; E = column"},
        "3896": {"comment":"MODE"},
        "3899": {"comment":"MODE 3 or 4?"},
        "3901": {"comment":"Then error 34"},
        "3904": {"comment":"MODE 1?"},
        "3907": {"comment":"MODE 2: the cell's first byte"},
        "3910": {"comment":"Its attribute: $2000 above"},
        "3915": {"synopsis":"MODE 1: the attribute area at $9800.","comment":"MODE 1: the cell's address"},
        "3918": {"comment":"D = $98 + row / 8"},
        "3926": {"synopsis":"Reads the byte from the screen and stacks it.","comment":"HL = the attribute's address"},
        "3928": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "3931": {"comment":"Stack it"},
        "3933": {"synopsis":"POINT, function code $23 (EVAL_FN_ROUTINES in ROM0): POINT (x, y), the pixel's value at x, y\non the current screen (GET_PLOT_COORDS, PIXEL_ADDR): 0 or 1 in MODE 1 and 2, 0-3 in MODE 3,\n0-15 in MODE 4 (the high nibble for an even x).\nEntry: CHAD at the token.\nExit: the value on the calculator stack (when running).\nError: 30 when the point is off the screen; 29 for bad syntax.","comment":"(x, y); running?"},
        "3937": {"comment":"B = the row; C (or HL) = x"},
        "3940": {"comment":"HL = the byte; A = the pixel in it"},
        "3943": {"comment":"B = the pixel + 1"},
        "3945": {"comment":"Read the byte"},
        "3948": {"comment":"E = the byte"},
        "3949": {"comment":"One bit a pixel"},
        "3951": {"comment":"MODE"},
        "3954": {"comment":"MODE 1 or 2?"},
        "3958": {"comment":"Four bits a pixel"},
        "3960": {"comment":"MODE 4?"},
        "3962": {"comment":"MODE 3: two bits a pixel"},
        "3964": {"comment":"Rearrange the byte's bits"},
        "3973": {"comment":"THFATT: fat pixels?"},
        "3977": {"comment":"Then two pixels in the byte"},
        "3979": {"comment":"Thin: rotate by twice (pixel + 1)"},
        "3985": {"synopsis":"Rotates the byte left B times and keeps the bits in D.","comment":"The byte"},
        "3986": {"synopsis":"Rotates the screen byte left once per count.","comment":"Rotate the pixel to the bottom"},
        "3989": {"comment":"Then mask it"},
        "3991": {"synopsis":"Two pixels in the byte: rotates 4 for an even x, none for an odd one.","comment":"The byte; 4 rotations for an even x"},
        "3994": {"comment":"x odd?"},
        "3996": {"comment":"Even: rotate"},
        "3998": {"synopsis":"Keeps the pixel's bits (D).","comment":"Keep the pixel's bits"},
        "3999": {"synopsis":"Puts HMPR back ($3FC6, the HMPR-only entry of RESTORE_PAGING) and stacks A.","comment":"HMPR back (ROM0's $3FC6)"},
        "4002": {"comment":"Stack A"},
        "4004": {"synopsis":"Takes two numbers off the calculator stack as bytes (GET_BYTE): the top must be below L, the\nnext below H.\nEntry: H, L = the limits.\nExit: E = the top number; D = A = the next.\nError: 32 when either is out of range; 30 when it is not 0-255.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Keep the limits"},
        "4005": {"comment":"The top number"},
        "4009": {"comment":"Below L?"},
        "4010": {"comment":"No: error 32"},
        "4012": {"comment":"Keep it and the limits"},
        "4014": {"comment":"The next number"},
        "4018": {"comment":"E = the top number"},
        "4019": {"comment":"D = the next"},
        "4020": {"comment":"Below H?"},
        "4022": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 32.","comment":"Stops with error code 32"},
        "4024": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $5B (INKEY$ #): reads a character from stream n (0-16, error 30\notherwise, through $1F62 in ROM0) through its channel's input routine (SELECT_STREAM,\nCHAN_INPUT), then puts the current channel back (SELECT_CHANNEL); goes on in INKEY_RESULT.\nEntry: n on the calculator stack.\nExit: the string on the calculator stack.\nError: 30 for a stream out of range; 47 when it is closed.","comment":"17 streams; error 30"},
        "4027": {"comment":"A = the stream, 0-16"},
        "4030": {"comment":"Keep CURCHL"},
        "4034": {"comment":"Select the stream"},
        "4037": {"comment":"Read a character"},
        "4040": {"comment":"The old channel"},
        "4041": {"comment":"Keep the result"},
        "4042": {"comment":"Select it again"},
        "4046": {"synopsis":"Stacks a key as a string: one character, or the empty string (five 0 bytes) when there is\nnone. ROM0's FN_READ_KEY (INKEY$) jumps here through RST $30 after READ_KEY_FLUSH;\nCALC_INKEY_STRM comes here too.\nEntry: carry when there is a character, A = it.\nExit: the string on the calculator stack.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"D = the character"},
        "4047": {"comment":"Got one: a 1-character string"},
        "4049": {"comment":"None: five 0 bytes, an empty string"},
        "4052": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $4B (BUTTON): BUTTON n for n 0-3 (error 30 otherwise, through $1F62 in\nROM0) gives 1 when the mouse buttons ANDed with a mask are not 0: n = 0 any button ($FF), 1\nbit 0, 2 bit 1, 3 bit 2, from the byte at $5B8F in MSEDP.\nEntry: n on the calculator stack.\nExit: 0 or 1 on the calculator stack.\nError: 30.","comment":"4 buttons, 0-3; error 30"},
        "4055": {"comment":"A = n"},
        "4058": {"comment":"n = 3 gives mask 4; 1, 2 stay"},
        "4062": {"comment":"n = 0: all the buttons"},
        "4065": {"synopsis":"Tests the mouse buttons byte with the mask.","comment":"The mouse buttons byte in MSEDP"},
        "4068": {"comment":"Any of them?"},
        "4071": {"comment":"Then 1"},
        "4073": {"synopsis":"Stacks A (STK_A in ROM0) and returns from there.","comment":"Stack A"},
        "4076": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $4A (SVAR): adds the word at ROM1 $FE44 ($5A00, where the system\nvariables start) to the top: SVAR n is the address $5A00 + n.\nEntry: n on the calculator stack.\nExit: the address in its place; returns from the calculator's caller as well.","comment":"Plus the word at $FE44: $5A00"},
        "4082": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $56 (CHR$): a one-character string of the byte n (GET_BYTE).\nEntry: n on the calculator stack.\nExit: the string on the calculator stack.\nError: 30 when n is not 0-255.","comment":"n, 0-255"},
        "4085": {"comment":"D = the character"},
        "4086": {"synopsis":"Stacks the character D as a one-byte string: puts it in TEMPW1 ($5AC8) and copies it to the\nworkspace (STK_STR_COPY).\nEntry: D = the character.\nExit: the string on the calculator stack.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"One byte"},
        "4089": {"comment":"TEMPW1 = the character"},
        "4095": {"comment":"Copy it and stack the string"},
        "4098": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $58 (BIN$, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): makes the binary digits of a\nnumber 0-65535, 8 digits when it is below 256, else 16. A 1 bit is the character in $5A03, a\n0 bit the one in $5A04 (a run saw \"1\" and \"0\": BIN$ 5 gave \"00000101\"). The digits are built\nbackwards below $5131, then stacked as a string copy (DIGITS_TO_STR).\nEntry: the number on the calculator stack.\nExit: the string on the calculator stack.\nError: stops with error code 30 for a number not 0-65535 (GET_UINT16).","comment":"The number, 0-65535 (GET_UINT16)"},
        "4101": {"comment":"DE = the number"},
        "4102": {"comment":"High byte 0?"},
        "4103": {"comment":"Then 8 digits"},
        "4108": {"comment":"Else 16"},
        "4110": {"synopsis":"BIN$ with C = the digit count: the digits go backwards from $5130.","comment":"The end of the digit buffer"},
        "4113": {"comment":"B = the digit count"},
        "4114": {"synopsis":"One digit a pass: the low bit of DE picks the character.","comment":"The next digit backwards"},
        "4115": {"comment":"The low bit to carry"},
        "4119": {"comment":"$5A03: the character for 1"},
        "4122": {"comment":"A 1?"},
        "4124": {"comment":"No: $5A04, the character for 0"},
        "4127": {"synopsis":"Stores the digit and loops for the next.","comment":"Store the digit"},
        "4128": {"comment":"For every digit"},
        "4130": {"synopsis":"Stacks a copy of the BC characters at HL as a string (STK_STR_COPY). BIN$ and HEX$ end here.\nEntry: HL = the characters; BC = their count.","comment":"Stack a copy (STK_STR_COPY)"},
        "4133": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $59 (HEX$, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): makes the hexadecimal digits of a\nlinear address: 2 digits below 256, 4 below 64K, 6 above (a run gave 6 for 70000).\nADDR_TO_PAGE splits the number; its 16K block count's low 2 bits become BC's top bits, the\nrest the third byte. Each byte's two digits are pushed by HEX_PUSH_BYTE, then popped\nbackwards into the buffer below $5127 and stacked (DIGITS_TO_STR).\nEntry: the number on the calculator stack.\nExit: the string on the calculator stack.\nError: stops with error code 30 for 33 blocks or more (ADDR_TO_PAGE).","comment":"A = 16K blocks, BC = the rest (ADDR_TO_PAGE)"},
        "4136": {"comment":"The blocks' low 2 bits to bits 7-6"},
        "4138": {"comment":"H = the rotated block count"},
        "4139": {"comment":"B's bits 7-6 from them"},
        "4143": {"comment":"B = the address's high byte"},
        "4144": {"comment":"E counts the digits"},
        "4146": {"comment":"Anything above C?"},
        "4147": {"comment":"No: two digits only"},
        "4149": {"comment":"The blocks' high bits: a third byte?"},
        "4152": {"comment":"No: four digits"},
        "4154": {"comment":"Keep B in A'"},
        "4157": {"comment":"B = the top byte"},
        "4158": {"comment":"Its two digits"},
        "4161": {"comment":"B back"},
        "4163": {"synopsis":"HEX$: the digits of B (the middle byte, or the top byte on the first pass).","comment":"B's two digits"},
        "4166": {"synopsis":"HEX$: the digits of C, the low byte, which every number has.","comment":"Then C's"},
        "4170": {"comment":"C = the digit count"},
        "4173": {"comment":"The digits end before $5127"},
        "4176": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "4177": {"synopsis":"Pops the E digit characters into the buffer, last digit first, from $5126 down.","comment":"Back one place"},
        "4178": {"comment":"The next digit, last first"},
        "4179": {"comment":"Store it"},
        "4180": {"comment":"For every digit"},
        "4182": {"comment":"Stack them (DIGITS_TO_STR)"},
        "4184": {"synopsis":"Pushes the two hexadecimal digit characters of B (high digit first) under the return\naddress, and counts them in E.\nEntry: B = the byte; E = the count so far.\nExit: E + 2; the two characters on the stack.\nChanges: AF, D, HL.","comment":"Two more digits"},
        "4186": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "4187": {"comment":"Two digits"},
        "4189": {"comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "4190": {"comment":"The high nibble first"},
        "4194": {"synopsis":"One digit: the low nibble of A to \"0\"-\"9\" or \"A\"-\"F\" (CP $0A, SBC $69, DAA), pushed.","comment":"One nibble"},
        "4196": {"comment":"0-9 or A-F as its character"},
        "4201": {"comment":"Under the return address"},
        "4202": {"comment":"The low nibble next"},
        "4203": {"comment":"Both done?"},
        "4206": {"comment":"Return"},
        "4207": {"synopsis":"MEM$'s running part (ROM0's FN_MEM_STR jumps here through RST $30): MEM$(a TO b) as a string\nthat is the memory itself, not a copy. The calculator keeps a in memory 0 and works out the\nlength b - a + constant 9 (1: a run gave 1 for MEM$(10 TO 10)); when operation $2C finds it\nnegative, operation $07 and constant 1 replace it (a run gave 0 for MEM$(10 TO 5)). Then a's\nlinear address becomes a page and an offset at $8000 (ADDR_TO_PAGE) and the string is\nstacked (STK_STR).\nEntry: a and b on the calculator stack.\nExit: the string on the calculator stack.\nError: 30 for an address or length out of range.","comment":"Calculator: MEM$ (a TO b)"},
        "4208": {"comment":"Swap: a on top"},
        "4209": {"comment":"Memory 0 = a"},
        "4210": {"comment":"b - a"},
        "4211": {"comment":"Constant 9 (1)"},
        "4212": {"comment":"Added: the length"},
        "4213": {"comment":"Duplicate it"},
        "4214": {"comment":"Negative?"},
        "4215": {"comment":"No: jump to $D07B"},
        "4217": {"comment":"Negative: replaced"},
        "4218": {"comment":"by constant 1 (0, by the run)"},
        "4219": {"comment":"Recall a"},
        "4220": {"comment":"End"},
        "4221": {"comment":"a as 16K blocks (A) and offset (HL)"},
        "4224": {"comment":"The offset at $8000"},
        "4226": {"comment":"The page (block - 1)"},
        "4227": {"comment":"Keep page and address"},
        "4229": {"comment":"The length, 0-65535 (GET_UINT16)"},
        "4232": {"comment":"DE = the address"},
        "4233": {"comment":"A = the page"},
        "4234": {"comment":"Stack the string AEDCB (STK_STR)"},
        "4237": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $02 (the table at ROM1 $C6FB), joins two strings: makes room for both\nat WKEND (WORKSP_ROOM, error 42 when the total would pass 64K), stacks the new string, then\ncopies the first string and the second after it with the far copy (ROM0's $2A5E, then $2A68,\nwhich goes on where the first copy left off).\nEntry: the two strings on the calculator stack, the second on top; DE kept.\nExit: the joined string on the calculator stack; HMPR put back.\nError: stops with error code 42 when the length reaches 64K.","comment":"HMPR, put back at the end"},
        "4240": {"comment":"Keep DE"},
        "4241": {"comment":"The second string: A, DE, BC (STK_FETCH)"},
        "4244": {"comment":"Keep its page, start and length"},
        "4247": {"comment":"Its length again, for the total"},
        "4248": {"comment":"The first string (STK_FETCH)"},
        "4251": {"comment":"The second's length"},
        "4252": {"comment":"Total length: 64K or more?"},
        "4253": {"comment":"Stops with error code 42 (LEN_OVER_ERR)"},
        "4256": {"comment":"Keep the first string"},
        "4259": {"comment":"BC = the total"},
        "4261": {"comment":"Room at WKEND for it (WORKSP_ROOM)"},
        "4264": {"comment":"Stack the new string (STK_STR_HMPR)"},
        "4267": {"comment":"The first's length"},
        "4268": {"comment":"In pages and bytes (SPLIT_PAGES)"},
        "4271": {"comment":"C = the destination page (HMPR)"},
        "4274": {"comment":"HL = the first's start"},
        "4275": {"comment":"A = its page"},
        "4276": {"comment":"Copy it upwards (ROM0's $2A5E: JFARLDIR's SCF)"},
        "4279": {"comment":"The second's length"},
        "4280": {"comment":"In pages and bytes (SPLIT_PAGES)"},
        "4283": {"comment":"DE = the second's start"},
        "4284": {"comment":"H = its page"},
        "4285": {"comment":"Upwards"},
        "4286": {"comment":"Copy it after the first (ROM0's $2A68)"},
        "4289": {"comment":"DE as on entry"},
        "4290": {"comment":"HMPR put back (RESTORE_HMPR)"},
        "4293": {"synopsis":"Reads a hexadecimal number after \"&\" (READ_NUMBER in ROM0 jumps here through RST $30 when\nthe character is \"&\"): digits 0-9 and A-F or a-f into a 24-bit value in A' and HL, error 28\npast 24 bits. A value up to 65535 is stacked as a small integer (STK_BC); a bigger one is\nnormalised to a floating point number (exponent $98 counted down) and stacked by STK_STORE.\nEntry: HL = CHAD at the \"&\".\nExit: the number on the calculator stack; CHAD at the first character that is not a digit.\nError: stops with error code 28 for a value past 24 bits (ERROR_28_STOP).","comment":"The value: A' = high byte, HL = low word"},
        "4297": {"synopsis":"The next character (RST $20): a digit?","comment":"DE = the value's low word meanwhile"},
        "4298": {"comment":"The next character (RST $20)"},
        "4300": {"comment":"A digit 0-9?"},
        "4304": {"comment":"Below 10?"},
        "4308": {"comment":"Back to the character, lower case"},
        "4312": {"comment":"Below \"a\"?"},
        "4316": {"comment":"Past \"f\"?"},
        "4320": {"comment":"\"a\"-\"f\" to 10-15"},
        "4322": {"synopsis":"Shifts the 24-bit value left 4 bits and puts the digit in.","comment":"Four bits of shift"},
        "4324": {"comment":"A = the high byte"},
        "4325": {"synopsis":"One bit of the shift: past 24 bits is error 28.","comment":"Shift HL left"},
        "4326": {"comment":"Into the high byte"},
        "4327": {"comment":"Past 24 bits: stops with error code 28"},
        "4330": {"comment":"Four times"},
        "4332": {"comment":"A = the digit"},
        "4333": {"comment":"Into the low nibble"},
        "4335": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "4337": {"synopsis":"The end of the digits: BC = the low 16 bits; a zero top byte stacks BC.","comment":"BC = the low word"},
        "4339": {"comment":"The high byte zero?"},
        "4341": {"comment":"Yes: stack BC"},
        "4343": {"comment":"The exponent for 24 bits"},
        "4345": {"synopsis":"Normalises: shifts until bit 7 of the top byte is set, one less on the exponent each time.","comment":"Top bit set?"},
        "4349": {"comment":"No: shift the 24 bits left"},
        "4351": {"comment":"One less on the exponent"},
        "4353": {"synopsis":"Clears the sign bit (positive) and stacks exponent B and the 4 mantissa bytes.","comment":"Positive: the sign bit off"},
        "4355": {"comment":"The mantissa: E, D, C, then B = 0"},
        "4358": {"comment":"A = the exponent"},
        "4361": {"comment":"Stack it (STK_STORE)"},
        "4364": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $5A (USR$, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): runs machine code at the linear\naddress on the calculator stack; ROM0's CALL_CODE_STR (with ROM1 paged out) stacks the\nstring AEDCB the code leaves.\nEntry: the address on the calculator stack.\nExit: through CALL_CODE_STR.","comment":"USR$: to ROM0's CALL_CODE_STR, ROM1 out"},
        "4369": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $45 (USR, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): runs machine code at the linear\naddress on the calculator stack; ROM0's $17FB (inside CALL_CODE_STR) stacks the BC the code\nleaves.\nEntry: the address on the calculator stack.\nExit: through ROM0's $17FB.","comment":"USR: to ROM0's $17FB, ROM1 out"},
        "4374": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $47 (PEEK, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): the byte at a linear address\n(LINEAR_ADDR pages it in at HMPR), read with ROM1 paged out (PEEK_HL_R1OFF), stacked as a\nnumber.\nEntry: the address on the calculator stack.\nExit: the byte on the calculator stack; HMPR put back.\nError: 30 for an address of 33 blocks or more.","comment":"Page in the address (LINEAR_ADDR)"},
        "4377": {"comment":"D = the HMPR to put back"},
        "4378": {"comment":"High byte 0"},
        "4379": {"comment":"Read the byte"},
        "4381": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $48 (DPEEK, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): the word at a linear address, low\nbyte first, each byte read with ROM1 paged out; ADDR_PAGE_IN moves an address past $BFFF to\nthe next page.\nEntry: the address on the calculator stack.\nExit: the word on the calculator stack; HMPR put back.\nError: 30 for an address out of range.","comment":"HMPR, put back at the end"},
        "4384": {"comment":"Page in the address (ADDR_PAGE_IN)"},
        "4387": {"comment":"The high byte first"},
        "4388": {"comment":"Read with ROM1 out (PEEK_HL_R1OFF)"},
        "4391": {"comment":"Back to the low byte"},
        "4392": {"comment":"D = the saved HMPR"},
        "4393": {"synopsis":"B = A (the high byte, 0 for PEEK) and C = the byte at HL; D holds the HMPR to put back.","comment":"B = the high byte"},
        "4394": {"comment":"The low byte"},
        "4397": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "4398": {"comment":"The saved HMPR"},
        "4399": {"synopsis":"Puts HMPR back from A and stacks BC (STK_BC). INSTR's code jumps here too (ROM1 $E8CD).\nEntry: A = the HMPR value; BC = the number.","comment":"HMPR put back"},
        "4401": {"synopsis":"Stacks BC as a small integer (STK_BC) and returns through it; several operations end here.\nEntry: BC = the number.","comment":"Stack BC (STK_BC)"},
        "4404": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $55 (TRUNC$, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): the string without its trailing\nspaces. It is copied to the buffer at $4F00 (STR_TO_BUFFER, so 1-255 characters) and the\nspaces counted off its end; a run gave LEN TRUNC$ \"ab  \" = 2. When nothing is left, STK_BC\nstacks five zero bytes, which read as an empty string.\nEntry: the string on the calculator stack.\nExit: the shortened copy on the calculator stack.\nError: stops with error code 27 for an empty string or one over 255 characters.","comment":"The string to $4F00 (STR_TO_BUFFER)"},
        "4407": {"comment":"HL = $4F00"},
        "4409": {"comment":"Past its last character"},
        "4410": {"comment":"Trailing spaces"},
        "4412": {"synopsis":"Steps back over one trailing space; a character that is not a space ends the loop.","comment":"Back one character"},
        "4413": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "4414": {"comment":"No: the length is C"},
        "4416": {"comment":"One less"},
        "4417": {"comment":"More characters?"},
        "4419": {"comment":"All spaces: five zero bytes, an empty string"},
        "4421": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $57 (STR$, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): ROM1 $D997 (JSTRS's body) makes\nthe number's text, and the text is stacked as a string copy.\nEntry: the number on the calculator stack.\nExit: the string on the calculator stack.","comment":"The number's text (JSTRS's body)"},
        "4424": {"synopsis":"Stacks the BC characters at DE as a string copy (STK_STR_COPY with HL = DE).","comment":"HL = the text"},
        "4425": {"comment":"Stack a copy (STK_STR_COPY)"},
        "4428": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $52 (CODE, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): the code of a string's first\ncharacter, 0 for an empty string. The string is paged in (UNSTK_STR_IN) and HMPR put back.\nEntry: the string on the calculator stack.\nExit: the number on the calculator stack.","comment":"HMPR, put back at the end"},
        "4431": {"comment":"The string, paged in (UNSTK_STR_IN)"},
        "4434": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "4436": {"comment":"Yes: BC = 0"},
        "4438": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "4439": {"comment":"BC = its code"},
        "4442": {"synopsis":"Takes the saved HMPR and stacks BC (PUT_HMPR_STK_BC).","comment":"The saved HMPR"},
        "4443": {"comment":"Put it back and stack BC"},
        "4445": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $51 (LEN, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): unstacks the string (STK_FETCH) and\nstacks its length.\nEntry: the string on the calculator stack.\nExit: the length on the calculator stack.","comment":"The string: BC = its length (STK_FETCH)"},
        "4448": {"comment":"Stack the length"},
        "4450": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $43 (SQR, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): the square root by Newton's method.\nThe number goes through operation $31 (after which only zero has a zero exponent) and is\nkept in memory 0; zero gives zero. The first guess halves the exponent (bias $80) with the\nmantissa's top byte $7F; then 5 passes of guess = (guess + x / guess) / 2, the halving done\nby decrementing the exponent.\nEntry: HL = the top value (as the calculator leaves it).\nExit: the root in its place.\nError: stops with error code 27 for a negative number (STR_BUF_ERR).","comment":"Calculator: x for the square root"},
        "4451": {"comment":"Operation $31"},
        "4452": {"comment":"Memory 0 = x"},
        "4453": {"comment":"End"},
        "4454": {"comment":"The exponent"},
        "4455": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "4456": {"comment":"Yes: the root is 0"},
        "4457": {"comment":"Halve the exponent (bias $80)"},
        "4460": {"comment":"The first guess's exponent"},
        "4461": {"comment":"The sign and top mantissa byte"},
        "4462": {"comment":"Negative?"},
        "4464": {"comment":"Stops with error code 27 (STR_BUF_ERR)"},
        "4467": {"comment":"The first guess's mantissa"},
        "4469": {"comment":"Five passes"},
        "4471": {"synopsis":"One Newton pass: guess + x / guess, then the exponent's DEC (HL) halves it.","comment":"Calculator: one Newton pass"},
        "4472": {"comment":"Duplicate the guess"},
        "4473": {"comment":"Recall x"},
        "4474": {"comment":"Swap: guess on top"},
        "4475": {"comment":"x / guess"},
        "4476": {"comment":"Added to the guess"},
        "4477": {"comment":"End"},
        "4478": {"comment":"Halved: one less on the exponent"},
        "4479": {"comment":"Five times"},
        "4482": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $41 (ABS, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): a floating point number loses its\nsign bit; a small integer with sign byte $FF is negated (NEG_SMALL_INT).\nEntry: HL = the number.\nExit: the number made positive in place.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"The exponent"},
        "4483": {"comment":"To the sign byte"},
        "4484": {"comment":"Floating point?"},
        "4485": {"comment":"Yes: clear its sign bit"},
        "4487": {"comment":"A small integer: sign byte $FF?"},
        "4489": {"comment":"No: already positive"},
        "4490": {"comment":"Negative: negate it"},
        "4492": {"synopsis":"A floating point number: clears the sign bit.","comment":"Sign bit off"},
        "4495": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $5D (unary minus, the table at ROM1 $C6FB; ROM1 $CD39 calls it too): a\nfloating point number's sign bit is flipped; a small integer's sign byte is complemented and\nits value negated; zero stays zero.\nEntry: HL = the number.\nExit: the number negated in place.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"The exponent"},
        "4496": {"comment":"To the sign byte"},
        "4497": {"comment":"Floating point?"},
        "4498": {"comment":"Yes: flip its sign bit"},
        "4500": {"comment":"A small integer: the value"},
        "4504": {"comment":"Zero stays zero"},
        "4505": {"comment":"Back to the sign byte"},
        "4507": {"comment":"The sign complemented"},
        "4509": {"synopsis":"Stores the sign byte, then replaces the 16-bit value with its two's complement.","comment":"Store the sign byte"},
        "4510": {"comment":"The value's low byte, complemented"},
        "4514": {"comment":"Its high byte, complemented"},
        "4518": {"comment":"Plus 1: the two's complement"},
        "4519": {"comment":"Stored back"},
        "4523": {"synopsis":"A floating point number: flips the sign bit.","comment":"Flip the sign bit"},
        "4528": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $42 (SGN, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): zero stays; otherwise the number\nbecomes the small integer 1 or -1 by its sign (ROM1 $CBC8 writes it).\nEntry: HL = the number.\nExit: -1, 0 or 1 in its place.","comment":"Zero? (ROM1 $C952)"},
        "4531": {"comment":"HL = the number, DE = STKEND"},
        "4532": {"comment":"Zero stays"},
        "4533": {"comment":"Keep STKEND"},
        "4534": {"comment":"The sign"},
        "4538": {"comment":"C = $FF negative, 0 positive"},
        "4540": {"comment":"Value 1"},
        "4543": {"comment":"Write the small integer (ROM1 $CBC8)"},
        "4546": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $44 (INT, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): rounds down. A small integer is\nalready whole. Otherwise operation $2E (1 for a number above 0, ROM1 $C8C1) and the $1E jump\nsend a positive number to INT_POS_CALC (truncate and end); a negative one is truncated\n(operation $30), and when the fraction was not zero subtracts constant 9 (1); a run gave INT\n-2.5 = -3.\nEntry: HL = the number.\nExit: the whole number in its place.","comment":"The exponent"},
        "4547": {"comment":"A small integer is whole already"},
        "4549": {"comment":"Calculator: rounds down"},
        "4550": {"comment":"Duplicate"},
        "4551": {"comment":"Operation $2E: above 0?"},
        "4552": {"comment":"Yes: jump to $D1D4"},
        "4554": {"comment":"Negative: duplicate"},
        "4555": {"comment":"Truncate (operation $30)"},
        "4556": {"comment":"Duplicate"},
        "4557": {"comment":"Swap the top and the third"},
        "4558": {"comment":"x - truncated: the fraction"},
        "4559": {"comment":"No fraction: jump to $D1D3"},
        "4561": {"comment":"Constant 9 (1)"},
        "4562": {"comment":"Subtracted: one lower"},
        "4563": {"comment":"End, and return from the caller"},
        "4564": {"synopsis":"INT's calculator bytes for the jump at ROM1 $D1C8: operation $30 (truncate, OP_TRUNCATE),\nthen $34 (end, and return from the caller). The decoder ends the stream at $D1D3, so these\ntwo bytes are marked as data.","comment":"Truncate, then end and return from the caller"},
        "4566": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $30 (the table at ROM1 $C6FB): truncates the number towards zero.\nExponent $81-$90 (1 to 65535): the top 16 mantissa bits are shifted down into a small\ninteger with the sign, written by ROM1 $CBC8. Below 1 all 40 bits are cleared (zero); from\n$91 the fraction bits ($A0 - exponent) are cleared from the end; from $A0 there are none.\nEntry: HL = the number; DE = STKEND.\nExit: HL = the truncated number in its place; DE kept.","comment":"The exponent"},
        "4567": {"comment":"A small integer is whole already"},
        "4569": {"comment":"Bits in a byte"},
        "4571": {"comment":"Below 1?"},
        "4573": {"comment":"Yes: clear it all ($D210)"},
        "4575": {"comment":"65536 or more?"},
        "4577": {"comment":"Yes: clear the fraction bits"},
        "4579": {"comment":"Keep STKEND"},
        "4580": {"comment":"DE = the top 16 mantissa bits"},
        "4584": {"comment":"Back to the exponent"},
        "4586": {"comment":"C = $FF: negative"},
        "4588": {"comment":"Sign bit set?"},
        "4590": {"comment":"Yes: negative"},
        "4592": {"comment":"Positive: the implied top bit"},
        "4594": {"comment":"C = 0"},
        "4595": {"synopsis":"A = the shift count; past 8 the low byte goes and the high byte moves down.","comment":"A = $90 - the exponent: the shift"},
        "4598": {"comment":"8 or more?"},
        "4602": {"comment":"Yes: a byte at once"},
        "4605": {"comment":"Eight fewer"},
        "4606": {"synopsis":"No shift left: store the integer.","comment":"No more shifting?"},
        "4608": {"comment":"B = the shift count"},
        "4609": {"synopsis":"Shifts DE right one bit, B times.","comment":"One bit right"},
        "4613": {"comment":"B times"},
        "4615": {"synopsis":"Writes the small integer (sign C, value DE) at HL (ROM1 $CBC8).","comment":"Write it as a small integer (ROM1 $CBC8)"},
        "4618": {"synopsis":"Exponent $91 and up: A = the count of fraction bits; $A0 and up has none (RET P). The LD\n($283E),HL after it writes to ROM: it only hides the LD A,$28 at $D210, the entry for a\nnumber below 1 (clear all 40 bits).","comment":"A = the exponent - $A0"},
        "4620": {"comment":"$A0 or more: no fraction bits"},
        "4621": {"comment":"A = the fraction bit count"},
        "4623": {"comment":"Writes ROM: hides LD A,$28 at $D210 (clear 40 bits)"},
        "4626": {"comment":"Keep STKEND"},
        "4627": {"comment":"HL = the number's end"},
        "4628": {"comment":"Writes ROM: hides LD (HL),0 at $D215, the loop"},
        "4631": {"comment":"Back one byte"},
        "4632": {"comment":"A whole byte to clear?"},
        "4633": {"comment":"Yes: clear it ($D215)"},
        "4635": {"comment":"The bits left in the last byte"},
        "4636": {"comment":"None?"},
        "4638": {"comment":"B = their count"},
        "4639": {"comment":"A = $FF"},
        "4640": {"synopsis":"Builds the mask that clears the low A bits of the last partly cleared byte.","comment":"Shift in that many zero bits"},
        "4643": {"comment":"Clear them in the byte"},
        "4645": {"synopsis":"HL back to the number; DE restored.","comment":"HL = the number"},
        "4646": {"comment":"STKEND back"},
        "4648": {"synopsis":"Calculator operation $4F (UDG, the table at ROM1 $C6FB): the address of a character's 8-byte\npattern. The string must be one character of code 32 or more. Codes below $80 count from\nCHARS, $80-$A8 from UDG - $480 (the UDG set starts at code $90), $A9 and up from HUDG; the\naddress is the base + 8 x the code (UDG_PATTERN_ADDR) stacked as a number.\nEntry: the string on the calculator stack.\nExit: the address on the calculator stack.\nError: stops with error code 27 for a string that is not one character, or a control code.","comment":"The string to $4F00 (STR_TO_BUFFER)"},
        "4651": {"comment":"One character?"},
        "4652": {"synopsis":"A wrong length or a code below 32: stops with error code 27 (STR_BUF_ERR).","comment":"No: stops with error code 27"},
        "4655": {"comment":"The character"},
        "4656": {"comment":"A control code?"},
        "4660": {"comment":"CHARS for the main set"},
        "4663": {"comment":"Below $80?"},
        "4667": {"comment":"UDG for $80-$A8"},
        "4670": {"comment":"Less $480: the UDG set starts at $90"},
        "4674": {"comment":"Below $A9?"},
        "4678": {"comment":"HUDG for $A9 and up, counted from 0"},
        "4683": {"synopsis":"DE = the base, HL = the code x 8 + the base, stacked (STK_HL).","comment":"DE = the base"},
        "4684": {"comment":"HL = the code"},
        "4687": {"comment":"x 8"},
        "4690": {"comment":"Plus the base"},
        "4691": {"comment":"Stack the address (STK_HL)"},
        "4694": {"synopsis":"JSCRN's body (ROM0's jump table entry at $0101 jumps here through RST $30): makes screen C\nthe current screen (SCREEN_SELECT).\nEntry: C = the screen, 1-16.\nError: stops with error code 43 when it is not open or not 1-16.","comment":"Screen C's slot"},
        "4697": {"comment":"Select it"},
        "4699": {"synopsis":"SCREEN's command address (CMDADDRT, token $E7): SCREEN n, the current screen for output. The\nnumber is checked or evaluated (SYN_NUM), then as SCREEN_SELECT.\nEntry: the BASIC pointer after SCREEN.\nError: 43 for a screen not open or not 1-16.","comment":"The screen number (SYN_NUM)"},
        "4702": {"comment":"Its slot (SCREEN_NUM_FIND)"},
        "4705": {"synopsis":"Makes the screen whose SCLIST slot HL points at the current one: the old slot (SCPTR) gets\nCUSCRNP, SCPTR = the new slot, the old screen's variables are saved into it (ROM0's $3BDF)\nand the new screen's loaded (LOAD_SCREEN_VARS). When CURDISP is 0 the new screen is also\ndisplayed (DISP_CURRENT).\nEntry: Z (from SCREEN_FIND) when the screen is not open; HL = its SCLIST slot; A = the slot.\nError: stops with error code 43 when it is not open.","comment":"Not open: stops with error code 43"},
        "4707": {"comment":"CUSCRNP, the current screen's byte"},
        "4710": {"comment":"The current screen's slot (SCPTR)"},
        "4714": {"comment":"Updated"},
        "4715": {"comment":"SCPTR = the new screen's slot"},
        "4718": {"comment":"The new screen's byte"},
        "4720": {"comment":"Save the variables into the old screen"},
        "4723": {"comment":"The new screen's byte"},
        "4724": {"comment":"Load its variables (LOAD_SCREEN_VARS)"},
        "4727": {"comment":"CURDISP"},
        "4730": {"comment":"0: show the current screen (DISP_CURRENT)"},
        "4735": {"synopsis":"Takes a screen number off the calculator stack (GET_BYTE), then as SCREEN_FIND.","comment":"The screen number (GET_BYTE)"},
        "4738": {"synopsis":"Finds screen C's slot in SCLIST, 16 bytes, one per screen: the screen's mode in bits 6-5 and\nits first page in bits 4-0, $FF when it is not open (a run: $7E for screen 1 after boot,\nmode 4 on page 30; OPEN SCREEN 2,4 gave $7C). ROM0's SET_CURDISP reaches it through RST $30.\nEntry: C = the screen, 1-16.\nExit: HL = the slot; A = its byte; Z when the screen is not open; C = the screen - 1.\nError: stops with error code 43 when C is not 1-16.\nChanges: AF, B, C, HL.","comment":"0-15"},
        "4739": {"comment":"A = the screen - 1"},
        "4740": {"comment":"16 or more?"},
        "4742": {"synopsis":"Screen number out of range, or (from SCREEN_SELECT, with Z and no carry) not open:\nDISPLAY_ERR.","comment":"Stops with error code 43 (DISPLAY_ERR)"},
        "4745": {"comment":"SCLIST"},
        "4748": {"comment":"HL = the screen's slot"},
        "4751": {"comment":"A = its byte"},
        "4752": {"comment":"Z: not open"},
        "4755": {"synopsis":"CLOSE's command address (CMDADDRT, token $99). CLOSE #n closes a stream: one on channel K,\nS, P, $ or B (CHAN_LETTER_TEST) is closed here, any other is passed to the DOS (hook 135).\nStreams 0-3 go back to their start-up channel (the bytes at ROM0 $0290), the others to 0\n(closed). CLOSE SCREEN and CLOSE n go on at CLOSE_NOT_STREAM.\nEntry: A = the character after CLOSE.\nError: 21 or 30 for a bad stream number.","comment":"\"#\"?"},
        "4757": {"comment":"No: CLOSE SCREEN or CLOSE n"},
        "4759": {"comment":"The stream number (SYN_NEXT_NUM)"},
        "4762": {"comment":"Its word (STREAM_FROM_CALC)"},
        "4765": {"comment":"Closed already: done"},
        "4766": {"comment":"Keep the word's address"},
        "4767": {"comment":"One of the ROM's channels?"},
        "4770": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "4772": {"comment":"Drop the word's address"},
        "4773": {"comment":"A DOS channel: hook 135 closes it"},
        "4776": {"synopsis":"A stream on one of the ROM's channels: 0-3 get their start-up word, 4 and up 0.","comment":"D = 0"},
        "4779": {"comment":"The stream number"},
        "4780": {"comment":"4 or more?"},
        "4782": {"comment":"Yes: E = 0, closed"},
        "4785": {"comment":"E = 0-3"},
        "4786": {"comment":"Its start-up byte at ROM0 $0290 + n"},
        "4790": {"comment":"Set the word from it"},
        "4793": {"synopsis":"CLOSE without \"#\": CLOSE SCREEN n, else CLOSE n (PAGES_RELEASE).","comment":"SCREEN?"},
        "4795": {"comment":"Yes: CLOSE SCREEN"},
        "4797": {"comment":"The page count (SYN_NUM)"},
        "4800": {"synopsis":"CLOSE n (OPEN TO also jumps here): gives back n (1-30) of the pages ALLOCT marks $40 (memory\npages, 1 up to LASTPAGE): the n below the first page not marked are cleared and LASTPAGE\nmoves down. It may not go below RAMTOPP + 1.\nEntry: n on the calculator stack.\nError: stops with error code 1 when the pages left would not reach past RAMTOPP; 30 for n\nnot 1-30.","comment":"B = C = n, HL = past the pages held"},
        "4803": {"comment":"RAMTOPP + 1"},
        "4807": {"comment":"E = the lowest page to keep"},
        "4808": {"comment":"The page after the release"},
        "4810": {"comment":"Below page 0?"},
        "4812": {"comment":"Below RAMTOPP + 1?"},
        "4813": {"synopsis":"Below page 0, or not past RAMTOPP: stops with error code 1 (NO_ROOM_ERR).","comment":"Stops with error code 1 (NO_ROOM_ERR)"},
        "4816": {"comment":"0: free"},
        "4817": {"synopsis":"Clears B entries of ALLOCT downwards.","comment":"Down one page"},
        "4818": {"comment":"Free it"},
        "4819": {"comment":"For n pages"},
        "4821": {"synopsis":"HL one down; LASTPAGE = its page number (L).\nEntry: HL = one past the last page marked.\nExit: HL = the last page's entry; A = LASTPAGE.","comment":"The last page held"},
        "4822": {"comment":"LASTPAGE = it"},
        "4827": {"synopsis":"The jump table entry ROM0's JT_018D (at $018D) reaches through RST $30: closes screen C\n(CLOSE_SCREEN).\nEntry: C = the screen, 1-16.\nError: 43 for screen 1 or a number not 1-16; 46 for the current screen.","comment":"Screen C's slot"},
        "4830": {"comment":"Close it"},
        "4832": {"synopsis":"CLOSE SCREEN n: the number, then its slot (SCREEN_NUM_FIND).","comment":"The screen number (SYN_NEXT_NUM)"},
        "4835": {"comment":"Its slot"},
        "4838": {"synopsis":"Closes the screen whose SCLIST slot HL holds: nothing when it is not open; screen 1 may not\nbe closed (error 43), nor the current screen (error 46). The slot becomes $FF and the\nscreen's two pages are freed in ALLOCT.\nEntry: Z when not open; HL = the slot; A = its byte; C = the screen - 1.\nError: stops with error code 43 for screen 1, 46 for the current screen.","comment":"Not open: nothing to do"},
        "4839": {"comment":"Screen 1?"},
        "4841": {"comment":"Yes: stops with error code 43"},
        "4844": {"comment":"B = its page"},
        "4847": {"comment":"The current screen's page"},
        "4852": {"comment":"The current screen?"},
        "4855": {"comment":"Stops with error code 46"},
        "4857": {"synopsis":"The slot closed ($FF) and the screen's page and the next one freed in ALLOCT.","comment":"The slot closed"},
        "4859": {"comment":"HL = the page's ALLOCT entry"},
        "4862": {"comment":"0: free"},
        "4863": {"comment":"The page freed"},
        "4864": {"comment":"And the next one"},
        "4867": {"synopsis":"OPEN's command address (CMDADDRT, token $98). OPEN #n;\"x\" opens a stream: a stream in use on\nchannel $ or B, or on a channel of the DOS, cannot be reopened (error 45). A one-letter name\nK, S, P, $ or B (either case, OPEN_LETTER_TAB) sets the stream's word to that channel's\ndisplacement; any other name goes to the DOS (hook 134). OPEN SCREEN and OPEN n go on at\nOPEN_NOT_STREAM.\nEntry: A = the character after OPEN.\nError: 45 for a stream in use; 18 for an empty name.","comment":"\"#\"?"},
        "4869": {"comment":"No: OPEN SCREEN or OPEN n"},
        "4872": {"comment":"The stream number (NEXT_NUM)"},
        "4875": {"comment":"\";\" or \",\" next"},
        "4878": {"comment":"The name (SYN_STR)"},
        "4881": {"comment":"The number back on top"},
        "4884": {"comment":"Its word (STREAM_FROM_CALC)"},
        "4887": {"comment":"Keep the word's address"},
        "4888": {"comment":"Closed: free to open"},
        "4890": {"comment":"Its channel: one of the ROM's?"},
        "4893": {"comment":"No: in use on a DOS channel"},
        "4895": {"comment":"K, S or P: may be opened again"},
        "4897": {"synopsis":"The stream is in use on a $ or B channel, or the DOS's: stops with error code 45.","comment":"Stops with error code 45"},
        "4899": {"synopsis":"The name: an empty one stops with error code 18 (ROM1 $E05C); one letter is looked up.","comment":"The name to $4F00 (STR_TO_BUF_255)"},
        "4902": {"comment":"Empty: stops with error code 18"},
        "4905": {"comment":"One character?"},
        "4906": {"comment":"No: the DOS's"},
        "4908": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "4909": {"comment":"In lower case"},
        "4911": {"comment":"OPEN_LETTER_TAB"},
        "4914": {"comment":"Five letters"},
        "4916": {"synopsis":"Compares the letter with one table entry; the byte after it is the displacement.","comment":"This one?"},
        "4917": {"comment":"To its displacement"},
        "4918": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "4920": {"comment":"To the next letter"},
        "4921": {"comment":"Five times"},
        "4923": {"synopsis":"A name the ROM does not know: the DOS opens it (hook 134).","comment":"Drop the word's address"},
        "4924": {"comment":"Hook 134: the DOS opens it"},
        "4927": {"synopsis":"E = the displacement from the table, then as STREAM_WORD_SET.","comment":"E = the displacement"},
        "4928": {"synopsis":"Sets the stream's word in STREAMS to E (high byte 0).\nEntry: the word's high byte address on the stack; E = the displacement.","comment":"The stream word's address"},
        "4929": {"comment":"High byte 0"},
        "4931": {"comment":"Low byte E"},
        "4934": {"synopsis":"OPEN's channel letters, read by ROM1 $D334: five pairs of a lower-case letter and the\nchannel's displacement from CHANS (k $01, s $06, p $10, $ $15, b $1A; channel R, $0B, cannot\nbe opened). The displacements match the start-up streams at ROM0 $028B.","comment":"Pairs of letter and displacement: k, s, p, $, b"},
        "4944": {"synopsis":"OPEN without \"#\": OPEN SCREEN, OPEN n (PAGES_RESERVE), or OPEN TO n, which makes LASTPAGE n\n- 1 by releasing (PAGES_RELEASE) or reserving the difference.","comment":"SCREEN?"},
        "4946": {"comment":"Yes: OPEN SCREEN"},
        "4948": {"comment":"TO?"},
        "4950": {"comment":"No: OPEN n"},
        "4952": {"comment":"The page count (SYN_NEXT_NUM)"},
        "4955": {"comment":"C = n (GET_BYTE)"},
        "4958": {"comment":"n - 1"},
        "4959": {"comment":"LASTPAGE"},
        "4962": {"comment":"The difference"},
        "4963": {"comment":"Already there: done"},
        "4964": {"comment":"More wanted"},
        "4966": {"comment":"Stack the pages to give back"},
        "4969": {"comment":"Release them (PAGES_RELEASE)"},
        "4972": {"synopsis":"OPEN TO n with n above the pages held: reserves the difference.","comment":"The pages to add"},
        "4974": {"comment":"Stacked"},
        "4977": {"comment":"Z: the count is stacked already"},
        "4978": {"synopsis":"OPEN n: reserves n (1-30) more memory pages: the n entries of ALLOCT after the last one\nmarked $40 must be free (error 1 otherwise); they are marked $40 and LASTPAGE becomes the\nlast (a run: OPEN 2 after boot marked pages 4 and 5, LASTPAGE 3 to 5). OPEN TO n enters with\nthe count already stacked and Z (CP A at $D371 skips the expression).\nEntry: Z with the count on the calculator stack, or NZ to evaluate it.\nError: stops with error code 1 when the pages are not free; 30 for n not 1-30.","comment":"The page count (SYN_NUM), unless stacked"},
        "4981": {"comment":"B = C = n, HL = past the pages held"},
        "4984": {"synopsis":"Each page must be free: a non-zero entry stops with error code 1.","comment":"Is the page free?"},
        "4986": {"comment":"No: stops with error code 1"},
        "4989": {"comment":"The next page"},
        "4990": {"comment":"For n pages"},
        "4992": {"comment":"B = n again"},
        "4993": {"comment":"LASTPAGE = the last new page"},
        "4996": {"synopsis":"Marks the pages $40, from the last down.","comment":"Mark it $40"},
        "4998": {"comment":"Down one"},
        "4999": {"comment":"For n pages"},
        "5002": {"synopsis":"JOPSCR's body (ROM0's jump table entry at $0158 jumps here through RST $30): opens screen C\nin mode B (OPEN_SCREEN_NEW).\nEntry: C = the screen, 2-16; B = the mode, 0-3.\nError: 43 for a number not 1-16; 44 when the screen is open; 1 for no room.","comment":"The mode, popped as A"},
        "5003": {"comment":"Screen C's slot"},
        "5006": {"comment":"Open it"},
        "5008": {"synopsis":"OPEN SCREEN n,m: m 1-4 (GET_BYTE_1_D with D = 4, error 34) and n, then as OPEN_SCREEN_NEW.","comment":"The screen and mode (SYN_NEXT_2NUM)"},
        "5011": {"comment":"Mode 1-4, else error 34"},
        "5014": {"comment":"A = the mode - 1 (GET_BYTE_1_D)"},
        "5017": {"comment":"Keep it"},
        "5018": {"comment":"The screen's slot (SCREEN_NUM_FIND)"},
        "5021": {"synopsis":"Opens the screen whose SCLIST slot HL holds, in mode A (stacked): it must not be open (error\n44). Two free pages, an even page and the next, are found from the top of ALLOCT down and\nmarked $C0; the slot gets the mode in bits 6-5 and the page. The old screen's variables and\nthe 40 bytes at $55D8 (the frame interrupt's two palettes) are saved to it; the new screen\nis made current, its mode set (MODE_SET_A, which clears it; THFATP 1 meanwhile) and the 40\nbytes and variables saved into it; then the old screen comes back with its variables and its\n40 bytes (a run: OPEN SCREEN 2,4 used pages 28-29, slot $7C).\nEntry: Z when the screen is not open; HL = the slot; the mode on the stack.\nError: stops with error code 44 when the screen is open; 1 when there are no two free pages.","comment":"Not open: go on"},
        "5023": {"comment":"Stops with error code 44"},
        "5025": {"synopsis":"Looks for a free pair of pages in ALLOCT.","comment":"Keep the slot"},
        "5026": {"comment":"From the top of ALLOCT"},
        "5029": {"synopsis":"Two entries down: both zero? Page 0 reached is error 1.","comment":"Down one page"},
        "5030": {"comment":"Its entry"},
        "5031": {"comment":"Down one more"},
        "5032": {"comment":"Page 0 reached: stops with error code 1"},
        "5035": {"comment":"Both pages free?"},
        "5036": {"comment":"No: the pair below"},
        "5038": {"comment":"DE = the slot"},
        "5039": {"comment":"A = the mode"},
        "5041": {"comment":"Both pages taken by the screen"},
        "5047": {"comment":"The mode to bits 6-5"},
        "5051": {"comment":"The page in bits 4-0"},
        "5055": {"comment":"The slot = mode and page"},
        "5056": {"comment":"Keep it"},
        "5057": {"comment":"Save the old screen's variables ($3BDF)"},
        "5060": {"comment":"And its 40 bytes from $55D8"},
        "5063": {"comment":"CUSCRNP"},
        "5066": {"comment":"B = the old screen's byte"},
        "5067": {"comment":"A = the new one"},
        "5068": {"comment":"The new screen current"},
        "5069": {"comment":"DE = the mode"},
        "5070": {"comment":"Keep the old screen's byte"},
        "5072": {"comment":"THFATP"},
        "5075": {"comment":"Kept in B"},
        "5076": {"comment":"1 meanwhile"},
        "5078": {"comment":"A = the mode"},
        "5079": {"comment":"Keep the old THFATP"},
        "5080": {"comment":"Set the mode in the new screen (MODE_SET_A)"},
        "5083": {"comment":"Save its 40 bytes from $55D8"},
        "5086": {"comment":"THFATP back"},
        "5090": {"comment":"Save the new screen's variables ($3BDF)"},
        "5093": {"comment":"The old screen's byte"},
        "5094": {"comment":"Load its variables back (LOAD_SCREEN_VARS)"},
        "5097": {"comment":"Carry: from the screen's page to $55D8"},
        "5098": {"comment":"Hides AND A at $D3EB (no carry: to the screen)"},
        "5100": {"comment":"The current screen's byte"},
        "5103": {"comment":"Copy its 40 bytes (SWAP_SCREEN_40)"},
        "5106": {"synopsis":"Looks for a screen in SCLIST whose page (bits 4-0) is L. No jump or call to it was found in\neither ROM page.\nEntry: L = the page.\nExit: Z when found, DE past its slot.\nChanges: AF, B, DE.","comment":"16 slots"},
        "5108": {"comment":"SCLIST"},
        "5111": {"synopsis":"Compares one slot's page with L.","comment":"The next slot"},
        "5113": {"comment":"Its page"},
        "5115": {"comment":"Page L?"},
        "5116": {"comment":"Yes: Z"},
        "5117": {"comment":"All 16"},
        "5120": {"synopsis":"Takes a page count 1-30 off the calculator stack (GET_BYTE_1_D, error 30) and finds the\nfirst ALLOCT entry after page 0 that is not $40.\nEntry: the count on the calculator stack.\nExit: B = C = the count; HL = the entry; D = its page.\nError: stops with error code 30 for a count not 1-30.","comment":"1-30, else error 30"},
        "5123": {"comment":"C = n (GET_BYTE_1_D)"},
        "5126": {"comment":"B = n"},
        "5127": {"comment":"ALLOCT"},
        "5130": {"synopsis":"Skips the entries marked $40.","comment":"The next page"},
        "5131": {"comment":"Its entry"},
        "5132": {"comment":"Marked $40?"},
        "5134": {"comment":"Yes: on"},
        "5136": {"comment":"D = the page"},
        "5138": {"synopsis":"Tells whether a stream's channel is one of the ROM's, from its letter at CHANS + DE + 3.\nEntry: DE = the stream's displacement (as STREAM_ENTRY gives it).\nExit: Z and no carry for K, S or P; Z and carry for $ or B; NZ for any other (a DOS\nchannel).\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"CHANS"},
        "5141": {"comment":"Plus the displacement"},
        "5142": {"comment":"To the channel's letter"},
        "5145": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "5146": {"comment":"K?"},
        "5149": {"comment":"S?"},
        "5152": {"comment":"P?"},
        "5155": {"comment":"$?"},
        "5157": {"comment":"Carry for $"},
        "5159": {"comment":"B?"},
        "5161": {"comment":"Carry for B"},
        "5163": {"comment":"A DOS channel: NZ, no carry"},
        "5165": {"synopsis":"The interrupt handler's ROM1 part, called by ROM0's INT_DEFAULT on a stack at $4C00. Keeps\nthe status in LASTSTAT, then serves the first of its bits that is low: bit 0 the line\ninterrupt (INT_LINE), bit 1 COMSV, bit 2 MIPV (with port $FD read), bit 3 the frame\n(INT_FRAME), else MOPV. A vector is called only when its high byte is not 0.\nEntry: C = the status port (bits low for the active interrupts); B = the interrupted LMPR.\nExit: HL = the interrupted SP (SPSTORE); A = the interrupted LMPR (INT_RETURN).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, and what the vectors change.\nKeeps: DE.","comment":"The status"},
        "5166": {"comment":"LASTSTAT"},
        "5169": {"comment":"Kept: B becomes A at the end"},
        "5171": {"comment":"Bit 0 low: the line interrupt?"},
        "5175": {"comment":"Bit 1 low?"},
        "5178": {"comment":"Bit 2 low?"},
        "5181": {"comment":"Bit 3 low: the frame interrupt?"},
        "5184": {"comment":"Else MOPV"},
        "5189": {"synopsis":"Status bit 1: the vector COMSV.","comment":"COMSV"},
        "5194": {"synopsis":"Status bit 2: the vector MIPV, with A = port $FD (MIDI in).","comment":"MIPV"},
        "5197": {"comment":"A = port $FD (MIDI in)"},
        "5199": {"synopsis":"Calls the vector in HL if its high byte is not 0, then returns.","comment":"A vector set (high byte not 0)?"},
        "5201": {"comment":"Yes: call it (CALL_HL)"},
        "5204": {"comment":"Return"},
        "5207": {"synopsis":"The frame interrupt: calls FRAMIV (when not 0), starts the line interrupt table at $5600\n(LINIPTR, first line to the line register), sends one of the two 16-byte palettes to the\nCLUT, and every $5A08 frames (SPEEDIC counts) switches the palette and swaps the two colours\nof every line table entry. Then FRAMES, the screen-off count, and the mouse and keyboard.","comment":"FRAMIV"},
        "5210": {"comment":"Set?"},
        "5212": {"comment":"Yes: call it (CALL_HL)"},
        "5215": {"comment":"The line interrupt table"},
        "5218": {"comment":"LINIPTR at its start"},
        "5221": {"comment":"Its first line"},
        "5222": {"comment":"To the line interrupt register (port $F9)"},
        "5224": {"comment":"PALFLAG"},
        "5227": {"comment":"The first palette's end"},
        "5230": {"comment":"Bit 0 set?"},
        "5233": {"comment":"Then the second palette's end, $55FB"},
        "5235": {"synopsis":"OTDR: 16 bytes to port $F8 (the CLUT) from $55E7 down, or from $55FB down when PALFLAG bit 0\nis set.","comment":"16 bytes to port $F8"},
        "5238": {"comment":"The palette to the CLUT"},
        "5240": {"comment":"SPEEDIC"},
        "5243": {"comment":"Count down: time to flash?"},
        "5246": {"comment":"PALFLAG"},
        "5247": {"comment":"Plus 1: the other palette"},
        "5248": {"comment":"The count again, from $5A08"},
        "5252": {"comment":"SPEEDIC reloaded"},
        "5253": {"comment":"The line table"},
        "5256": {"comment":"Swap its colours"},
        "5258": {"synopsis":"Swaps bytes 2 and 3 of a line table entry (the two colours).","comment":"To the entry's colours"},
        "5260": {"comment":"The first colour"},
        "5261": {"comment":"The second"},
        "5263": {"comment":"Swapped"},
        "5266": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "5268": {"synopsis":"The next entry: $FF ends the table.","comment":"Its line"},
        "5269": {"comment":"$FF: the end?"},
        "5272": {"synopsis":"FRAMES + 1; every 256 frames SOFFCT counts down, and at 0 (unless SOFE is set) the screen is\nturned off: port $FE bit 7 (SOFF) and SOFLG = $80.","comment":"FRAMES"},
        "5275": {"comment":"Plus 1: carry?"},
        "5278": {"comment":"SOFFCT"},
        "5281": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "5285": {"comment":"Not 0 yet"},
        "5287": {"comment":"SOFE"},
        "5290": {"comment":"Screen-off disabled?"},
        "5293": {"comment":"Bit 7: the screen off"},
        "5295": {"comment":"Port $FE"},
        "5297": {"comment":"SOFLG = $80: it is off"},
        "5300": {"synopsis":"Carries into FRAMES' other bytes and FRAMES34.","comment":"FRAMES' next byte"},
        "5301": {"comment":"Plus 1: carry?"},
        "5304": {"comment":"The third byte"},
        "5308": {"comment":"FRAMES34"},
        "5311": {"comment":"Plus 1"},
        "5315": {"synopsis":"The mouse: with MOUSV's high byte 0 the ROM reads 8 bytes from port $FFFE into MSEDP (the\nmouse); otherwise MOUSV is called (a run: MOUSV = 0 after boot).","comment":"MOUSV"},
        "5318": {"comment":"High byte 0?"},
        "5321": {"comment":"No: call MOUSV"},
        "5323": {"comment":"A = $FF: port $FFFE, the mouse"},
        "5325": {"comment":"MSEDP"},
        "5328": {"comment":"8 bytes"},
        "5330": {"synopsis":"Reads one mouse byte (port $FFFE).","comment":"Port $FFFE"},
        "5332": {"comment":"One mouse byte"},
        "5334": {"comment":"To MSEDP"},
        "5336": {"comment":"Eight times"},
        "5338": {"synopsis":"Calls MOUSV when NZ, then scans the keyboard (KEY_SCAN_QUEUE).","comment":"MOUSV (when set)"},
        "5341": {"comment":"The keyboard (KEY_SCAN_QUEUE)"},
        "5344": {"comment":"Return"},
        "5346": {"synopsis":"The line interrupt: for each entry of the line table at LINIPTR that is due, waits (when\nSPEN, port $FE bit 5, is low) while HPEN still reads the entry's line, then writes the\nentry's colour to its CLUT entry. Entries on the same line follow at once; the next line's\nentry is waited for; otherwise LINIPTR and the line register are set for the next one. An\nentry is 4 bytes: line, CLUT entry, colour, the other colour (the flash swaps them); $FF\nends the table.","comment":"LINIPTR"},
        "5349": {"synopsis":"D = this entry's line.","comment":"D = the entry's line"},
        "5350": {"comment":"C = port $F8; B = 1 for HPEN"},
        "5353": {"comment":"SPEN (port $FE bit 5)"},
        "5355": {"comment":"High?"},
        "5357": {"comment":"Yes: no waiting"},
        "5359": {"synopsis":"Waits while HPEN (port $01F8) still reads this line.","comment":"HPEN, the beam's line"},
        "5361": {"comment":"Still this line?"},
        "5362": {"comment":"Wait"},
        "5364": {"synopsis":"Writes the colour to CLUT entry B (port $F8 with B high); then the next entry.","comment":"To the CLUT entry number"},
        "5365": {"comment":"B = the entry"},
        "5366": {"comment":"To the colour"},
        "5367": {"comment":"The colour"},
        "5368": {"comment":"To the CLUT"},
        "5370": {"comment":"Past the other colour"},
        "5372": {"comment":"The next entry's line"},
        "5373": {"comment":"The same line?"},
        "5374": {"comment":"Yes: its colour at once"},
        "5376": {"comment":"The next line?"},
        "5378": {"comment":"Yes: wait for it"},
        "5380": {"comment":"A = its line ($FF at the end)"},
        "5381": {"comment":"LINIPTR"},
        "5384": {"comment":"Line interrupt register"},
        "5386": {"synopsis":"The handler's exit: HL = SPSTORE; DE and AF (A = the interrupted LMPR) popped.","comment":"SPSTORE: the interrupted SP"},
        "5389": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "5390": {"comment":"A = the interrupted LMPR"},
        "5392": {"synopsis":"Scans the keyboard (KEY_SCAN_REPEAT), then moves the next key from the queue to RBHEAD when\nthere is one and FLAGS bit 5 is clear, setting that bit (a new key). The queue is KBQB, 8\nbytes, with KBQP's low byte the write index and its high byte the read index. ROM0's\nKEY_POLL calls it through RST $30; the frame interrupt calls it too.\nExit: RBHEAD and FLAGS bit 5 as above.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Scan the keyboard"},
        "5395": {"comment":"KBQP"},
        "5398": {"comment":"Read index = write index?"},
        "5400": {"comment":"Yes: the queue is empty"},
        "5401": {"comment":"FLAGS"},
        "5404": {"comment":"A key waiting already?"},
        "5406": {"comment":"Yes: leave it"},
        "5407": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 5: a new key"},
        "5409": {"comment":"HL = the read index"},
        "5412": {"comment":"The next read index"},
        "5415": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5418": {"comment":"KBQB"},
        "5421": {"comment":"The key's place"},
        "5422": {"comment":"The key"},
        "5423": {"comment":"RBHEAD"},
        "5427": {"synopsis":"Scans the matrix (KEY_MATRIX_SCAN) and handles a new key and the repeat: a key not among the\nlast two key numbers seen ($5C56-$5C57; key $41 is compared with the third, $5C58, too) is\nqueued at once and REPCT set to REPDEL; a held key counts REPCT down and, while it is still\ndown and no key waits (FLAGS bit 5), is queued again every REPSPD frames. The key numbers\nseen move along $5C56-$5C58, 0 for no key.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Scan the matrix"},
        "5430": {"comment":"0: no key"},
        "5432": {"comment":"None"},
        "5434": {"comment":"The last key numbers seen"},
        "5437": {"comment":"E = the key number"},
        "5438": {"comment":"The last one?"},
        "5441": {"comment":"The one before?"},
        "5445": {"comment":"Key $41?"},
        "5449": {"comment":"Then also the third"},
        "5451": {"synopsis":"C = the key's code (KEY_CODE_LOOKUP); NZ: a new key.","comment":"Keep the answer"},
        "5452": {"comment":"The key's code"},
        "5455": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "5456": {"comment":"REPCT"},
        "5459": {"comment":"Z: a held key"},
        "5460": {"comment":"A new key"},
        "5462": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "5463": {"comment":"Not yet"},
        "5464": {"comment":"REPCT's address"},
        "5465": {"comment":"The previous scan's rows, less 1"},
        "5468": {"comment":"LKPB: H = the row, L = the bit's shift"},
        "5471": {"comment":"The row"},
        "5472": {"comment":"Its place in the previous scan"},
        "5474": {"comment":"The row byte"},
        "5475": {"synopsis":"Rotates the row byte to the key's bit (LKPB): carry when it is up.","comment":"Rotate to the key's bit"},
        "5476": {"comment":"Count the rotations"},
        "5479": {"comment":"REPCT's address back"},
        "5480": {"comment":"Up: no repeat"},
        "5481": {"comment":"REPCT 1: try again next frame"},
        "5482": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 5: a key waiting?"},
        "5487": {"comment":"Yes: later"},
        "5488": {"comment":"REPSPD for the repeats after"},
        "5491": {"comment":"Then queue the key"},
        "5493": {"synopsis":"A new key: REPCT = REPDEL.","comment":"REPDEL for the first repeat"},
        "5496": {"synopsis":"Sets REPCT, then puts C in the queue unless it is full.","comment":"REPCT"},
        "5497": {"comment":"KBQP"},
        "5500": {"comment":"The write index"},
        "5501": {"comment":"Plus 1, MOD 8"},
        "5504": {"comment":"Full: the read index?"},
        "5505": {"comment":"Yes: the key is lost"},
        "5506": {"comment":"The new write index"},
        "5509": {"comment":"HL = the old one"},
        "5511": {"comment":"KBQB"},
        "5515": {"comment":"The key's code queued"},
        "5516": {"comment":"LASTKV: the key number"},
        "5519": {"synopsis":"Moves the key numbers along $5C56-$5C58: A goes in at $5C56.","comment":"$5C56: the last key numbers"},
        "5522": {"comment":"C = the last"},
        "5523": {"comment":"The new one in"},
        "5524": {"comment":"The one before"},
        "5525": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "5526": {"comment":"The last moves down"},
        "5527": {"comment":"The third"},
        "5528": {"comment":"The one before moves down"},
        "5530": {"synopsis":"Gets the key's code from the keyboard table RHTAB: 70 bytes for each shift state, so RHTAB +\n70 x D + E. With KLFLAG bit 3 set a letter is made a capital. ROM0's READ_KEY_GOT calls it\nthrough RST $30.\nEntry: E = the key number; D = the shift state (LASTKV, as KEY_MATRIX_SCAN leaves DE).\nExit: A = the code.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"RHTAB, the keyboard table"},
        "5533": {"comment":"A = the shift state"},
        "5534": {"comment":"DE = the key number"},
        "5536": {"comment":"Its place in the first set"},
        "5537": {"comment":"Shift state 0?"},
        "5540": {"comment":"70 bytes a set"},
        "5542": {"synopsis":"70 bytes on per shift state.","comment":"The next set"},
        "5543": {"comment":"For each shift state"},
        "5546": {"synopsis":"KLFLAG bit 3: capitals?","comment":"KLFLAG bit 3: capitals"},
        "5551": {"comment":"The code"},
        "5552": {"comment":"Not set: done"},
        "5553": {"comment":"A letter? (IS_LETTER)"},
        "5556": {"comment":"No: as it is"},
        "5557": {"comment":"A capital"},
        "5560": {"synopsis":"Scans the matrix (KEY_MATRIX_SCAN) and, when it finds no key, scans it again (falls into\nKEY_MATRIX_SCAN). ROM0's READ_KEY_FLUSH calls it through RST $30.\nExit: Z when a key is down, DE = LASTKV.","comment":"Scan"},
        "5563": {"comment":"A key: done"},
        "5564": {"synopsis":"Reads the 9 keyboard rows into RBUFF ($5BEE): port $FE gives bits 4-0 and the status port\n$F9 bits 7-5 of rows $FE-$7F, then row $FF (bits 4-1 only). Four keys never count as new\npresses: row $FE bit 0, row $7F bit 1 and row $FF bit 0 (the shift-state keys) and row $F7\nbit 5. Each row is compared with the last scan kept at $5BF7: a bit newly low marks a new\npress. A new key's number (row and bit, also in LKPB) goes to LASTKV's low byte and resets\nSOFFCT, turning the screen back on if SOFLG says it is off; with no new key the last one\nstays while any key is down. The shift state (0-3, read from the ports) goes to LASTKV's\nhigh byte.\nExit: Z with DE = LASTKV when a key is down; NZ (B = 1) when none is.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"RBUFF"},
        "5565": {"comment":"Keep it"},
        "5568": {"comment":"Row $FE first (port $FEFE)"},
        "5571": {"comment":"Bits 7-5 from port $F9"},
        "5573": {"synopsis":"Reads row B: bits 4-0 from port $FE, bits 7-5 from port $F9.","comment":"Bits 4-0 of the row (port $FE)"},
        "5575": {"comment":"A = the row (high address byte)"},
        "5576": {"comment":"The status port's bits"},
        "5577": {"comment":"Bits 7-5 from it, 4-0 from port $FE"},
        "5581": {"comment":"The last row ($FF)?"},
        "5583": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "5584": {"comment":"Store the row"},
        "5585": {"comment":"B back"},
        "5586": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "5587": {"comment":"The next row: $FD, $FB, ... $7F"},
        "5589": {"comment":"More"},
        "5591": {"comment":"Then row $FF"},
        "5595": {"synopsis":"The last row ($FF): bits 4-1 kept.","comment":"Only bits 4-1 count"},
        "5597": {"comment":"Store it"},
        "5598": {"comment":"HL = RBUFF"},
        "5599": {"comment":"DE = RBUFF too"},
        "5601": {"comment":"Row $FE bit 0 left out"},
        "5606": {"comment":"Row $F7 bit 5 left out"},
        "5612": {"comment":"Row $7F bit 1 left out"},
        "5614": {"comment":"HL = the previous scan at $5BF7"},
        "5616": {"comment":"Nine rows"},
        "5618": {"synopsis":"For each row: the new bits replace the old copy; a bit newly low stays low in RBUFF.","comment":"The new row"},
        "5619": {"comment":"C = the previous"},
        "5620": {"comment":"The new one kept for next time"},
        "5621": {"comment":"The changed bits"},
        "5622": {"comment":"Low for a change"},
        "5623": {"comment":"Low only for a key newly down"},
        "5624": {"comment":"In RBUFF"},
        "5625": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "5627": {"comment":"Nine rows"},
        "5629": {"comment":"Nine rows, from the last"},
        "5631": {"synopsis":"Looks for a row with a new press, from the last row back.","comment":"Back one row"},
        "5632": {"comment":"Its new presses"},
        "5633": {"comment":"Any?"},
        "5634": {"comment":"Yes: the key's number"},
        "5636": {"comment":"For every row"},
        "5638": {"comment":"Nine rows"},
        "5640": {"comment":"LASTKV: the last key"},
        "5644": {"synopsis":"No new press: is any key still down (the copy at $5BF7)?","comment":"Back one row"},
        "5645": {"comment":"The row now"},
        "5646": {"comment":"Any key down?"},
        "5647": {"comment":"Yes: keep the last key"},
        "5649": {"comment":"For every row"},
        "5651": {"comment":"No key: NZ"},
        "5653": {"synopsis":"C = the bit's position (9 less one per shift), then the key number 9C - B.","comment":"The row's bits"},
        "5654": {"comment":"C = 9"},
        "5656": {"synopsis":"Counts the rotations until a low bit falls out.","comment":"One less a bit"},
        "5657": {"comment":"The next bit out"},
        "5658": {"comment":"Up: go on"},
        "5660": {"comment":"LKPB = the row (B) and C"},
        "5664": {"comment":"The key number = 9C - B"},
        "5670": {"comment":"E = the key number"},
        "5671": {"comment":"SOFFCT"},
        "5674": {"comment":"0"},
        "5675": {"comment":"SOFFCT reset"},
        "5676": {"comment":"SOFLG"},
        "5677": {"comment":"The screen off?"},
        "5678": {"comment":"No"},
        "5680": {"comment":"SOFLG 0: back on"},
        "5682": {"comment":"BORDCOL"},
        "5685": {"comment":"Bit 7 (SOFF) off"},
        "5687": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5690": {"comment":"The screen on (port $FE)"},
        "5692": {"synopsis":"The shift state into D: 1 for row $FE bit 0, 3 for row $FF bit 0, 2 for row $7F bit 1, else\n0.","comment":"Row $FE (port $FEFE)"},
        "5697": {"comment":"Bit 0"},
        "5699": {"comment":"Down?"},
        "5700": {"comment":"Yes: D = 1"},
        "5702": {"comment":"Row $FF (port $FFFE)"},
        "5705": {"comment":"Bit 0"},
        "5706": {"comment":"D = 3"},
        "5708": {"comment":"Down?"},
        "5710": {"comment":"D = 2"},
        "5711": {"comment":"Row $7F (port $7FFE)"},
        "5715": {"comment":"Bit 1 down?"},
        "5716": {"comment":"Yes: D = 2"},
        "5718": {"comment":"D = 0: no shift"},
        "5720": {"synopsis":"LASTKV = DE (E the key number, D the shift state).","comment":"LASTKV = DE"},
        "5725": {"synopsis":"GO SUB's command address (CMDADDRT, token $B5). HL = GOSUB_RUN, and the LD IX that follows\nhides GO TO's own entry at $D661 (token $B4), LD HL,GOTO_CALC_LINE: both then evaluate the\nline number (EXPECT_NUM) and end their syntax check, and jump to HL. GO TO ON n; a, b, ...\n(or GO SUB ON) evaluates the numbers up to the n-th and leaves that one for HL (GOTO_ON); a\nrun of GO TO ON 2; 100,200 went to line 200.\nEntry: A = the character after the keyword.\nError: 29 for a bad syntax.","comment":"GO SUB: its running part"},
        "5728": {"comment":"Hides LD HL,GOTO_CALC_LINE at $D661 (GO TO)"},
        "5732": {"comment":"The running part, for the RET"},
        "5733": {"comment":"ON?"},
        "5735": {"comment":"Yes: GO TO ON / GO SUB ON"},
        "5737": {"comment":"The line number (EXPECT_NUM)"},
        "5740": {"comment":"HL = the running part"},
        "5741": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done (SYNTAX_STOP)"},
        "5744": {"comment":"Run it"},
        "5745": {"synopsis":"GO TO ON / GO SUB ON: the selector, then \";\" (error 29 otherwise).","comment":"The selector (NEXT_NUM)"},
        "5748": {"comment":"Keep the flags (carry: running)"},
        "5749": {"comment":"\";\"?"},
        "5751": {"comment":"No: stops with error code 29 (STOP_ERR29)"},
        "5754": {"comment":"Carry: running"},
        "5755": {"comment":"Running"},
        "5757": {"comment":"Drop the running part"},
        "5758": {"synopsis":"Checking syntax: every number after the \";\", separated by commas.","comment":"The next number (NEXT_NUM)"},
        "5761": {"comment":"\",\"?"},
        "5763": {"comment":"Yes: another"},
        "5765": {"comment":"Syntax checked"},
        "5766": {"synopsis":"Running: C = the selector, 255 when it is over 255.","comment":"The selector (CALC_POP_BYTE)"},
        "5769": {"comment":"$FF when over 255"},
        "5770": {"comment":"Not over"},
        "5772": {"comment":"C = 255"},
        "5773": {"synopsis":"Evaluates the next number; the C-th stays on the calculator stack and the RET runs HL.\nOthers are dropped; when the list ends first, nothing happens.","comment":"Keep the count"},
        "5774": {"comment":"The next number (NEXT_NUM)"},
        "5777": {"comment":"The count"},
        "5778": {"comment":"This one?"},
        "5779": {"comment":"Yes: run HL with it stacked"},
        "5780": {"comment":"No: drop it (STK_DROP)"},
        "5783": {"comment":"The current character"},
        "5784": {"comment":"\",\"?"},
        "5786": {"comment":"Yes: another"},
        "5788": {"comment":"None chosen: drop HL"},
        "5790": {"synopsis":"GO SUB's running part: the line number (0-65279, error 30), a GO SUB entry ($00) on the\nBASIC stack (BSTK_PUSH), then jumps to the line (SET_NEWPPC_0).\nEntry: the line number on the calculator stack.\nError: 30 for a line out of range; 41 when the BASIC stack is full.","comment":"The line number (GET_UINT16)"},
        "5793": {"comment":"$FFxx?"},
        "5795": {"comment":"Stops with error code 30 (ERR_OUT_RANGE)"},
        "5798": {"comment":"Type $00: GO SUB"},
        "5800": {"comment":"Keep the line"},
        "5801": {"comment":"Push the entry (BSTK_PUSH)"},
        "5805": {"comment":"Go to the line (SET_NEWPPC_0)"},
        "5808": {"synopsis":"The jump table entry ROM0's JT_018A (at $018A) reaches through RST $30: looks up the word at\nDE in a list of bit-7 ended keywords, letters in either case. A space in a keyword may be\nleft out in the text. A match whose last character is a letter-like code ($3F and up) must\nnot be followed by a letter, \"$\" or \"_\" (IS_NAME_START). ROM1 $C58A uses it on the keyword\nlist from $F8C7 with A = $C5.\nEntry: HL = 2 bytes before the first entry (HL + 1 ends an entry); A = the count of entries\n+ 1; DE = the text.\nExit: NZ when found, A = the entry's number (1 for the first), HL = the text, DE past the\nkeyword; Z when not found.\nChanges: AF, AF', BC, DE, HL.","comment":"C = the entries left"},
        "5809": {"comment":"A' = the count"},
        "5810": {"synopsis":"Steps to the end of the current entry (bit 7 set).","comment":"The next byte"},
        "5811": {"synopsis":"Is this byte the last of the entry?","comment":"The end of an entry?"},
        "5813": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "5815": {"comment":"One entry fewer"},
        "5816": {"comment":"None left: Z, not found"},
        "5817": {"comment":"The entry's first byte"},
        "5818": {"comment":"The text's first character"},
        "5819": {"comment":"Same?"},
        "5820": {"comment":"Either case"},
        "5822": {"comment":"No: skip this entry"},
        "5824": {"comment":"Keep the text's start"},
        "5825": {"comment":"Past its first character"},
        "5826": {"synopsis":"Compares the next characters of the keyword and the text.","comment":"The keyword's next byte"},
        "5828": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "5830": {"comment":"The text's next character"},
        "5832": {"comment":"No space in the keyword"},
        "5834": {"comment":"The text has the space too?"},
        "5835": {"comment":"Yes: on"},
        "5837": {"comment":"No: skip the keyword's space"},
        "5838": {"synopsis":"Same letter, either case?","comment":"Same?"},
        "5839": {"comment":"Either case"},
        "5841": {"comment":"Yes: on"},
        "5843": {"comment":"Only bit 7 differs?"},
        "5845": {"comment":"No: not this entry"},
        "5847": {"comment":"The keyword's last byte?"},
        "5848": {"comment":"Bit 7 to carry"},
        "5849": {"comment":"Yes: the end"},
        "5851": {"synopsis":"No match: back to the text's start, on to the next entry.","comment":"The text's start"},
        "5852": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "5854": {"synopsis":"The keyword's last character matched: may the text go on?","comment":"A letter-like last character?"},
        "5856": {"comment":"Carry: it is"},
        "5857": {"comment":"The text's next character"},
        "5858": {"comment":"Then it may not be a name character"},
        "5861": {"comment":"It is: no match"},
        "5863": {"comment":"HL = the text's start"},
        "5864": {"comment":"A = the count"},
        "5865": {"comment":"Less those left: the entry's number"},
        "5867": {"synopsis":"JMODE's body (ROM0's jump table entry at $015B jumps here through RST $30): sets screen mode\nA (0-3 for modes 1-4). MODE takes it, modes 3 and 4 run ROM1 $D81A, and CUSCRNP's bits 6-5\nthe mode (VMPR too when the current screen is the displayed one). The character size (8 x 8\nin mode 1, 8 x 9 otherwise) and the windows are set (CHAR_WINDOWS_SET). Going into or out of\nmode 3 swaps M23PAPP and M23LSC with M3PAPP and M3LSC (on the way in ROM1 $F180 converts the\ntwo colours, then ROM1 $F17B runs) and, with THFATP 0, doubles or halves XCOORD and the\nnumber at NVARS + $57 (XCOORD_SCALE). Ends by clearing the screen (ROM0's CLS_ALL).\nEntry: A = the mode, 0-3.\nExit: through CLS_ALL.","comment":"Modes 1-4 as 0-3"},
        "5869": {"comment":"MODE"},
        "5872": {"comment":"C = the old mode"},
        "5873": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5874": {"comment":"The new mode"},
        "5875": {"comment":"Mode 3 or 4?"},
        "5877": {"comment":"Keep the flags"},
        "5878": {"comment":"Yes: ROM1 $D81A"},
        "5883": {"comment":"The mode to bits 6-5"},
        "5886": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "5887": {"comment":"CUSCRNP"},
        "5890": {"comment":"Its mode bits replaced"},
        "5895": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5896": {"comment":"VMPR: the screen shown"},
        "5898": {"comment":"The current one?"},
        "5901": {"comment":"No"},
        "5903": {"comment":"VMPR: the new mode shows"},
        "5906": {"synopsis":"Character height 8 in mode 1, 9 otherwise; width 8.","comment":"A = the mode, flags of CP 2"},
        "5907": {"comment":"C = the old mode"},
        "5908": {"comment":"Keep A"},
        "5909": {"comment":"Mode 1?"},
        "5911": {"comment":"$FF for mode 1, else 0"},
        "5912": {"comment":"Width 8, height 9"},
        "5915": {"comment":"Height 8 in mode 1"},
        "5917": {"comment":"Z for mode 3"},
        "5918": {"comment":"Size and windows (CHAR_WINDOWS_SET)"},
        "5921": {"comment":"TEMPB1: the old mode"},
        "5924": {"comment":"The new mode 3?"},
        "5926": {"comment":"The old mode 3?"},
        "5928": {"comment":"No: clear the screen"},
        "5930": {"comment":"M3PAPP back to M23PAPP"},
        "5936": {"comment":"M3LSC back to M23LSC"},
        "5942": {"comment":"C = 2: halve"},
        "5943": {"comment":"The x coordinates"},
        "5945": {"synopsis":"The new mode is 3 (MODE 3 is A = 2): nothing to do when the old was too.","comment":"The old mode 3 too?"},
        "5947": {"comment":"Yes: clear the screen"},
        "5949": {"comment":"M23PAPP kept in M3PAPP"},
        "5955": {"comment":"Convert the paper colour (ROM1 $F180)"},
        "5958": {"comment":"Keep it"},
        "5959": {"comment":"The ink"},
        "5960": {"comment":"Convert it"},
        "5963": {"comment":"H = the ink"},
        "5964": {"comment":"L = the paper"},
        "5966": {"comment":"M23PAPP set"},
        "5969": {"comment":"M23LSC kept in M3LSC"},
        "5975": {"comment":"ROM1 $F17B"},
        "5978": {"comment":"C = 0: double"},
        "5980": {"synopsis":"With THFATP 0, XCOORD_SCALE (A = 0 doubles, otherwise halves); then ROM1 $EDBB.","comment":"THFATP"},
        "5983": {"comment":"0?"},
        "5984": {"comment":"A = C"},
        "5985": {"comment":"Then scale the x coordinates"},
        "5988": {"comment":"ROM1 $EDBB"},
        "5991": {"synopsis":"Clears the screen: ROM0's CLS_ALL, with ROM1 paged out.","comment":"Clear the screen: ROM0's CLS_ALL"},
        "5996": {"synopsis":"Sets the character size and the windows: CSIZEH = L, CSIZEW = H, TEMPB1 = C. The rows are\n192 / CSIZEH; ORGOFF = 2 x CSIZEH and LSOFF = the rest of the division. The upper window\ncovers columns 0 to 31 (63 in mode 3, or 84 with 6-pixel characters when FL60R8 is 0, CSIZEW\nthen 6) and rows 0 to rows - 3; the lower window the next two rows; WINDMAX = the right\ncolumn and the upper window's bottom row.\nEntry: H = the width; L = the height; C = for TEMPB1; Z for mode 3.\nExit: AF kept.\nChanges: DE, HL.","comment":"Keep AF (Z for mode 3)"},
        "5997": {"comment":"TEMPB1 = C"},
        "6001": {"comment":"CSIZEH = L, CSIZEW = H"},
        "6004": {"comment":"192 lines"},
        "6006": {"comment":"E counts the rows, from -4"},
        "6008": {"synopsis":"Counts the rows: E = 192 / L - 3 when done.","comment":"One more row"},
        "6009": {"comment":"One row's height"},
        "6010": {"comment":"Room for it?"},
        "6012": {"comment":"A = the lines left over"},
        "6013": {"comment":"LSOFF"},
        "6016": {"comment":"Twice the height"},
        "6018": {"comment":"ORGOFF"},
        "6021": {"comment":"Right column 31"},
        "6023": {"comment":"Z: mode 3?"},
        "6025": {"comment":"No"},
        "6027": {"comment":"Right column 63"},
        "6029": {"comment":"FL60R8"},
        "6032": {"comment":"Not 0: 64 columns"},
        "6035": {"comment":"Right column 84"},
        "6037": {"comment":"6 pixels wide"},
        "6039": {"comment":"CSIZEW"},
        "6042": {"synopsis":"UWRHS, UWLHS, UWTOP, UWBOT, LWRHS, LWLHS, LWTOP, LWBOT and WINDMAX.","comment":"UWRHS"},
        "6046": {"comment":"UWLHS = 0"},
        "6049": {"comment":"UWTOP = 0"},
        "6051": {"comment":"UWBOT = the rows - 3"},
        "6053": {"comment":"LWRHS"},
        "6055": {"comment":"WINDMAX = the right column and bottom row"},
        "6059": {"comment":"LWLHS = 0"},
        "6062": {"comment":"LWTOP = UWBOT + 1"},
        "6065": {"comment":"LWBOT = UWBOT + 2"},
        "6067": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "6069": {"synopsis":"FATPIX's command address (CMDADDRT, token $A7): FATPIX 0 or 1 sets THFATP. In mode 3 a\nchange halves (1) or doubles (0) the x coordinates (XCOORD_SCALE).\nEntry: the BASIC pointer after FATPIX.\nError: 30 for a number not 0-1.","comment":"The number (SYN_NUM)"},
        "6072": {"comment":"0-1, else error 30"},
        "6075": {"comment":"A = it (ROM0's $1F62)"},
        "6078": {"comment":"THFATP"},
        "6081": {"comment":"No change?"},
        "6083": {"comment":"Set"},
        "6084": {"comment":"MODE"},
        "6087": {"comment":"Mode 3?"},
        "6089": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "6090": {"comment":"A = THFATP"},
        "6091": {"synopsis":"Halves (A not 0) or doubles (A = 0) XCOORD, and the 5-byte number at NVARS + $57 by ROM0's\nHALVE_OR_DOUBLE (with ROM1 paged out).\nEntry: A selects.","comment":"XCOORD"},
        "6094": {"comment":"A = 0?"},
        "6095": {"comment":"Yes: double it"},
        "6097": {"comment":"Halve it"},
        "6101": {"comment":"Hides ADD HL,HL at $D7D6: double"},
        "6103": {"comment":"XCOORD set"},
        "6106": {"comment":"Keep A"},
        "6107": {"comment":"NVARS (NVARS_PTR)"},
        "6110": {"comment":"A: the choice"},
        "6111": {"comment":"NVARS + $57"},
        "6114": {"comment":"HL = the number there"},
        "6115": {"comment":"Halve or double it: ROM0's HALVE_OR_DOUBLE"},
        "6120": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 30: a CSIZE value out of range.","comment":"Stops with error code 30"},
        "6122": {"synopsis":"CSIZE's command address (CMDADDRT, token $A8): CSIZE w,h with w 6 or 8 and h 6-32. FL60R8 =\nw - 6 (0 gives mode 3 its 85 columns), then the character size and windows\n(CHAR_WINDOWS_SET); in mode 3 it goes on at ROM1 $D81A.\nEntry: the BASIC pointer after CSIZE.\nError: stops with error code 30 for a size out of range.","comment":"Width and height (SYN_2NUM)"},
        "6125": {"comment":"The height"},
        "6128": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6129": {"comment":"The width"},
        "6132": {"comment":"6?"},
        "6136": {"comment":"8?"},
        "6138": {"comment":"Neither: error 30"},
        "6140": {"synopsis":"The height must be 6-32.","comment":"E = the height"},
        "6141": {"comment":"D = the width"},
        "6142": {"comment":"The height"},
        "6143": {"comment":"Below 6?"},
        "6145": {"comment":"Height below 6? Error"},
        "6147": {"comment":"Height 33 or more? Error"},
        "6151": {"comment":"H = the width, L = the height"},
        "6152": {"comment":"FL60R8 = width - 6: 0 or 2"},
        "6158": {"comment":"C = MODE"},
        "6162": {"comment":"Z: MODE 3 (MODE byte 2)"},
        "6165": {"comment":"Remakes the window limits (ROM1 $D76C)"},
        "6169": {"comment":"Not MODE 3: done"},
        "6170": {"synopsis":"Makes EXTAB ($5B20), the table that widens 4 bits of a character pattern to screen bytes:\nwith Z (MODE 3, MODE byte 2) 16 bytes, each bit of the index doubled (2 bits a pixel);\notherwise (MODE 4) 16 words, each bit of the index made 4 bits (4 bits a pixel), high byte\nfirst. ROM1 $D6F6 calls it when the mode changes to 3 or 4; CSIZE in MODE 3 falls into it.\nEntry: Z for MODE 3, NZ for MODE 4.\nExit: EXTAB made.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"EXTAB"},
        "6173": {"comment":"Index 0"},
        "6175": {"comment":"MODE 3: one byte each"},
        "6177": {"synopsis":"MODE 4: the word for index C, high byte first, for C = 0 to 15."},
        "6178": {"comment":"DE = each bit of C made 4"},
        "6181": {"comment":"High byte first"},
        "6186": {"comment":"Index 16? Done"},
        "6192": {"synopsis":"MODE 3: the byte for index C, for C = 0 to 15."},
        "6193": {"comment":"E = each bit of C's low 4 bits doubled"},
        "6199": {"comment":"Index 16? Done"},
        "6205": {"synopsis":"Widens the low 4 bits of A to 16 bits, each bit made 4 bits: bit 0 gives bits 0-3, bit 3\nbits 12-15. Doubles twice through BYTE_BITS_X2. Also makes the block graphics ($DD99).\nEntry: A = the bits.\nExit: DE = the 16 bits.\nChanges: AF, B, DE.","comment":"E = the low 4 bits doubled"},
        "6208": {"comment":"Doubled again: DE"},
        "6209": {"synopsis":"Doubles each bit of A: DE = A's 8 bits, each one twice (bit 0 gives bits 0-1, bit 7 bits\n14-15), so E holds A's low 4 bits doubled.\nEntry: A = the byte.\nExit: DE = the 16 bits; A as it was.\nChanges: F, B, DE.","comment":"8 bits"},
        "6211": {"synopsis":"Shifts the next bit of A into DE twice.","comment":"The bit into carry"},
        "6212": {"comment":"Into DE's top"},
        "6216": {"comment":"A back"},
        "6217": {"comment":"The same bit again"},
        "6218": {"comment":"Into DE's top again"},
        "6225": {"synopsis":"AUTO's body (token $ED in the command table at ROM1 $FD65): AUTO [start [,step]]. With no\nnumber the start is EPPC + 10 and the step 10; the step is 10 unless given. When running,\nAUTOFLG = 1 if the start is at least the step (otherwise 0 and nothing more), EPPC = start -\nstep, AUTOSTEP = step, and the main loop is entered again at ROM0's MAIN_FROM_SDTOP (the two\nreturn addresses dropped).\nEntry: A = the current character.\nExit: returns when checking syntax, or with AUTOFLG 0; otherwise does not return.","comment":"No number?"},
        "6230": {"comment":"HL = BC = the start"},
        "6233": {"comment":"Step 10"},
        "6236": {"comment":"A step too?"},
        "6241": {"comment":"BC = the step"},
        "6247": {"synopsis":"AUTO with no number: the start EPPC + 10, the step 10.","comment":"EPPC"},
        "6250": {"comment":"Plus 10"},
        "6254": {"synopsis":"Sets AUTOFLG, EPPC and AUTOSTEP from the start (HL) and the step (BC) and enters the main\nloop; returns when checking syntax.","comment":"Checking syntax? Done"},
        "6258": {"comment":"Start - step"},
        "6261": {"comment":"A = 1 when start >= step"},
        "6263": {"comment":"AUTOFLG"},
        "6266": {"comment":"Start below the step: AUTO off"},
        "6267": {"comment":"EPPC = start - step"},
        "6270": {"comment":"AUTOSTEP"},
        "6274": {"comment":"Drops two return addresses"},
        "6276": {"comment":"ROM1 out: on at MAIN_FROM_SDTOP"},
        "6282": {"synopsis":"SOUND's body (token $AE in the command table at ROM1 $FD65): SOUND r,v; r,v; ... writes SAA\n1099 registers.\n1. Reads each register (0-31, error 30 otherwise) and value (0-255) into a buffer at $4F00,\n   two bytes a pair, while ';' follows.\n2. Ends the buffer with $FF and sends each pair: the register to port $01FF (the SAA's\n   address), the value to port $00FF (its data).\nWhen checking syntax only the expressions are checked.\nEntry: the BASIC pointer after SOUND.\nError: 30 for a register over 31 or a value over 255.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The pair buffer"},
        "6285": {"synopsis":"Reads one register,value pair; when running, puts it in the buffer at DE."},
        "6286": {"comment":"Register, value"},
        "6290": {"comment":"Checking syntax? Nothing stored"},
        "6293": {"comment":"The value, 0-255"},
        "6297": {"comment":"Register below 32, or error 30"},
        "6305": {"comment":"Buffer: the register"},
        "6308": {"comment":"Then the value"},
        "6310": {"comment":"256 bytes filled (E wrapped)? Jumps to $4F66"},
        "6313": {"synopsis":"Another pair follows a ';'; otherwise the statement ends."},
        "6314": {"comment":"';'?"},
        "6318": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6321": {"synopsis":"Ends the buffer with $FF and writes its pairs to the SAA 1099.","comment":"Checking syntax: returns from the caller"},
        "6324": {"comment":"The end marker"},
        "6327": {"comment":"Port $01FF: the SAA's address"},
        "6330": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "6335": {"synopsis":"Writes one pair: register D to the address port, value E to the data port.","comment":"SAA address: the register"},
        "6337": {"comment":"Port $00FF"},
        "6338": {"comment":"SAA data: the value"},
        "6340": {"comment":"Port $01FF again"},
        "6341": {"synopsis":"Takes the next pair from the buffer; a register byte of $FF ends.","comment":"D = the register"},
        "6343": {"comment":"E = the value"},
        "6345": {"comment":"The $FF end?"},
        "6349": {"synopsis":"BOOT's body (token $E9 in the command table at ROM1 $FD65): BOOT [n].\n1. A number other than 0: loads the boot sector from the disk in drive 1 (BOOT_READ_DISK),\n   which does not return.\n2. BOOT or BOOT 0 with a DOS in memory (DOSFLG not 0): DOS hook 136 (HAUTO).\n3. Otherwise loads the boot sector, then DOS hook 128 (INIT).\nEntry: the BASIC pointer after BOOT.\nExit: returns when checking syntax.","comment":"Optional number (syntax: returns from the caller)"},
        "6352": {"comment":"A = the number"},
        "6355": {"comment":"Not 0: load from the disk"},
        "6358": {"comment":"DOSFLG: a DOS in memory?"},
        "6364": {"comment":"Yes: DOS hook 136 (HAUTO)"},
        "6367": {"synopsis":"No DOS in memory: loads and runs the boot sector, then DOS hook 128 (INIT).","comment":"Load the DOS's boot sector"},
        "6370": {"comment":"DOS hook 128 (INIT)"},
        "6373": {"synopsis":"Loads the boot sector from the disk in drive 1 (the WD1772 at ports $E0-$E3) and runs it.\n1. Finds a page from 31 down whose ALLOCT byte is 0 or $60 (error 1 if none) and pages it in\n   at $8000 (HMPR).\n2. Interrupts the controller ($D0) and seeks track 0 ($09); waits for 6 changes of the index\n   bit (error 55 when they take too long: no disk turning).\n3. Seeks track 4, sector 1, stepping in ($59) or out ($79), and reads the sector ($80) to\n   $8000; on an error retries, seeking track 0 again on the 5th try; error 19 after 10.\n4. The 4 bytes at $8100 must match \"BOOT\" (the keyword at ROM1 $FB94), case and bit 7\n   ignored (error 53 otherwise); then jumps to $8009.\nExit: does not return.\nError: 1, 55, 19 or 53.","comment":"ALLOCT's entry for page 31"},
        "6376": {"synopsis":"Looks down ALLOCT from page 31 for a page whose byte is 0 or $60."},
        "6377": {"comment":"Free?"},
        "6380": {"comment":"Or $60?"},
        "6384": {"comment":"The page below; past page 1?"},
        "6387": {"comment":"No page: stops with error code 1"},
        "6389": {"synopsis":"Pages the page found in at $8000 and starts the controller: Force Interrupt, then track 0.","comment":"The page"},
        "6390": {"comment":"At $8000 (HMPR)"},
        "6393": {"comment":"Force Interrupt command"},
        "6395": {"comment":"Sends it"},
        "6398": {"comment":"Seek track 0 and wait"},
        "6401": {"comment":"The time-out: $FE00 x 256"},
        "6404": {"comment":"6 index changes"},
        "6406": {"synopsis":"Counts down the time-out while waiting for the index bit to change; error 55 at its end.","comment":"Time-out count"},
        "6411": {"comment":"Its high part; run out?"},
        "6414": {"comment":"Stops with error code 55"},
        "6416": {"synopsis":"Has the status's index bit (bit 1) changed since the last read?","comment":"WD1772 status"},
        "6419": {"comment":"Index bit changed?"},
        "6424": {"comment":"The new status"},
        "6425": {"comment":"6 changes seen?"},
        "6427": {"comment":"Track 0 again"},
        "6430": {"comment":"D = track 4, E = sector 1"},
        "6433": {"comment":"A' = the tries"},
        "6435": {"synopsis":"Puts the sector number in the sector register (port $E2), then seeks the track.","comment":"Sector register: sector 1"},
        "6438": {"synopsis":"Steps the head until the track register says track D (4).","comment":"Wait while busy"},
        "6441": {"comment":"Track register"},
        "6443": {"comment":"Track 4?"},
        "6446": {"comment":"Step out"},
        "6448": {"comment":"Above track 4? Out"},
        "6450": {"comment":"Below: step in"},
        "6452": {"synopsis":"Sends the step command in C and tests the track again."},
        "6457": {"synopsis":"Reads the sector into $8000 with interrupts off: the Read Sector command, then a byte from\nthe data port (INI) each time the status shows a data request, until the controller is not\nbusy.","comment":"No interrupts while reading"},
        "6458": {"comment":"Read Sector command"},
        "6463": {"comment":"To $8000"},
        "6466": {"comment":"The data port $E3"},
        "6469": {"comment":"CP $ED hides INI at $1946: a byte from the data port"},
        "6472": {"synopsis":"Waits for the next data request (another byte) or the end of the command (not busy).","comment":"WD1772 status"},
        "6474": {"comment":"Data request? Read the byte"},
        "6478": {"comment":"Still busy?"},
        "6482": {"comment":"Lost data, CRC or not found?"},
        "6486": {"comment":"Another try"},
        "6488": {"comment":"The 5th?"},
        "6491": {"comment":"Yes: back to track 0 first"},
        "6495": {"comment":"10 tries? Stops with error code 19"},
        "6501": {"comment":"Try again"},
        "6503": {"synopsis":"Compares the 4 bytes at $8100 with \"BOOT\" at ROM1 $FB94, then runs the sector at $8009.","comment":"The sector's bytes from $8100"},
        "6506": {"comment":"\"BOOT\" in the keyword list"},
        "6509": {"comment":"4 letters"},
        "6511": {"synopsis":"Compares one letter, case and bit 7 ignored."},
        "6513": {"comment":"The same letter?"},
        "6518": {"comment":"No: stops with error code 53"},
        "6520": {"synopsis":"The next letter; after 4 jumps into the boot sector at $8009."},
        "6523": {"comment":"Runs the boot code"},
        "6526": {"synopsis":"Waits until drive 1's controller is not busy, then sends it command C (FDC1_CMD).\nEntry: C = the command.\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "6529": {"synopsis":"Writes command C to drive 1's WD1772 (port $E0) and waits a little (256 DJNZ turns) before\nthe status is read.\nEntry: C = the command.\nExit: B = 0.\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "6530": {"comment":"WD1772 command register"},
        "6532": {"comment":"A short delay"},
        "6534": {"synopsis":"The delay loop."},
        "6537": {"synopsis":"Seeks track 0 on drive 1 (command $09) and falls into FDC1_WAIT_READY.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"Restore command (to track 0)"},
        "6542": {"synopsis":"Waits until drive 1's WD1772 is not busy (status bit 0); stops with error 14 when ESC is\npressed.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"WD1772 status"},
        "6544": {"comment":"Not busy? Done"},
        "6546": {"comment":"ESC: error 14"},
        "6551": {"synopsis":"JSTRS's body (ROM0's JSTRS jumps here; ROM1 $D145 calls it for STR$): takes the number off\nthe calculator stack and writes its text in PRNBUFF ($5BA0).\n1. NUM_TO_DIGITS writes the sign, a leading 0 kept for rounding and up to 9 digits, with a\n   point for a fraction; a number of 2^29 or more, or below 1, is first scaled by a power of\n   ten kept in EPOWER.\n2. When the digits ran out (DIGITS 0) the last one is dropped and rounds the rest up when it\n   is 5 or more.\n3. Trailing zeros of a fraction, and the point when nothing follows it, are removed; the\n   leading 0 is removed unless the rounding carried into it.\n4. A scaled number is written as a fraction with leading zeros when its power fits FRACLIM\n   (6), otherwise with a point after the first digit and \"E+n\" or \"E-n\".\nObserved in PRNBUFF after PRINT: 1/3 gives 0.33333333, 123456789 1.2345679E+8, 1E-5 0.00001,\n1E-7 1E-7.\nEntry: a number on the calculator stack.\nExit: DE = PRNBUFF; BC = the length.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL'.","comment":"FRACLIM: 6"},
        "6556": {"comment":"The digits into PRNBUFF"},
        "6559": {"comment":"DIGITS: ran out?"},
        "6563": {"comment":"No: nothing to round"},
        "6565": {"comment":"NPRPOS back: drops the last digit"},
        "6573": {"comment":"Below 5? No rounding"},
        "6577": {"synopsis":"Rounds up: this digit becomes 0 and the carry goes to the one before it.","comment":"This one 0"},
        "6579": {"synopsis":"Steps back to the previous digit, past the point."},
        "6581": {"comment":"The point? Past it"},
        "6585": {"comment":"Digit + 1"},
        "6586": {"comment":"Was 9? 0 and carry on"},
        "6591": {"synopsis":"BC = the text's length; trims trailing zeros of a fraction (and of a scaled number), then\nthe leading 0.","comment":"NPRPOS: the end"},
        "6597": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "6602": {"comment":"Only 1 character? Done"},
        "6604": {"comment":"HL = the end"},
        "6606": {"comment":"DECPNTED: a point?"},
        "6610": {"comment":"Yes: strip zeros"},
        "6612": {"synopsis":"No point, or the point reached: strips on only for a scaled number (EPOWER not 0).","comment":"EPOWER: scaled?"},
        "6616": {"comment":"No: keep the rest"},
        "6618": {"synopsis":"Drops a trailing 0 and looks at the character before it.","comment":"One character shorter"},
        "6621": {"comment":"Another 0?"},
        "6626": {"comment":"The point? Shorter at it"},
        "6630": {"comment":"Keeps this digit"},
        "6631": {"synopsis":"Looks at the first character after a '-'."},
        "6632": {"comment":"A sign?"},
        "6636": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6638": {"synopsis":"Is the leading 0 still there (no rounding carried into it)? Then it is removed and the text\nmoved left one place; EPOWER 1-$80 becomes EPOWER + 1 unless that is 8.","comment":"The leading 0?"},
        "6640": {"comment":"No: the carry reached it"},
        "6642": {"comment":"EPOWER"},
        "6645": {"comment":"1 more for 1-$80, kept otherwise"},
        "6650": {"comment":"8? Kept as it was"},
        "6657": {"synopsis":"Removes the leading 0: one shorter, NPRPOS back one, the text moved left.","comment":"One shorter"},
        "6659": {"comment":"NPRPOS back one"},
        "6666": {"comment":"From the next character"},
        "6669": {"comment":"10 bytes left one place"},
        "6674": {"synopsis":"Chooses the form: as it is when not scaled and a digit is left or a point was written; a\nfull 10-digit integer is redone scaled (EPOWER $FF); a scaled number goes on at NTT_SCALED.","comment":"PRNBUFF"},
        "6677": {"comment":"DIGITS"},
        "6680": {"comment":"OR DECPNTED"},
        "6685": {"comment":"H = EPOWER"},
        "6689": {"comment":"Scaled?"},
        "6693": {"comment":"Digits left or a point: done"},
        "6695": {"comment":"EPOWER $FF"},
        "6699": {"comment":"Trims again"},
        "6701": {"synopsis":"A scaled number: H = EPOWER, 1 more when digits are left or a point was written."},
        "6705": {"synopsis":"H - 8 is the power to show: 0 needs no exponent; below FRACLIM it is written as a fraction\nwith leading zeros (NTT_LEAD_ZEROS); otherwise with \"E\".","comment":"L = FRACLIM"},
        "6709": {"comment":"The power"},
        "6712": {"comment":"0: as it is"},
        "6715": {"comment":"Below FRACLIM: leading zeros"},
        "6717": {"comment":"Negative? Its magnitude"},
        "6722": {"synopsis":"Splits the power into its tens and units digits (L, A).","comment":"Tens digit, from '0'"},
        "6724": {"synopsis":"Counts tens."},
        "6729": {"comment":"A = the units digit"},
        "6732": {"comment":"D = EPOWER, E = the tens"},
        "6733": {"comment":"HL = the end of the text"},
        "6734": {"comment":"'E'"},
        "6737": {"comment":"'+'"},
        "6739": {"comment":"EPOWER positive: the power is negative"},
        "6743": {"comment":"'-'"},
        "6745": {"synopsis":"Writes the tens digit unless it is 0."},
        "6747": {"comment":"Tens 0? Left out"},
        "6751": {"comment":"One longer"},
        "6754": {"synopsis":"Writes the units digit; 3 more characters (E, sign, units)."},
        "6756": {"comment":"E, sign, units"},
        "6759": {"comment":"The text"},
        "6768": {"synopsis":"Is there more than one digit before the 'E'? Then a point goes after the first."},
        "6769": {"comment":"The second character"},
        "6772": {"synopsis":"Ends here at an 'E' (or when no exponent was needed); otherwise inserts the point."},
        "6774": {"comment":"One longer"},
        "6775": {"comment":"A gap of 1"},
        "6782": {"comment":"The point after the first digit"},
        "6786": {"synopsis":"A small power: writes the number as \"0.\" and zeros before its digits; the gap is at most 19\nand the length at most 21.","comment":"The zeros to insert"},
        "6787": {"comment":"At most 19"},
        "6793": {"synopsis":"Opens the gap for \"0.\" and the zeros."},
        "6794": {"comment":"Moves the text right"},
        "6798": {"comment":"The new length"},
        "6800": {"comment":"At most 21"},
        "6806": {"synopsis":"Writes the '0' and the point, then the zeros."},
        "6807": {"comment":"'0'"},
        "6809": {"comment":"Then '.'"},
        "6813": {"synopsis":"Writes A, then zeros."},
        "6816": {"synopsis":"Next character of the gap."},
        "6819": {"synopsis":"Done: DE = PRNBUFF."},
        "6823": {"synopsis":"Moves the text in PRNBUFF A places to the right (LDDR from the buffer's end, $5BB4), opening\na gap after its first character, or after the '-' and the first.\nEntry: A = the gap.\nExit: HL = the byte before the text (PRNBUFF - 1, or PRNBUFF after a '-').\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.\nKeeps: BC."},
        "6824": {"comment":"HL = -A"},
        "6830": {"comment":"BC = 21 - A bytes"},
        "6837": {"comment":"A sign first?"},
        "6844": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "6845": {"synopsis":"Moves the bytes right from the buffer's end.","comment":"The buffer's last byte"},
        "6848": {"comment":"Source: A bytes before it"},
        "6853": {"synopsis":"Writes the sign, a 0 and the digits of the number on the calculator stack in PRNBUFF (from\nNUM_TO_TEXT).\n1. DIGITS = 10, EPOWER = 0, DECPNTED = 0, NPRPOS = PRNBUFF; the number is made floating\n   point and dropped (its bytes stay; HL = it).\n2. '-' when negative, then a '0'; a zero ends there.\n3. A number from 1 to below 2^29 (exponent $81-$9D): its integer part becomes BCD\n   (BIN_TO_BCD) and digits; then the fraction's digits after a point, multiplying by 10,\n   until DIGITS runs out.\n4. Otherwise NTD_SCALE scales it first.\nExit: NPRPOS past the last character; DIGITS 0 when the digits ran out.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL'.","comment":"DIGITS = 10"},
        "6859": {"comment":"EPOWER = 0, DECPNTED = 0"},
        "6864": {"comment":"NPRPOS = PRNBUFF"},
        "6867": {"comment":"Floating point, then dropped"},
        "6871": {"comment":"HL = the number, DE past it"},
        "6876": {"comment":"Negative?"},
        "6880": {"comment":"'-' (not counted)"},
        "6885": {"comment":"The leading '0'"},
        "6888": {"comment":"The exponent"},
        "6890": {"comment":"Zero? Done"},
        "6891": {"comment":"Below 1? Scale it"},
        "6895": {"comment":"The bits before the point"},
        "6897": {"comment":"30 or more? Scale it"},
        "6901": {"synopsis":"Converts a number of A integer bits (1-29): HL' = the mantissa's top word (bit 7 set), HL\nits low word; the integer part's digits, then a point and the fraction's.","comment":"The mantissa's top word"},
        "6903": {"comment":"The hidden top bit"},
        "6908": {"comment":"HL' = it"},
        "6912": {"comment":"The low word"},
        "6916": {"comment":"Integer part to BCD; the fraction left"},
        "6920": {"comment":"Its digits"},
        "6924": {"comment":"Digits ran out? Done"},
        "6925": {"comment":"No fraction?"},
        "6931": {"comment":"'.'"},
        "6934": {"comment":"The fraction into DE' and DE"},
        "6937": {"synopsis":"Multiplies the 32-bit fraction by 10; the part over 1 is the next digit."},
        "6938": {"comment":"Low word x 10"},
        "6943": {"comment":"High word x 10 + the carry"},
        "6948": {"comment":"A = the digit"},
        "6951": {"comment":"Until the digits run out"},
        "6954": {"synopsis":"Multiplies DE by 10 and adds A: E then D through MUL10_BYTE.\nEntry: DE = the word; A = the carry in.\nExit: E = the low byte of the result; L = its high byte; A = the carry out (0-9).\nChanges: AF, BC, E, HL.","comment":"E first"},
        "6958": {"comment":"Its low byte"},
        "6959": {"comment":"Then D"},
        "6960": {"synopsis":"HL = C x 10 + A.\nEntry: C = the byte; A = the carry in.\nExit: L = the low byte; A = H = the carry out.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "6964": {"comment":"Times 4"},
        "6966": {"comment":"Times 5"},
        "6967": {"comment":"Times 10"},
        "6969": {"comment":"Plus A"},
        "6972": {"synopsis":"A number below 1 (carry) or of 2^29 or more: put back on the calculator stack and scaled by\na power of ten so its integer part has about 9 digits; EPOWER = that power less 1. Then it\nis converted as NTD_INT_FORM.","comment":"STKEND: the number back on the stack"},
        "6978": {"comment":"Small: the power from $80 - exponent"},
        "6981": {"comment":"Plus 9"},
        "6985": {"synopsis":"A large number: the power is 8 - its decimal exponent.","comment":"Its decimal exponent"},
        "6990": {"comment":"8 - it"},
        "6991": {"synopsis":"EPOWER = the power - 1; scales by 10^power and converts the result.","comment":"EPOWER"},
        "6996": {"comment":"Times 10^A"},
        "6999": {"comment":"HL = the scaled number"},
        "7002": {"comment":"Its integer bits"},
        "7008": {"synopsis":"Writes '.' at NPRPOS and sets DECPNTED, without counting a digit.\nChanges: AF."},
        "7010": {"comment":"DECPNTED"},
        "7015": {"synopsis":"Writes the digit '0' (PUT_DIGIT with A = 0)."},
        "7016": {"synopsis":"Writes the digit A at NPRPOS and counts it in DIGITS. $1B73 (inside the LD HL below) is a\nsecond entry that writes the character A without counting it.\nEntry: A = the digit (0-9).\nExit: carry when DIGITS has reached 0.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: HL.","comment":"As a character"},
        "7019": {"comment":"DIGITS - 1"},
        "7023": {"comment":"Not 0: no carry"},
        "7025": {"comment":"Run out: carry"},
        "7026": {"comment":"Hides PUSH HL ($1B73), AND A ($1B74)"},
        "7029": {"comment":"NPRPOS"},
        "7034": {"comment":"Moved on"},
        "7039": {"synopsis":"For a number below 1: A = $80 - its exponent, then as DEC_EXP_EST."},
        "7043": {"synopsis":"Estimates the decimal exponent of a binary one: A = INT(A x 0.30103), log10 of 2 as a 5-byte\nconstant.\nEntry: A = the binary exponent.\nExit: A = the estimate; DE at the dropped result.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Stacks A"},
        "7046": {"comment":"Times log10(2); INT; dropped"},
        "7057": {"comment":"Its low byte"},
        "7061": {"synopsis":"Shifts the top A bits of the 32-bit number HL'HL out, doubling the 5-byte BCD number in\nBCDBUFF ($5BB0-$5BB4, high byte first) with each bit added: the integer part as 10 BCD\ndigits.\nEntry: A = the bits (1-29); HL' = the high word; HL = the low word.\nExit: BCDBUFF set; HL'HL = the rest (the fraction) at the top.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, HL'."},
        "7062": {"comment":"BCDBUFF = 0"},
        "7068": {"synopsis":"Clears BCDBUFF."},
        "7072": {"synopsis":"Shifts the next bit out of HL'HL into carry.","comment":"The low word"},
        "7074": {"comment":"The high word: the top bit to carry"},
        "7077": {"comment":"BCDBUFF's last byte"},
        "7082": {"synopsis":"BCDBUFF x 2 + the bit, a byte at a time with DAA."},
        "7083": {"comment":"Doubled, plus carry"},
        "7084": {"comment":"Kept BCD"},
        "7089": {"comment":"Bits left?"},
        "7093": {"synopsis":"Writes BCDBUFF's digits through PUT_DIGIT, leading zeros left out: each digit is rotated out\nof the top with RLD, a 15 rotated in at the bottom first marks the end.\nExit: carry when DIGITS ran out.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"C = 1 while zeros are left out"},
        "7095": {"comment":"The end mark"},
        "7097": {"synopsis":"Rotates the 10 digits left by one: the top one comes out in A."},
        "7099": {"comment":"BCDBUFF's last byte"},
        "7102": {"synopsis":"One byte of the rotation."},
        "7107": {"comment":"Not 0: write it"},
        "7109": {"comment":"A leading 0? Left out"},
        "7112": {"synopsis":"Writes the digit; the end mark (10 or more) ends.","comment":"Leading zeros over"},
        "7115": {"comment":"The end mark?"},
        "7118": {"comment":"Write it"},
        "7121": {"comment":"Until the digits run out"},
        "7124": {"synopsis":"Multiplies the number on the calculator stack by 10^A, A signed (dividing for a negative A),\nby squaring 10 for each bit of |A|. ROM0's READ_EXP_SCALE jumps here for a number's\nexponent; NTD_SCALE calls it.\nEntry: A = the power (-128 to 127); a number on the calculator stack.\nExit: the result on the calculator stack.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, MEM 0.","comment":"C = the sign"},
        "7129": {"comment":"Its magnitude"},
        "7131": {"synopsis":"B = |A|; stacks 10, the first power."},
        "7132": {"comment":"Stacks 10"},
        "7137": {"synopsis":"The next power: squares it.","comment":"Duplicate, multiply"},
        "7141": {"synopsis":"The next bit of |A|: multiplies or divides the number by this power when it is set.","comment":"Bit set?"},
        "7145": {"comment":"Negative? Divide"},
        "7149": {"comment":"Number x power; power kept"},
        "7156": {"synopsis":"Divides the number by this power, keeping the power.","comment":"Number / power; power kept"},
        "7161": {"synopsis":"More bits? Squares again; else drops the power.","comment":"Bits left?"},
        "7164": {"comment":"STKEND: the power dropped"},
        "7168": {"synopsis":"The output routine of channels K, S and P (their output word, $01CC, is a RST $30 to here):\nprints character A on the device DEVICE selects.\n1. Codes below 32 are control codes (PRT_CTRL); 128 and up graphics, UDGs and keywords\n   (PRT_HIGH_CODE).\n2. Otherwise FLAGS bit 0 is set for a space, OPCHAR = A, and its pattern (CHARS + 8 x A) is\n   printed at the print position: past the right-hand limit (or with a pending newline,\n   column $FE) a new line comes first. PATOUT prints the pattern; the position moves one\n   column on.\nEntry: A = the character.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"A control code?"},
        "7173": {"comment":"128 or more?"},
        "7178": {"comment":"CHARS"},
        "7182": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 0: a space printed"},
        "7187": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "7193": {"synopsis":"HL = DE + 8 x A: the pattern of character A in the set at DE."},
        "7199": {"comment":"The pattern"},
        "7200": {"comment":"OPCHAR"},
        "7204": {"synopsis":"Gets the print position; past the right-hand limit, moves to a new line first (as ENTER with\nE = $FF) and, with $5ABD set after a line overflow, calls ROM1 $F46A and prints B again.","comment":"DE = the position, A = the limit"},
        "7207": {"comment":"Fits on this line?"},
        "7210": {"comment":"C = 0 when the line just overflowed"},
        "7214": {"comment":"E = $FF: a new line now"},
        "7216": {"comment":"DEVICE: carry for the printer"},
        "7222": {"comment":"New line"},
        "7227": {"comment":"$5ABD set?"},
        "7231": {"comment":"No: place it again"},
        "7234": {"comment":"An overflow?"},
        "7238": {"comment":"ROM1 $F46A"},
        "7241": {"comment":"The character again"},
        "7244": {"synopsis":"Prints the pattern at HL at position DE through PATOUT (B = $FF with OVER, C = INVERT), then\nmoves the position one column on (STORE_PRINT_POS)."},
        "7245": {"comment":"OVERT"},
        "7248": {"comment":"B = $FF when not 0"},
        "7253": {"comment":"INVERT"},
        "7257": {"comment":"PATOUT"},
        "7264": {"comment":"The position"},
        "7265": {"comment":"One column on"},
        "7266": {"synopsis":"Stores HL as the print position of DEVICE's device: 0 SPOSNU, 1 SPOSNL, otherwise PRPOSN.\nEntry: HL = the position (H the row, L the column).\nChanges: AF.","comment":"DEVICE"},
        "7269": {"comment":"Upper screen?"},
        "7272": {"comment":"Lower screen?"},
        "7275": {"comment":"PRPOSN"},
        "7279": {"synopsis":"The lower screen: SPOSNL.","comment":"SPOSNL"},
        "7283": {"synopsis":"The upper screen: SPOSNU.","comment":"SPOSNU"},
        "7287": {"synopsis":"The routine PATOUT holds after boot (the start-up value at ROM1 $FC40): prints a character\npattern. Nothing when DMPFLG is set; on the printer (DEVICE 2) OPCHAR goes to the printer\nitself; on a screen the pattern is printed by PRINT_PAT_SCREEN, twice (DOUBLE_PATTERN, the\nsecond half with DHADJ = 8) when CSIZEH is 16 or more.\nEntry: HL = the pattern; DE = the position; B = $FF for OVER; C = INVERT.","comment":"DMPFLG"},
        "7291": {"comment":"Set: nothing printed"},
        "7292": {"comment":"DEVICE"},
        "7295": {"comment":"The printer?"},
        "7299": {"comment":"CSIZEH"},
        "7302": {"comment":"Below 16: one pattern"},
        "7307": {"comment":"Each row twice at $5129"},
        "7312": {"comment":"The top half"},
        "7315": {"comment":"DHADJ: 8 rows down"},
        "7322": {"comment":"The lower half"},
        "7328": {"comment":"DHADJ = 0"},
        "7333": {"synopsis":"The printer: sends OPCHAR to it (PRINTER_OUT_A)."},
        "7339": {"synopsis":"Codes 128 and up: graphics and UDGs (PRT_GRAPHIC) for $80-$84, or for any code when FLAGE\nbit 7 or INQUFG bit 0 is set; otherwise keywords (PRT_TOKEN)."},
        "7340": {"comment":"INQUFG bit 0"},
        "7345": {"comment":"OR FLAGE"},
        "7349": {"comment":"Bit 7: as a graphic?"},
        "7353": {"comment":"Below $85?"},
        "7355": {"synopsis":"Carry: printed as a graphic or UDG."},
        "7358": {"synopsis":"Prints keyword token A ($85-$FE) or, for $FF, sets the channel to take the function code\nthat follows. ROM0's CHAN_R_CODE85 jumps here for the editor's channel.\n1. PRTOKV is called first when set.\n2. $FF: the current output becomes CHAN_OUT_DCEE (PRT_FN_PREFIX).\n3. Otherwise the keyword is found from one of 4 starting points in the keyword list ($F9BC\n   for $85-$9F, $FA2F for $A0-$BF, $FACB for $C0-$DF, $FB67 for $E0-$FE) and printed with a\n   space before (unless one was just printed) and after (after a letter or '$').\nEntry: A = the code.","comment":"PRTOKV"},
        "7361": {"comment":"Called when set"},
        "7364": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "7368": {"comment":"A = token - $85"},
        "7370": {"comment":"$85-$9F: from USING"},
        "7381": {"comment":"$A0-$BF: from PALETTE"},
        "7388": {"comment":"$C0-$DF: from FOR"},
        "7395": {"comment":"$E0 on: from OUT"},
        "7400": {"synopsis":"$FF: the next byte goes to CHAN_OUT_DCEE (the saved output is put back there).","comment":"CHAN_OUT_DCEE"},
        "7406": {"synopsis":"The byte after $FF: puts the saved output routine back and prints the function keyword for\ncode A ($3B on) from the keyword list. Codes $3B-$52 count from PI ($F8C9), with no spaces\nexcept a trailing one for codes $42 and $43; $53-$79 from SIN ($F92A), with a trailing\nspace; $7A on from MOD ($F9A3), spaces around the first 7 and none after. ROM0's\nCHAN_OUT_DCEE jumps here.\nEntry: A = the code.","comment":"Saved output back"},
        "7409": {"comment":"Index from $3B"},
        "7411": {"comment":"$3B-$52?"},
        "7415": {"comment":"$53-$79?"},
        "7419": {"comment":"$7A on: from MOD"},
        "7422": {"comment":"The first 7: spaces round"},
        "7428": {"synopsis":"Codes $3B-$52 from PI: a trailing space for index 7 and 8 only.","comment":"From PI"},
        "7441": {"synopsis":"Codes $53-$79: from SIN, with a trailing space.","comment":"The index from SIN"},
        "7446": {"synopsis":"Prints keyword A of the list at DE with no space before it and the trailing-space test\nafter.","comment":"No carry: trailing test"},
        "7448": {"comment":"Carry: no leading space"},
        "7451": {"synopsis":"JPOMSG's body (ROM0's POMSG_R1 jumps here): prints message A of the table at DE (bit-7 ended\nentries), expanded in a buffer at $50CB, with no spaces added.\nEntry: A = the message number (0 the first); DE = the table.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Carry: no spaces"},
        "7454": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "7462": {"synopsis":"Keyword A of the list at DE with no spaces. Hides AND A at $1D28: keyword A with both\nspaces."},
        "7463": {"comment":"Hides AND A ($1D28): no carry, both spaces"},
        "7466": {"synopsis":"Keeps the leading-space flag and expands keyword A into the buffer at $50C0."},
        "7470": {"synopsis":"A leading space unless carry or FLAGS bit 0 (a space was just printed)."},
        "7471": {"comment":"No leading space?"},
        "7473": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 0: a space last?"},
        "7479": {"comment":"No: one now"},
        "7482": {"synopsis":"Prints the text; then a space after it when the flag allows and its last character is a\nletter or '$'.","comment":"The text"},
        "7486": {"comment":"No trailing space?"},
        "7487": {"comment":"Its last character"},
        "7489": {"comment":"A letter?"},
        "7493": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "7496": {"synopsis":"Prints a space."},
        "7500": {"synopsis":"Expands entry A of the bit-7-ended table at DE into the buffer at $50C0 (MSG_TO_HL). ROM0's\nREPORT_TEXT calls it for an error message.\nEntry: A = the entry (0 the first); DE = the table.\nExit: DE = $50C0; BC = the length.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The buffer"},
        "7503": {"synopsis":"Expands entry A of the table at DE to HL; DE = HL's start and BC = the length."},
        "7504": {"comment":"Copies it"},
        "7509": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "7514": {"synopsis":"Copies entry A of the bit-7-ended table at DE to HL, clearing bit 7. A byte below 32 stands\nfor entry n of the table at ROM1 $F819, copied in its place (recursively).\nEntry: A = the entry; DE = the table; HL = the destination.\nExit: HL past the copy; DE past the entry.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"A + 1 entries to count"},
        "7518": {"synopsis":"Skips one entry: up to its byte with bit 7 set."},
        "7523": {"synopsis":"Entries left to skip?"},
        "7525": {"synopsis":"Copies the next byte; one below 32 is expanded from the table at $F819."},
        "7526": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "7528": {"comment":"Below 32?"},
        "7533": {"comment":"The table of common parts"},
        "7536": {"comment":"Copies part A"},
        "7540": {"comment":"Hides LD (HL),A; INC HL ($1D75)"},
        "7543": {"comment":"The byte again"},
        "7545": {"comment":"Bit 7: the last?"},
        "7549": {"synopsis":"A graphic code: on the printer, OPCHAR = A and LPRTV is called when set; then $80-$8F are\nblock graphics made at $5121 (unless BGFLG is set) and the rest UDGs (PRT_UDG).\nEntry: C = the code.","comment":"DEVICE"},
        "7552": {"comment":"The printer?"},
        "7557": {"comment":"OPCHAR"},
        "7560": {"comment":"LPRTV"},
        "7563": {"comment":"Called when set"},
        "7566": {"synopsis":"BGFLG set, or $90 and up: a UDG; otherwise a block graphic: bits 0 and 1 the top half's\nright and left, bits 2 and 3 the bottom half's.","comment":"BGFLG"},
        "7573": {"comment":"$90 or more?"},
        "7577": {"comment":"Each bit 4 wide: E top, D bottom"},
        "7580": {"comment":"The pattern at $5121"},
        "7584": {"comment":"4 rows of E"},
        "7586": {"synopsis":"The top 4 rows."},
        "7592": {"synopsis":"The bottom 4 rows."},
        "7596": {"comment":"The pattern"},
        "7597": {"comment":"B = the code"},
        "7598": {"comment":"Prints it"},
        "7601": {"synopsis":"A UDG: codes $A9 and up from HUDG, the others from UDG (UDG - $480 + 8 x code).","comment":"HUDG"},
        "7604": {"comment":"$A9 or more?"},
        "7609": {"comment":"Minus $90 x 8"},
        "7612": {"comment":"UDG"},
        "7616": {"synopsis":"DE = the set's base; prints the pattern (PRT_PATTERN_AT)."},
        "7620": {"synopsis":"Control codes: 6 to 23 go through CTRL_OFFSETS with C = the code and DE, A, carry from\nGET_PRINT_POS (the position, the limit, the printer); the others print '?'.\nEntry: A = the code.","comment":"24 or more?"},
        "7624": {"comment":"Below 6?"},
        "7631": {"comment":"CTRL_OFFSETS - 6"},
        "7635": {"comment":"The offset"},
        "7636": {"comment":"HL = the handler"},
        "7637": {"comment":"C = the code"},
        "7638": {"comment":"DE = the position, A = the limit"},
        "7641": {"comment":"To the handler"},
        "7642": {"synopsis":"The control codes' handlers: one byte for each code 6 to 23, the handler's distance from the\nbyte itself (PRT_CTRL adds it). 6 comma, 7 '?', 8 back, 9 right, 10 down, 11 up, 12 delete,\n13 ENTER, 14 an erasing space, 15 '?', 16-21 a colour item (one parameter), 22 AT and 23 TAB\n(two).","comment":"6: CTRL_COMMA"},
        "7643": {"comment":"7: PRT_QUERY"},
        "7644": {"comment":"8: CTRL_BACKSPACE"},
        "7645": {"comment":"9: CTRL_RIGHT"},
        "7646": {"comment":"10: CTRL_LINE_FEED"},
        "7647": {"comment":"11: CTRL_UP"},
        "7648": {"comment":"12: CTRL_DELETE"},
        "7649": {"comment":"13: CTRL_ENTER"},
        "7650": {"comment":"14: ERASE_SPACE"},
        "7651": {"comment":"15: PRT_QUERY"},
        "7652": {"comment":"16-21: CTRL_ONE_PARAM"},
        "7658": {"comment":"22-23: CTRL_TWO_PARAMS"},
        "7660": {"synopsis":"Code 6 (the PRINT comma): spaces to the next field of 16 columns (8 when TABVAR is set) from\nWINDLHS, at most to WINDRHS + 1; with a pending newline (column past WINDRHS) a whole field\nof spaces.\nEntry: E = the column.","comment":"The column"},
        "7661": {"comment":"WINDLHS"},
        "7664": {"comment":"Relative to it"},
        "7666": {"comment":"TABVAR"},
        "7670": {"comment":"Fields of 16"},
        "7675": {"comment":"Fields of 8"},
        "7678": {"synopsis":"The next field's column, at most WINDRHS + 1; A = the spaces to it.","comment":"WINDRHS"},
        "7681": {"comment":"Pending newline?"},
        "7685": {"comment":"This field's start"},
        "7686": {"comment":"Plus a field"},
        "7687": {"comment":"Plus WINDLHS"},
        "7688": {"comment":"WINDRHS"},
        "7689": {"comment":"Past it?"},
        "7692": {"comment":"WINDRHS + 1"},
        "7694": {"synopsis":"A = the target column - E."},
        "7695": {"synopsis":"Prints A spaces (none for 0). TAB jumps here."},
        "7697": {"synopsis":"Prints B spaces."},
        "7703": {"synopsis":"A pending newline: a whole field of spaces."},
        "7704": {"comment":"B = the field's width"},
        "7707": {"synopsis":"Prints '?': an unknown control code, or one the device cannot do."},
        "7711": {"synopsis":"Code 8: one column back; at WINDLHS to WINDRHS of the row above (not on the printer, not\nabove WINDTOP); from a pending newline to WINDRHS.\nEntry: D, E = the position; A = WINDRHS (from GET_PRINT_POS).","comment":"WINDLHS"},
        "7714": {"comment":"At the left edge?"},
        "7715": {"comment":"WINDRHS"},
        "7720": {"comment":"Back one"},
        "7721": {"comment":"Still past WINDRHS?"},
        "7724": {"comment":"WINDRHS"},
        "7725": {"synopsis":"Stores DE as the print position."},
        "7729": {"synopsis":"To WINDRHS of the row above; the printer prints '?'.","comment":"Column WINDRHS"},
        "7730": {"comment":"DEVICE"},
        "7733": {"comment":"The printer: '?'"},
        "7735": {"synopsis":"Code 11: one row up, not above WINDTOP; the printer prints '?'.","comment":"The printer: '?'"},
        "7737": {"comment":"WINDTOP"},
        "7740": {"comment":"The top row? Stays"},
        "7745": {"synopsis":"Code 9: one column right, printing a space with OVER 1 and INVERSE 0 so nothing changes on\nthe screen.","comment":"OVERT, INVERT kept"},
        "7749": {"comment":"M23PAPT kept"},
        "7753": {"comment":"OVER 1, INVERSE 0"},
        "7756": {"comment":"1 space"},
        "7760": {"synopsis":"Code 12: back one column, an erasing space, back again; the printer prints '?'.","comment":"The printer: '?'"},
        "7762": {"comment":"Back"},
        "7765": {"comment":"Erase"},
        "7768": {"comment":"Back"},
        "7772": {"synopsis":"Erases the listing's current-line marker: prints AT row,5 and an erasing space, where row is\nLNPTR - WINDTOP (0 if negative). ROM0's LIST_CURSOR_MOVE and LCUR_DOWN call it.\nExit: A = C = the marker's row in the window; H = $5B.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"WINDTOP"},
        "7776": {"comment":"LNPTR"},
        "7779": {"comment":"Its row in the window"},
        "7783": {"synopsis":"AT row,5, then an erasing space."},
        "7784": {"comment":"Column 5"},
        "7786": {"comment":"AT A,E (ROM0 $081A)"},
        "7789": {"comment":"Erasing space"},
        "7796": {"synopsis":"Code 14: one erasing space (ERASE_SPACES with B = 1)."},
        "7798": {"synopsis":"Prints B spaces in the permanent paper colour (M23PAPP) with OVER 0 and INVERSE 0, then puts\nOVERT, INVERT and M23PAPT back. The listing (ROM1 $F3C5, $F485) uses it.\nEntry: B = the count.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"OVERT, INVERT kept"},
        "7802": {"comment":"M23PAPT kept"},
        "7806": {"comment":"M23PAPP"},
        "7809": {"comment":"As M23PAPT"},
        "7812": {"comment":"OVER 0, INVERSE 0"},
        "7815": {"synopsis":"Sets OVERT and INVERT from HL and prints B spaces, then restores them."},
        "7818": {"synopsis":"Prints the spaces."},
        "7823": {"comment":"M23PAPT back"},
        "7827": {"comment":"OVERT, INVERT back"},
        "7832": {"synopsis":"Code 10: one row down (scrolling at WINDBOT), the column kept."},
        "7833": {"comment":"E = $FE: down a row"},
        "7839": {"comment":"The old column"},
        "7842": {"synopsis":"Code 13 (ENTER), also the new line before a character past the limit. On the printer: a CR\n(and AFTERCR when not 0), the column 0. On a screen: E below $FE sets the column to $FE, a\npending newline; E $FF (or $FE) moves down a row (scrolling at WINDBOT through\nWIN_BOTTOM_LINE), to column WINDLHS for $FF, $FE for $FE.\nEntry: D, E = the position; carry for the printer.","comment":"The printer?"},
        "7844": {"comment":"The column"},
        "7845": {"comment":"Pending already ($FE, $FF)?"},
        "7849": {"comment":"WINDBOT"},
        "7852": {"comment":"The last row?"},
        "7856": {"comment":"Scroll or stop"},
        "7860": {"comment":"Stays on it"},
        "7861": {"synopsis":"The next row: column WINDLHS for E = $FF.","comment":"Next row"},
        "7862": {"comment":"$FF? Column WINDLHS"},
        "7868": {"synopsis":"Column $FE: the newline is pending."},
        "7870": {"synopsis":"E = the new column."},
        "7872": {"synopsis":"Stores the position."},
        "7875": {"synopsis":"The printer: CR, column 0 in PRPOSN, then AFTERCR's byte when it is not 0.","comment":"CR to the printer"},
        "7880": {"comment":"PRPOSN's column 0"},
        "7884": {"comment":"AFTERCR"},
        "7888": {"comment":"0: nothing after"},
        "7889": {"synopsis":"Sends A to the printer as it is, through the output routine of the channel at CHANS + $19\n(observed after boot: the 6th channel, \"B\", whose output word is ROM0's JSENDA).\nEntry: A = the byte.","comment":"CHANS"},
        "7892": {"comment":"Plus $19: the B channel's output word"},
        "7899": {"synopsis":"Codes 16-21 (a colour item): the next byte goes to CHAN_OUT_DEF3; TVDATA = the code.","comment":"CHAN_OUT_DEF3"},
        "7904": {"synopsis":"Codes 22 and 23 (AT, TAB): the next byte goes to ROM0's OUT_TAKE_PARAM; TVDATA = the code.","comment":"OUT_TAKE_PARAM"},
        "7907": {"synopsis":"Makes DE the current output (SET_TEMP_OUTPUT) and keeps the code in TVDATA."},
        "7910": {"comment":"TVDATA: the code"},
        "7915": {"synopsis":"Keeps the current channel's output routine in OPSTORE and makes DE its output routine, so\nthe next byte printed goes to DE.\nEntry: DE = the routine.\nChanges: DE, HL."},
        "7916": {"comment":"OPSTORE = the current output"},
        "7923": {"synopsis":"The last parameter of a control code (ROM0's CHAN_OUT_DEF3 jumps here after putting the\noutput back): TVDATA = the code and the first parameter. Codes 16-21: colour item code - 16\n= A (COLOUR_ITEM_SET); 22: AT (CTRL_AT); 23: TAB to column TVDATA+1 of the window, spaces\nprinted (a new line first when the column is behind).\nEntry: A = the parameter.","comment":"L = the code, H = the first parameter"},
        "7926": {"comment":"D = this one"},
        "7928": {"comment":"A colour item?"},
        "7933": {"comment":"AT?"},
        "7935": {"comment":"TAB: E = the column"},
        "7938": {"comment":"C = the limit"},
        "7939": {"comment":"Pending newline?"},
        "7943": {"comment":"WINDLHS + column - E"},
        "7948": {"comment":"There already"},
        "7949": {"comment":"Ahead: the spaces to it"},
        "7951": {"comment":"Behind: on to the next line"},
        "7954": {"synopsis":"Prints A spaces (PRT_A_SPACES)."},
        "7958": {"synopsis":"AT row,column in the window: error 32 past WINDRHS; past WINDBOT on the upper screen error\n32, on the lower screen the window grows up (LOWER_WIN_GROW) and the row is WINDBOT.\nEntry: H = the row; D = the column."},
        "7959": {"comment":"E = the column"},
        "7960": {"comment":"WINDLHS"},
        "7965": {"comment":"The screen's column"},
        "7967": {"comment":"WINDRHS"},
        "7969": {"comment":"Past it? Error 32"},
        "7971": {"comment":"WINDTOP"},
        "7975": {"comment":"The screen's row"},
        "7976": {"comment":"WINDBOT"},
        "7979": {"comment":"Within? Store it"},
        "7981": {"comment":"B = rows past the bottom"},
        "7984": {"comment":"DEVICE"},
        "7988": {"comment":"The upper screen: error 32"},
        "7990": {"comment":"The row: WINDBOT"},
        "7992": {"synopsis":"Grows the lower window up a row, B times."},
        "8000": {"synopsis":"Stores the new position (STORE_PRINT_POS)."},
        "8004": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 32: a position outside the window."},
        "8006": {"synopsis":"OPSTORE = the output routine of the current channel (the first word at CURCHL).\nChanges: DE, HL.","comment":"CURCHL"},
        "8012": {"comment":"OPSTORE"},
        "8017": {"synopsis":"A new line at the window's bottom.\n1. During an automatic listing (DFLAG bit 4): when the byte at $5B86 is 1 the listing ends\n   (stream 0, SP from LISTSP, ROM0's AUTO_LIST_END); otherwise the window scrolls.\n2. The lower screen grows up a row (LOWER_WIN_GROW).\n3. The upper screen: ESC stops with error 14; unless SPROMPT is set, SCRCT counts down and\n   at 0 the scroll message (UMSGS message 1) waits for a key: space or N stops (error 14),\n   any other key goes on with SCRCT = the window's height. Then the window scrolls up a row.","comment":"DFLAG"},
        "8020": {"comment":"Bit 4: automatic listing?"},
        "8024": {"comment":"$5B86"},
        "8028": {"comment":"Not 1: scroll"},
        "8030": {"comment":"Stream 0"},
        "8033": {"comment":"LISTSP"},
        "8037": {"comment":"The listing ends"},
        "8040": {"synopsis":"Not listing: the lower screen grows; the upper one may ask before it scrolls.","comment":"DEVICE"},
        "8043": {"comment":"The lower screen?"},
        "8046": {"comment":"ESC: error 14"},
        "8049": {"comment":"SPROMPT"},
        "8053": {"comment":"Set: no question"},
        "8055": {"comment":"SCRCT"},
        "8058": {"comment":"Counted down to 0?"},
        "8061": {"comment":"SCRCT = the height"},
        "8064": {"comment":"Temporary colours kept"},
        "8067": {"comment":"CURCHL kept"},
        "8073": {"comment":"UMSGS message 1, then a key"},
        "8080": {"comment":"Space?"},
        "8084": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "8086": {"comment":"'N'?"},
        "8088": {"synopsis":"Space or N: $5ABD = 0, then error 14; otherwise the channel and colours are put back.","comment":"$5ABD = 0"},
        "8091": {"comment":"Stops with error code 14"},
        "8094": {"comment":"CURCHL back"},
        "8098": {"comment":"Its set-up again"},
        "8101": {"comment":"Temporary colours back"},
        "8104": {"comment":"CEXTAB again"},
        "8107": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the window up a row (ROM0's SCROLL_WIN_UP1)."},
        "8110": {"synopsis":"SCRCT = WINDBOT - WINDTOP + 1, the rows before the next scroll question.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"L = WINDTOP, H = WINDBOT"},
        "8120": {"synopsis":"Grows the lower window up a row: LWTOP and WINDTOP - 1 (error 32 when LWTOP is 1), the byte\nat $5AC3 - 1; then it scrolls. When it reaches the upper screen's print row, that row moves\nup one and the upper window (stream -2, its WINDBOT this row) scrolls up first.","comment":"LWTOP"},
        "8124": {"comment":"Would be 0? Error 32"},
        "8127": {"comment":"LWTOP - 1"},
        "8128": {"comment":"WINDTOP too"},
        "8131": {"comment":"$5AC3 - 1"},
        "8135": {"comment":"SPOSNU's row"},
        "8138": {"comment":"Reached it?"},
        "8142": {"comment":"Upper row up one"},
        "8143": {"comment":"Stream -2: the upper screen"},
        "8147": {"comment":"Its WINDBOT: this row"},
        "8150": {"comment":"Scroll it up"},
        "8153": {"comment":"Stream -3: the lower screen again"},
        "8158": {"synopsis":"Copies the 8 bytes at $5AC8 back to the temporary colours $5A4D-$5A54. $1FE0 (SCF, hidden in\nthe LD H below) is a second entry that saves them there instead.\nChanges: F, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"No carry: restore"},
        "8159": {"comment":"Hides SCF ($1FE0): save"},
        "8161": {"comment":"THFATT on"},
        "8164": {"comment":"TEMPW1 on"},
        "8167": {"comment":"Save?"},
        "8169": {"comment":"Restore: the other way"},
        "8170": {"synopsis":"Copies the 8 bytes (ROM0's COPY_8_BYTES)."},
        "8173": {"synopsis":"Copies the 8-byte pattern at HL to $5129 with each byte twice: a pattern twice as high.\nEntry: HL = the pattern.\nExit: HL = $5129.\nKeeps: BC, DE."},
        "8175": {"comment":"The tall pattern"},
        "8179": {"comment":"8 rows"},
        "8181": {"synopsis":"One row, twice."},
        "8193": {"synopsis":"Clears the lower window, prints message A of UMSGS (A = 3 at $E4E5: the 'Start tape and then\npress a key' prompt), empties the key queue, waits for a new key and clears the lower window\nagain (falls into CLS_LOWER_KEEPAF). ROM1 $DF8B calls it too.\nEntry: A = the message number.\nExit: A = the key.\nChanges: all.","comment":"Clear the lower window"},
        "8196": {"comment":"Print message A of UMSGS"},
        "8199": {"comment":"Empty the key queue"},
        "8202": {"comment":"Wait for a new key: A = the key"},
        "8205": {"synopsis":"Clears the lower window (ROM0 CLS_LOWER) keeping AF.\nExit: AF as on entry.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Keep the key"},
        "8206": {"comment":"CLS_LOWER"},
        "8211": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the routine whose address MNOP holds (the main screen's output routine, which\nROM0's CLS_LOWER puts back). ROM0's CALL_R1_E013 jumps here.\nEntry: as the routine wants it.\nExit: as the routine leaves it.","comment":"BC = MNOP"},
        "8215": {"comment":"Jump there"},
        "8217": {"synopsis":"SAVE, LOAD, MERGE and VERIFY (tokens $94-$97; the command table's entries for all four reach\nit). CURCMD tells them apart.\n1. OVER after the keyword sets OVERF to 0 (nonzero without it); SLDEVT, SLNUMT = SLDEV,\n   SLNUM.\n2. The file name, a string. Running, it goes into the header buffer at $4B00: the name at\n   $4B01 (blanked to spaces, the fields after it to $FF); at most 10 characters for tape, 14\n   for other devices (error 18). An empty name is error 18 for SAVE and matches any file\n   otherwise; a SAVE name starting with a character 0-3 puts it in the header's flags byte\n   ($4B0F).\n3. What follows: CODE [start[,length[,auto-run]]], SCREEN$, LINE n (a program that runs; not\n   VERIFY), DATA name() (an array), or nothing (the program). Each sets the header's type\n   ($10 program, $11 numeric array, $12 string array, $13 code, $14 screen) and its fields.\n4. SAVE goes to SAVE_FILE. The others find a header (FIND_HEADER on tape, DOS hook HGTHD\n   otherwise) and load or verify by its type: LOAD_SCREEN, LOAD_PROG_ARRAY, ROM0's\n   RAMRUN_C5D4 for MERGE, SLC_BLOCK_LOAD for the rest.\nEntry: A = the character after the keyword.\nError: 18 (the name), 19 (a length that does not match, a failed load), 29 (syntax), 2 (DATA\nof an array that is not there, except for LOAD).","comment":"OVER after the keyword? OVERF = 0"},
        "8222": {"comment":"Not OVER: leave the pointer"},
        "8224": {"comment":"Past OVER"},
        "8225": {"synopsis":"SAVE_LOAD_CMD past any OVER: copies SLDEV and SLNUM to SLDEVT and SLNUMT and reads the file\nname.","comment":"SLDEV and SLNUM"},
        "8228": {"comment":"to SLDEVT and SLNUMT"},
        "8231": {"comment":"The file name: a string"},
        "8234": {"comment":"Checking syntax: the rest"},
        "8236": {"comment":"The header buffer's name: 25 spaces"},
        "8241": {"synopsis":"Fills B bytes with spaces from HL (the header buffer's name).","comment":"A space"},
        "8246": {"comment":"Then 14 bytes of $FF"},
        "8248": {"synopsis":"Fills B bytes with $FF from HL: the start, length and auto-run fields ($4B1F-$4B27) start as\n'not given'.","comment":"$FF: start, length, auto-run unset"},
        "8253": {"comment":"The name to $4F00: DE = it, BC = its length"},
        "8256": {"comment":"At most 10 characters for tape"},
        "8258": {"comment":"Tape?"},
        "8263": {"comment":"Other devices: at most 14"},
        "8265": {"synopsis":"Checks the name's length C against the limit H (error 18 when it reaches it), then handles\nan empty name.","comment":"The length"},
        "8266": {"comment":"Too long? Error 18"},
        "8269": {"comment":"$FF: any name (a copied name writes over it)"},
        "8274": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "8275": {"comment":"CURCMD"},
        "8278": {"comment":"Not empty"},
        "8280": {"comment":"Empty for SAVE? Error 18"},
        "8282": {"comment":"LOAD, MERGE, VERIFY: any name"},
        "8284": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 18 (a file name that is too long, or empty for SAVE). ROM1 $D326 jumps\nhere too.","comment":"Stops with error code 18"},
        "8286": {"synopsis":"A name that is not empty: for SAVE, a first character below 4 goes to the header's flags\nbyte ($4B0F) and is not part of the name.","comment":"SAVE?"},
        "8288": {"comment":"No: copy the name"},
        "8290": {"comment":"The name's first character"},
        "8291": {"comment":"Below 4?"},
        "8293": {"comment":"No: copy it all"},
        "8295": {"comment":"It goes to the header's flags byte"},
        "8298": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8299": {"comment":"Nothing else?"},
        "8302": {"synopsis":"Copies the name (BC bytes at DE) to the header buffer's name at $4B01.","comment":"HL = the name, DE = $4B01"},
        "8303": {"comment":"Copy it to the header"},
        "8305": {"synopsis":"Reads what follows the name: $FF (CODE or SCREEN$) to SLC_FN_WORD, LINE to the line number,\nanything else to SLC_DATA_Q.","comment":"What follows the name?"},
        "8306": {"comment":"$FF: a function word (CODE, SCREEN$)"},
        "8310": {"comment":"LINE?"},
        "8312": {"comment":"No: DATA or a program"},
        "8315": {"comment":"CURCMD"},
        "8318": {"comment":"VERIFY ... LINE? Error 29"},
        "8323": {"comment":"The line number"},
        "8326": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "8328": {"comment":"BC = the line"},
        "8331": {"comment":"The auto-run field: 0, then the line"},
        "8337": {"comment":"The line's low byte"},
        "8339": {"comment":"Its high byte"},
        "8340": {"synopsis":"A program: ends the syntax check; running, fills the header with the start (PROG), the\nlength (ELINE - 1 - PROG) and the offsets from PROG of NVARS, NUMEND and SAVARS\n($4B10-$4B18), and sets type $10.","comment":"A program: done when checking syntax"},
        "8343": {"comment":"A:HL = PROG"},
        "8346": {"comment":"The start: PROG's page"},
        "8349": {"comment":"and offset"},
        "8352": {"comment":"C:DE = PROG"},
        "8354": {"comment":"A:HL = ELINE"},
        "8357": {"comment":"Back one byte"},
        "8358": {"comment":"Still at $8000 or above?"},
        "8362": {"comment":"No: the page before"},
        "8363": {"synopsis":"Subtracts PROG from the end and stores the program's length (pages, offset) at $4B22.","comment":"A:HL = the length (ELINE - 1 - PROG)"},
        "8366": {"comment":"Its pages"},
        "8369": {"comment":"and the rest"},
        "8372": {"comment":"Three pointers"},
        "8374": {"comment":"From NVARS's high byte down"},
        "8378": {"comment":"To the header's $10-$18"},
        "8382": {"synopsis":"Loop: reads a 3-byte system pointer downwards from IX, subtracts PROG and stores the offset\nat IY.","comment":"The pointer's address, high byte"},
        "8387": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "8392": {"comment":"Its page"},
        "8397": {"comment":"Less PROG: the offset"},
        "8400": {"comment":"Its pages"},
        "8405": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "8410": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "8415": {"comment":"The next pointer: NUMEND, then SAVARS"},
        "8417": {"comment":"Type $10: a program"},
        "8422": {"synopsis":"After $FF: CODE takes up to three numbers (start, length, auto-run address) into $4B1F,\n$4B22 and $4B25 as a 16K block and an offset in $8000-$BFFF; SAVE needs at least two. Not\nCODE: SLC_SCREEN.","comment":"The function's code"},
        "8423": {"comment":"CODE?"},
        "8425": {"comment":"No: SCREEN$?"},
        "8427": {"comment":"The start, length and auto-run fields"},
        "8430": {"comment":"At most three numbers"},
        "8432": {"comment":"Past CODE"},
        "8433": {"comment":"End of the statement?"},
        "8436": {"comment":"No: a number"},
        "8438": {"comment":"CURCMD"},
        "8441": {"comment":"SAVE ... CODE with no numbers? Error 29"},
        "8445": {"comment":"LOAD, VERIFY, MERGE: the header's values"},
        "8447": {"synopsis":"After a comma: error 29 for a fourth number, else past the comma to the next.","comment":"A fourth number?"},
        "8448": {"synopsis":"Error 29 (STOP_ERR29) when Z: CODE with no number for SAVE, or a fourth number.","comment":"Error 29 (STOP_ERR29)"},
        "8451": {"comment":"Past the comma"},
        "8452": {"synopsis":"Evaluates one number; running, stores it at DE as a block (ADDR_TO_PAGE) and an offset with\nbit 15 set.","comment":"Keep the count"},
        "8453": {"comment":"and the field"},
        "8454": {"comment":"The number"},
        "8457": {"comment":"Checking syntax: the next"},
        "8459": {"comment":"A = 16K blocks, DE = the rest"},
        "8462": {"comment":"The field"},
        "8463": {"comment":"HL = it, DE = the offset"},
        "8464": {"comment":"The block"},
        "8466": {"comment":"The offset's low byte"},
        "8468": {"comment":"In $8000-$BFFF"},
        "8470": {"comment":"Its high byte"},
        "8471": {"comment":"The next field"},
        "8473": {"synopsis":"After a number: a comma takes another; otherwise SAVE with only a start is error 29."},
        "8475": {"comment":"The current character"},
        "8476": {"comment":"A comma: another number"},
        "8480": {"comment":"CURCMD"},
        "8483": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "8487": {"comment":"Only the start given?"},
        "8490": {"comment":"Yes: error 29"},
        "8492": {"synopsis":"Ends the syntax check and sets type $13 (code).","comment":"Done when checking syntax"},
        "8495": {"comment":"Type $13: code"},
        "8500": {"synopsis":"SCREEN$ (error 29 for any other function word): the header gets MODE at $4B10, the start\nCUSCRNP:$8000 and the length of the screen plus 40 bytes from $55D8 and the table at $5600\n(length from $EEB2), which are copied in after the screen's bytes; type $14.","comment":"SCREEN$?"},
        "8502": {"comment":"No: error 29"},
        "8505": {"comment":"Past SCREEN$; done when checking syntax"},
        "8508": {"comment":"BC = the length of the table at $5600"},
        "8511": {"comment":"Plus 40 bytes at $55D8"},
        "8515": {"comment":"MODE"},
        "8518": {"comment":"To the header's $10"},
        "8521": {"comment":"A:DE = the screen's size"},
        "8524": {"comment":"C = its pages"},
        "8525": {"comment":"Keep the extra length"},
        "8526": {"comment":"Keep the screen's size"},
        "8527": {"comment":"DE = the whole length"},
        "8529": {"comment":"The start field"},
        "8532": {"comment":"CUSCRNP: the screen's page"},
        "8536": {"comment":"At offset $8000"},
        "8542": {"comment":"The length: pages"},
        "8545": {"comment":"and the rest"},
        "8548": {"comment":"DE = the screen's size"},
        "8549": {"comment":"Where the extra bytes go"},
        "8551": {"comment":"A 24K screen?"},
        "8555": {"comment":"Yes: in the next page"},
        "8556": {"synopsis":"Copies the 40 bytes at $55D8 and the table at $5600 after the screen in its page (the next\npage for a 24K screen).","comment":"BC = the extra length"},
        "8557": {"comment":"From $55D8"},
        "8560": {"comment":"HMPR: that page"},
        "8563": {"comment":"Copy the palette bytes after the screen"},
        "8565": {"comment":"Type $14: a screen"},
        "8569": {"synopsis":"DATA? Takes an array name (not for MERGE: error 29) and records the array: its page and\naddress at $4B1F, its length + 14 at $4B22, its type byte and name at $4B10; type $11\nnumeric, $12 string. Anything else: SLC_PROGRAM.","comment":"DATA?"},
        "8571": {"comment":"No: a program"},
        "8574": {"comment":"CURCMD"},
        "8577": {"comment":"MERGE ... DATA? Error 29"},
        "8581": {"comment":"Past DATA"},
        "8582": {"comment":"Find the array named at the pointer"},
        "8587": {"comment":"Keep its flags: Z when there is none"},
        "8588": {"comment":"Type $12: a string array"},
        "8590": {"comment":"FLAGS"},
        "8593": {"comment":"Bit 6 (a number)? Numeric"},
        "8597": {"comment":"Checking syntax"},
        "8599": {"comment":"Running: the current character"},
        "8600": {"comment":"A ')'?"},
        "8604": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8607": {"synopsis":"Checking the syntax of a string name: a string array needs its ')'.","comment":"A string array?"},
        "8611": {"comment":"Yes: needs its ')'"},
        "8613": {"synopsis":"A numeric name: type $11; it must be an array (error 29), with its ')'.","comment":"Type $11: a numeric array"},
        "8614": {"comment":"Not an array? Error 29"},
        "8616": {"synopsis":"Error 29 (STOP_ERR29) when Z: MERGE with DATA, or a numeric name that is not an array."},
        "8619": {"synopsis":"Requires the ')' that ends the array's name.","comment":"The current character"},
        "8620": {"comment":"Needs ')'"},
        "8623": {"synopsis":"With Z from SAVE_VAR_LOC (no such array) to SLC_ARR_NONE; otherwise records the array's\npage, address and length.","comment":"The flags back"},
        "8624": {"comment":"Keep the type"},
        "8625": {"comment":"Not there?"},
        "8627": {"comment":"Its HMPR value: the page"},
        "8630": {"comment":"The start: the page"},
        "8633": {"comment":"and the address"},
        "8637": {"comment":"The length the array's header gives"},
        "8640": {"comment":"A:HL = it, plus 14"},
        "8643": {"comment":"The length field"},
        "8651": {"synopsis":"No such array: only LOAD may go on (it makes a new one); otherwise error 2 (NO_SUCH_ARRAY).","comment":"No such array: CURCMD"},
        "8654": {"comment":"Only LOAD may name a new one: error 2"},
        "8659": {"synopsis":"Ends the syntax check and copies the array's type byte and name (11 bytes from $513F) to\n$4B10.","comment":"A = the type"},
