        "9481": {"comment":"Save it"},
        "9484": {"synopsis":"Gives the size of a screen in mode A + 1.\nEntry: A = the mode (0-3).\nExit: A:DE = pages and bytes: 0:$1B00, 0:$3800, 1:$2000 (modes 3 and 4).\nChanges: AF, DE.","comment":"Mode 1: 6912 bytes"},
        "9488": {"comment":"Mode 1: A = 0"},
        "9489": {"comment":"Mode 2: $3800 bytes"},
        "9492": {"comment":"Mode 2: A = 1"},
        "9493": {"comment":"Modes 3 and 4: one page and $2000 bytes"},
        "9498": {"synopsis":"Tells whether the ROM handles the device in SLDEVT itself: tape ('T') always, the network\n('N') when no DOS is loaded (DOSFLG 0).\nExit: Z when the ROM handles it.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Tape?"},
        "9501": {"comment":"Yes: Z"},
        "9502": {"comment":"The network?"},
        "9504": {"comment":"No: NZ (the DOS)"},
        "9505": {"comment":"DOSFLG"},
        "9508": {"comment":"Z when no DOS is loaded"},
        "9510": {"synopsis":"Tests SLDEVT for tape.\nExit: Z when it is 'T'; A = SLDEVT.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"SLDEVT"},
        "9513": {"comment":"Z for 'T'"},
        "9516": {"synopsis":"Compares a screen's page and mode bits (A, bits 6-0) with VMPR's. ROM0's DISP_SWITCH calls\nit.\nEntry: A = the screen's VMPR value.\nExit: Z when it is the screen shown; D = A's bits 6-0.\nChanges: AF, D.","comment":"The page and mode bits"},
        "9518": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9519": {"comment":"VMPR"},
        "9521": {"comment":"Without bit 7 (MIDI IN)"},
        "9523": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "9525": {"synopsis":"Sends a block over MIDI OUT (the ROM's network): a pause, a wait for the MIDI IN line to\nstay idle, the flag byte, the bytes (NET_BLOCK with NET_PUT_BYTE) and the XOR check byte\n(seeded with the flag). Falls into NET_SEND_BYTE.\nEntry: the flag byte on the stack (TAPE_SAVE's PUSH AF); HL = the start; C = 16K pages; DE =\nthe rest.\nExit: carry clear.","comment":"Keep the length"},
        "9526": {"comment":"A short pause"},
        "9531": {"comment":"The length back"},
        "9532": {"comment":"Wait for the line to go idle"},
        "9535": {"comment":"The flag byte"},
