        "9643": {"comment":"Border 1 for the bytes"},
        "9645": {"comment":"A marker bit after the byte"},
        "9646": {"comment":"Bit 7 to carry"},
        "9648": {"synopsis":"One bit from carry: C = H for a 1, L for a 0.","comment":"A 1: H"},
        "9649": {"comment":"1?"},
        "9651": {"comment":"A 0: L"},
        "9652": {"synopsis":"The bit's two edges, C apart.","comment":"The other level"},
        "9655": {"comment":"The first edge"},
        "9657": {"comment":"Wait the half"},
        "9658": {"synopsis":"Loop: the first half's wait."},
        "9660": {"comment":"For the time the loop takes"},
        "9662": {"comment":"Back"},
        "9664": {"comment":"The next bit; Z after the marker"},
        "9666": {"comment":"The second edge"},
        "9668": {"comment":"The byte done"},
        "9671": {"comment":"Wait the half"},
        "9672": {"synopsis":"Loop: the second half's wait."},
        "9674": {"comment":"The next bit"},
        "9676": {"synopsis":"After a byte: the next data byte, or the check byte (twice) when the count runs out, or the\nend.","comment":"The pointer and count"},
        "9677": {"comment":"Count 0?"},
        "9679": {"comment":"C: the count's high part"},
        "9680": {"comment":"No: the next byte"},
        "9682": {"comment":"Past the end?"},
        "9684": {"comment":"C was $FE: done"},
        "9685": {"comment":"Counts the end"},
        "9686": {"comment":"Still bytes to go?"},
        "9690": {"comment":"The check byte"},
        "9694": {"synopsis":"Takes the next byte into B and the XOR check.","comment":"One fewer"},
        "9695": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "9696": {"comment":"Into the check byte"},
        "9699": {"synopsis":"Tests ESC (returns with carry when pressed) and steps the address, paging on at $C000.","comment":"ESC?"},
        "9703": {"comment":"Bit 5 of STATUS, row $F7"},
        "9705": {"comment":"Pressed: carry"},
        "9707": {"comment":"The next address"},
        "9708": {"comment":"Past $BFFF?"},
        "9711": {"comment":"HMPR: the next page"},
        "9714": {"comment":"No"},
        "9716": {"comment":"Back to $8000"},
        "9718": {"comment":"The next page"},
        "9720": {"synopsis":"Starts the byte in B: E = it with a marker bit; B = the last half's wait less the time spent\nhere.","comment":"The byte to send"},
        "9721": {"comment":"Timing registers"},
        "9722": {"comment":"E = it"},
        "9723": {"comment":"The last half's count"},
        "9724": {"comment":"B = 1"},
        "9725": {"comment":"Less the byte's overhead"},
        "9727": {"comment":"Too short: wait 1"},
        "9729": {"comment":"B = C - $10"},
        "9731": {"comment":"A marker bit after the byte"},
        "9732": {"synopsis":"Shifts the byte's bit 7 out and finishes the last bit's second half.","comment":"Bit 7 to carry"},
        "9734": {"comment":"Finish the last half"},
        "9736": {"synopsis":"JSAVE's body (ROM0's jump table): saves a block on tape or the ROM's network (TAPE_SAVE),\nthen puts the border back and tests ESC.\nEntry: A = the flag byte; HL = the start; C, D, E = the length.\nExit: carry set when it was saved.\nError: 14 (ESC).","comment":"Save the block"},
        "9739": {"comment":"Carry: saved"},
        "9742": {"synopsis":"JLOAD's body (ROM0's jump table): loads (carry) or verifies a block from tape or the ROM's\nnetwork (TAPE_LOAD); falls into TAPE_END.\nEntry: carry = load; A = the flag byte; HL = the start; C, DE = the length.\nExit: carry set when it worked.\nError: 14 (ESC).","comment":"Load or verify the block"},
        "9745": {"synopsis":"Interrupts back on, the border from BORDCOL, ESC tested (error 14), keeping AF.","comment":"Interrupts back on"},
        "9746": {"comment":"Keep the result"},
        "9747": {"comment":"BORDCOL"},
        "9750": {"comment":"The border back"},
        "9752": {"comment":"ESC? Error 14"},
        "9755": {"comment":"The result back"},
        "9757": {"synopsis":"Loads or verifies a block from MIDI IN (the ROM's network): waits for the line to stay idle\nand a byte; until it is the flag byte asked for, waits again; then the bytes (NET_BLOCK with\nNET_GET_BYTE) and the check byte.\nEntry: the flag byte and the load carry on the stack (TAPE_LOAD's PUSH AF); HL = the start;\nC = 16K pages; DE = the rest.\nExit: carry set when the check byte matches.\nError: 19 when a byte does not come in time or differs (VERIFY).","comment":"The flag byte, carry: load"},
        "9758": {"comment":"B = the flag byte"},
        "9759": {"comment":"Carry kept in F'"},
        "9760": {"comment":"A = the flag byte"},
        "9761": {"synopsis":"Waits for the line to go idle, then for a byte.","comment":"Keep it"},
        "9762": {"comment":"Wait for the line to go idle"},
        "9765": {"synopsis":"Loop: until a byte comes.","comment":"A byte?"},
        "9768": {"comment":"Not yet"},
        "9770": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "9771": {"comment":"The flag byte"},
        "9772": {"comment":"This block's?"},
        "9773": {"comment":"No: wait for the next block"},
        "9775": {"comment":"Each byte: NET_GET_BYTE"},
        "9779": {"comment":"Receive the block"},
        "9782": {"comment":"The check byte"},
        "9785": {"synopsis":"Stops with error 19 when carry is clear (a timeout, or a VERIFY difference with no carry);\notherwise the check byte test.","comment":"Timed out: error 19"},
        "9788": {"comment":"The check"},
        "9791": {"comment":"Carry: it matches"},
        "9794": {"synopsis":"Called through IX for each byte saved: sends the byte at HL and adds it to the XOR check in\nH'.\nEntry: HL = the byte.","comment":"The byte"},
        "9795": {"comment":"Send it"},
        "9798": {"comment":"Into the check"},
        "9800": {"synopsis":"Called through IX for each byte loaded: reads a byte (error 19 on a timeout), stores it at\nHL (AF' carry) or compares it (error 19 when it differs), then adds it to the XOR check in\nH'.\nEntry: HL = where.","comment":"A byte"},
        "9803": {"comment":"Timed out: error 19"},
        "9805": {"comment":"Load?"},
        "9806": {"comment":"No: verify"},
        "9808": {"comment":"Load: store it"},
        "9812": {"synopsis":"VERIFY: compares the byte with the one at HL.","comment":"Verify"},
        "9813": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "9814": {"comment":"No: error 19"},
        "9816": {"synopsis":"Adds A to the XOR check in H'.","comment":"Into the check: H' xor A"},
        "9821": {"synopsis":"Loads or verifies a block from tape (the network: NET_LOAD). Finds a leader: 256 cycles each\nwithin a quarter of the running average (avg = (15 x avg + new) / 16); then the sync, a half\nshorter than 0.375 x the average followed by one under 0.75 x; then bytes, a bit a cycle:\ntoo long (1.25 x the average or more) fails, D or more is a 1. The first byte must be the\nflag byte (a 0 is taken as 1 with the length cut to 17, a Spectrum header); then the bytes\nare stored or compared, and the last is the check byte: the XOR of all must be 0. ESC\nreturns at once.\nEntry: A = the flag byte; carry = load; HL = the start (HMPR paged); C, DE = the length\n(pages, offset).\nExit: carry set when the block was loaded and checks.\nChanges: all, the alternate registers, TEMPW1, TEMPW2.","comment":"No interrupts"},
        "9822": {"comment":"Keep the flag byte"},
        "9823": {"comment":"Tape?"},
        "9826": {"comment":"No: the network"},
        "9828": {"comment":"The flag byte, carry: load"},
        "9829": {"comment":"C:DE as a linear count"},
        "9832": {"comment":"TEMPW1: the count's high part"},
        "9836": {"comment":"TEMPW2: the start"},
        "9839": {"comment":"For the counter"},
        "9840": {"comment":"The flag byte and carry in AF'"},
        "9841": {"comment":"Border 0, bit 3 set"},
        "9845": {"synopsis":"Starts the search: returns when ESC is pressed.","comment":"ESC?"},
        "9848": {"comment":"Yes: back"},
        "9849": {"synopsis":"Waits for four edges, takes the cycle as the average.","comment":"B: the level and border"},
        "9851": {"comment":"Two edges"},
        "9854": {"comment":"None? Again"},
        "9856": {"comment":"Two more"},
        "9859": {"comment":"None? Again"},
        "9861": {"comment":"The first count is the average"},
        "9866": {"comment":"L = 0: 256 cycles"},
        "9868": {"synopsis":"Loop: 256 steady cycles, each within a quarter of the running average.","comment":"A cycle"},
        "9871": {"comment":"None? Again"},
        "9873": {"comment":"HL = the average x 16"},
        "9880": {"comment":"x 15"},
        "9882": {"comment":"C = the new count"},
        "9883": {"comment":"+ the new count"},
        "9884": {"comment":"x 16"},
        "9888": {"comment":"L = the new average"},
        "9889": {"comment":"The difference"},
        "9891": {"comment":"Its size"},
        "9895": {"synopsis":"Compares 4 x the difference with the average.","comment":"x 4"},
        "9897": {"comment":"A quarter of the average or more?"},
        "9899": {"comment":"Yes: start again"},
        "9901": {"comment":"256 steady cycles?"},
        "9904": {"comment":"Border colour 2"},
        "9910": {"comment":"The thresholds"},
        "9911": {"comment":"The average"},
        "9912": {"comment":"/ 2"},
        "9914": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "9915": {"comment":"/ 4"},
        "9917": {"comment":"+ the average: 1.25 x"},
        "9918": {"comment":"E = the longest cycle"},
        "9919": {"comment":"D = the one/zero split"},
        "9924": {"comment":"1.5 x the average"},
        "9926": {"comment":"B = the count's high part"},
        "9930": {"comment":"+ 1"},
        "9932": {"comment":"H = 0.75 x the average"},
        "9935": {"synopsis":"Loop: waits for a short half after the leader (the sync).","comment":"Count from 0"},
        "9937": {"comment":"One edge"},
        "9940": {"comment":"0.75 x the average or more?"},
        "9941": {"comment":"Yes: start again"},
        "9943": {"comment":"Twice it"},
        "9944": {"comment":"Still a leader half?"},
        "9945": {"comment":"Yes: the next"},
        "9947": {"comment":"The sync's second edge"},
        "9950": {"comment":"Short enough?"},
        "9951": {"comment":"No: wait on"},
        "9953": {"comment":"Border colour 1"},
        "9958": {"comment":"HL' = the start"},
        "9962": {"comment":"The bytes"},
        "9964": {"synopsis":"The first byte: a 0 counts as 1 (a 17-byte block); it must be the flag byte asked for.","comment":"C = the load flag"},
        "9966": {"comment":"The flag byte read 0?"},
        "9968": {"comment":"No"},
        "9970": {"comment":"Taken as 1"},
        "9971": {"comment":"With a length of 17 bytes"},
        "9973": {"synopsis":"Returns NZ when the flag byte is not the one asked for; then keeps the load flag in carry'\nwith Z, so later bytes go to the store.","comment":"The flag byte expected?"},
        "9974": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "9975": {"comment":"The load flag"},
        "9976": {"comment":"To carry"},
