        "10239": {"comment":"As a count"},
        "10251": {"synopsis":"Makes the WORKSP, WKEND and KCUR pointers addressable with page A in HMPR (PTR_REL_PAGE_A on\neach). ROM0's ELINE_LINE_NUM calls it (RST $30) with ELINE's page; ROM1 $E7D9 calls it too.\nEntry: A = the page.\nExit: AF kept; HL at KCURP's entry.\nChanges: HL.","comment":"WORKSPP"},
        "10254": {"comment":"Relative to page A"},
        "10257": {"comment":"WKENDP"},
        "10262": {"comment":"KCURP, then falls into PTR_REL_PAGE_A"},
        "10264": {"synopsis":"Re-expresses the pointer whose page byte is at HL (the address word after it) for HMPR = A:\nwhen the page byte's bits 4-0 are not A, decrements the page byte and sets bit 6 of the\naddress's high byte, so the place is seen at $C000-$FFFF through page A.\nEntry: HL = the page byte; A = the page.\nExit: AF kept; HL = the high byte when it changed.\nChanges: HL.","comment":"Keep A"},
        "10265": {"comment":"Page byte's page the same as A?"},
        "10268": {"comment":"Yes: nothing to do"},
        "10270": {"comment":"One page lower"},
        "10271": {"comment":"To the address's high byte"},
        "10273": {"comment":"+ $4000: seen through the page before"},
        "10275": {"synopsis":"Puts AF back and returns."},
        "10277": {"synopsis":"After a block of the program moved: adjusts the pointers held in the entries from BSTKEND up\nto the $FF that ends them (ADJUST_PTR_HL on each, keeping each page byte's bits 7-5), then\nthe loop addresses of the FOR-NEXT variables (ADJUST_FOR_VARS through CALL_INLINE). ROM1\n$E7CF calls it.\nEntry: A = the page; BC = the first letter chain word for ADJUST_FOR_VARS; DE = the offset;\nAF' carry, TEMPW4/TEMPW5 as ADJUST_PTR_HL wants.\nExit: A = the page; DE kept.\nChanges: AF', BC, HL, IY.","comment":"Keep BC (popped as HL at the end)"},
        "10278": {"comment":"C = the page"},
        "10279": {"comment":"BSTKEND"},
        "10282": {"synopsis":"The next entry: $FF ends them.","comment":"The entry's type/page byte"},
        "10283": {"comment":"$FF: the end?"},
        "10285": {"comment":"No: an entry"},
        "10287": {"comment":"HL = the chain word passed in BC"},
        "10289": {"comment":"TEMPW3 = the offset"},
        "10293": {"comment":"D = the page"},
        "10294": {"comment":"The direction flag back in F"},
        "10295": {"comment":"ADJUST_FOR_VARS, ROM1 out"},
        "10300": {"comment":"Flag back to F'"},
        "10302": {"comment":"A = the page"},
        "10304": {"synopsis":"Adjusts one entry's pointer, keeps its type bits 7-5, steps 4 bytes; an entry of type $40 is\nfollowed by bytes up to a zero word, skipped by BSTK_SKIP_DATA.","comment":"Keep the original byte"},
        "10306": {"comment":"ADJUST_PTR_HL on this pointer"},
        "10311": {"comment":"The original's bits 7-5"},
