        "10325": {"synopsis":"Skips the bytes after a type $40 entry up to and past a zero word.","comment":"A zero word?"},
        "10330": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "10331": {"comment":"The next entry"},
        "10333": {"synopsis":"JSENDA's body: sends A to the parallel printer. Waits while bit 0 of the status port (C of\nLPTPRTI) is set, stopping with error 14 if ESC is pressed (ESC_STOP_14); writes A to the\nport below it, then writes B and B-1 to the status port (the strobe).\nEntry: A = the byte; LPTPRTI = the status port (C) and the strobe value (B).\nExit: BC, AF kept.\nError: stops with error code 14 on ESC."},
        "10335": {"comment":"LPTPRTI: C = status port, B = strobe value"},
        "10339": {"synopsis":"Waits for the printer: bit 0 of the status port clear.","comment":"ESC pressed? Stops with error code 14"},
        "10342": {"comment":"The status"},
        "10344": {"comment":"Bit 0 set: busy?"},
        "10347": {"comment":"The data port"},
        "10349": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "10351": {"comment":"Back to the status port"},
        "10352": {"comment":"Strobe on"},
        "10354": {"comment":"And off"},
        "10359": {"synopsis":"JHEAPROOM's body: reserves BC bytes of the heap by moving HEAPEND up (BC positive) or gives\nthem back (BC negative). An end below $4000 is clamped to HPST, the heap's start; an end\nthat would reach BSTKEND fails.\nEntry: BC = the bytes.\nExit: carry set when it worked, DE = the old HEAPEND; carry clear: no room, nothing changed.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"HEAPEND"},
        "10362": {"comment":"The new end"},
        "10363": {"comment":"Below $4000 (given back past the start)?"},
        "10366": {"comment":"No: check the room"},
        "10368": {"comment":"Yes: back to HPST, the heap's start"},
        "10373": {"synopsis":"A new end in RAM: it must stay below BSTKEND.","comment":"BSTKEND"},
        "10377": {"comment":"Would it reach BSTKEND?"},
        "10379": {"comment":"Yes: no room, carry clear"},
        "10380": {"comment":"The new end back"},
        "10381": {"synopsis":"Stores the new HEAPEND, returning the old one in DE.","comment":"DE = the old HEAPEND"},
        "10385": {"comment":"HEAPEND = the new end"},
        "10389": {"synopsis":"INSTR's body (function code $2F): INSTR([start,] a$, b$) finds b$ in a$ from the start\n(default: stack constant 9 put under the first string) and stacks the position, 0 when not\nfound. The pattern goes to the buffer at $4F00; the byte at $5A05 is the character that\nmatches anything (C' for FIND_PATTERN).\nExit: the position on the calculator stack (running); HMPR put back.\nError: stops with error code 4 when the start is 0; 27 for an empty or too long pattern; 29\nfor bad syntax.","comment":"'(', past it"},
        "10392": {"comment":"The first item, either kind"},
        "10395": {"comment":"A number: the start"},
        "10397": {"comment":"Checking syntax: no start to stack"},
        "10405": {"synopsis":"A number came first (the start): a comma and the string to search.","comment":"A comma and the string to search"},
        "10408": {"synopsis":"The comma, the pattern string and ')'; when running, searches.","comment":"A comma, the pattern and ')'"},
        "10411": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "10412": {"comment":"Keep HMPR"},
        "10415": {"comment":"The pattern to $4F00"},
        "10418": {"comment":"Keep its length"},
        "10419": {"comment":"The text: DE = address, BC = length"},
        "10424": {"comment":"The start"},
        "10427": {"comment":"Start 0?"},
        "10428": {"comment":"Yes: stops with error code 4"},
        "10431": {"comment":"The character that matches anything"},
        "10435": {"comment":"Into C'"},
        "10437": {"comment":"Positions to skip"},
        "10438": {"comment":"HL = the text's length"},
        "10439": {"comment":"DE = the text"},
        "10440": {"comment":"A = the pattern's length"},
        "10444": {"comment":"The HMPR value kept at $E8AC"},
        "10445": {"comment":"HMPR back, BC stacked"},
        "10448": {"synopsis":"Searches the BC-1 skipped text for the pattern: the text is HL bytes at DE (paged in at\n$8000), the pattern A bytes at $4F00. Returns with carry and BC = 0 when the pattern is\nempty or does not fit after the start; texts of $3F00 positions or more are searched in\npieces of $3EFF.\nEntry: A = the pattern's length; BC = the start - 1; DE = the text; HL = its length; HMPR at\nthe text.\nExit: found: no carry, BC = the position; not found: carry, BC = 0 (as FIND_PATTERN).\nChanges: all.","comment":"Keep the start - 1"},
        "10449": {"comment":"BC = the pattern's length"},
        "10452": {"comment":"An empty pattern?"},
        "10453": {"comment":"Yes: not found"},
        "10456": {"comment":"Room for the pattern?"},
        "10459": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "10461": {"comment":"Positions it can start at"},
        "10462": {"comment":"Less the skipped ones"},
        "10464": {"synopsis":"No room for the pattern after the start: not found.","comment":"None left: not found"},
        "10467": {"comment":"DE = the positions to try"},
        "10469": {"comment":"The pattern's length into AF'"},
        "10470": {"comment":"The first position to try"},
        "10471": {"comment":"Past $FFFF: next page"},
        "10474": {"synopsis":"Searches the next piece: positions over $3EFF go in pieces of $3EFF, HL kept in $8000-$BFFF\n(NORM_HL).","comment":"HL back below $C000, next page in"},
        "10477": {"comment":"Positions in D"},
        "10478": {"comment":"Fewer than $3F00?"},
        "10480": {"comment":"Yes: one search"},
        "10482": {"comment":"Keep the count"},
        "10483": {"comment":"A piece of $3EFF positions"},
        "10486": {"comment":"Search it"},
        "10489": {"comment":"Found"},
        "10491": {"comment":"The next piece's start"},
        "10496": {"comment":"The count back, the start kept"},
        "10497": {"comment":"Positions left"},
        "10500": {"comment":"BC = the next start"},
        "10501": {"comment":"Search on"},
        "10503": {"synopsis":"Calls FIND_PATTERN with the pattern's length from AF' and BC (its base) through BCSTORE,\nkeeping AF'.","comment":"The pattern's length back in A"},
        "10504": {"comment":"Keep it"},
        "10505": {"comment":"BCSTORE: CALL_INLINE's BC"},
        "10509": {"comment":"FIND_PATTERN, ROM1 out"},
        "10514": {"synopsis":"Puts the pattern's length back in AF' and returns FIND_PATTERN's result.","comment":"Keep the result's flags"},
        "10515": {"comment":"The pattern's length"},
        "10516": {"comment":"Back into AF'"},
        "10518": {"synopsis":"LENGTH's body (function code $25): LENGTH(n, name) for a variable, found and recorded by\nSAVE_VAR_LOC (through CALL_INLINE): n = 0 stacks its address as a page-relative number\n(STK_PAGE_REL); for a string or an array, n = 1 stacks a string's length or an array's first\ndimension, n = 2 an array's second dimension (1 when it has one).\nExit: the number on the calculator stack (running).\nError: stops with error code 2 when the variable does not exist, 30 for another n, 29 for\nbad syntax.","comment":"'(', past it"},
        "10521": {"comment":"n"},
        "10524": {"comment":"A comma"},
        "10527": {"comment":"Finds the name, records it at $5121"},
        "10532": {"comment":"Not there: stops with error code 2"},
        "10535": {"comment":"The character after the name"},
        "10536": {"comment":"')', carry when running"},
        "10539": {"comment":"Running flag to AF'"},
        "10540": {"comment":"A numeric array (type bit 5)?"},
        "10542": {"comment":"No"},
        "10544": {"comment":"Yet another ')' check"},
        "10548": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "10549": {"comment":"Size info"},
        "10551": {"synopsis":"Not a numeric array: checking syntax ends here; a sign flag clear goes to LENGTH_INFO, set\n(probably a simple numeric variable) allows only n = 0.","comment":"Running flag back"},
        "10552": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "10553": {"comment":"Sign clear: size info"},
        "10556": {"comment":"n"},
        "10559": {"comment":"Only 0 allowed"},
        "10560": {"comment":"Otherwise stops with error code 30"},
        "10562": {"comment":"The variable's address"},
        "10565": {"synopsis":"Stacks the address HL with the page at $5123 as a page-relative number.","comment":"Its HMPR value"},
        "10569": {"comment":"Stacks B:HL as a number"},
        "10572": {"synopsis":"Reads the size from the 7 bytes SAVE_VAR_LOC copied to $5124: a string's 3-byte length, or\nan array's dimension count and sizes.","comment":"Keep the type"},
        "10573": {"comment":"n"},
        "10577": {"comment":"The bytes recorded from the variable"},
        "10580": {"comment":"Keep n"},
        "10581": {"comment":"The type"},
        "10582": {"comment":"An array (bit 5 or 6)?"},
        "10584": {"comment":"A string: the pages part of the length"},
        "10586": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "10588": {"comment":"Array"},
        "10590": {"comment":"Pages into bits 7-6"},
        "10592": {"comment":"With the high byte bits"},
        "10593": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "10594": {"synopsis":"DE = 1: no second dimension."},
        "10599": {"synopsis":"An array: A = the dimension count, BC = the first size, DE = the second.","comment":"The dimension count"},
        "10601": {"comment":"First size"},
        "10605": {"comment":"One dimension?"},
        "10608": {"comment":"Second size"},
        "10612": {"synopsis":"HL = the address of the size's bytes in the variable itself (from $5121).","comment":"Offset of the size's bytes ($5124 + ...)"},
        "10615": {"comment":"The variable's address"},
        "10618": {"comment":"Plus that offset"},
        "10623": {"synopsis":"Stacks what n asks for: 0 the address, 1 BC, 2 DE.","comment":"n"},
        "10624": {"comment":"0: the address"},
        "10627": {"comment":"1?"},
        "10628": {"comment":"Yes: BC"},
        "10631": {"comment":"HL = the second size"},
        "10632": {"comment":"2?"},
        "10633": {"comment":"Yes: stack it"},
        "10636": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 30: n out of range.","comment":"Stops with error code 30"},
        "10638": {"synopsis":"STRING$'s body (function code $36): STRING$(n, a$) builds a$ repeated n times in the buffer\nat $4F00 and stacks a copy (STK_STR_COPY). An empty result goes to STRING_EMPTY.\nExit: the string on the calculator stack (running).\nError: stops with error code 42 when the result is $200 bytes or more, 27 when a$ is empty\nor over 255 characters (STR_TO_BUFFER), 30 for n over 255.","comment":"'(', n, a comma, a$ and ')'"},
        "10641": {"comment":"Checking syntax: done"},
        "10642": {"comment":"a$ to memory 0; n, n, a$, a$"},
        "10647": {"comment":"calc $51 on a$, probably its length"},
        "10648": {"comment":"n, a$, n, length"},
        "10649": {"comment":"n x length"},
        "10651": {"comment":"The result's length"},
        "10654": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "10657": {"comment":"$200 bytes or more?"},
        "10660": {"comment":"Yes: stops with error code 42"},
        "10663": {"comment":"Keep the length"},
        "10664": {"comment":"a$ to $4F00"},
        "10669": {"comment":"n"},
        "10672": {"comment":"HL = $4F00"},
        "10673": {"comment":"DE = $4F00 too (moved by LDIR)"},
        "10675": {"comment":"BC = a$'s length"},
        "10676": {"synopsis":"Copies a$ once more after the copies so far; A counts them."},
        "10678": {"comment":"One more copy"},
        "10682": {"comment":"More?"},
        "10685": {"comment":"The total length"},
        "10686": {"comment":"Copies it to the workspace and stacks it"},
        "10689": {"synopsis":"An empty result: drops both values and stacks BC (0) through STK_BC.","comment":"Drop, drop"},
        "10693": {"comment":"Stacks 0"},
        "10696": {"synopsis":"Takes a point off the calculator stack (GET_PLOT_COORDS through CALL_INLINE). Thin pixels,\nand CURCMD + MODE = $ED (FILL, token $EB, in MODE 3), split x into TEMPW1 and C\n(THIN_X_WINDOW; for the second, x is doubled first). ROM0's CIRCLE_AT_R and FILL_SET_FLAG\ncall it.\nEntry: x and y on the calculator stack.\nExit: B = the row; carry clear: C = x; carry set: C = x - TEMPW1 (0-255), TEMPW1 = the rest.\nError: as GET_PLOT_COORDS.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The point, ROM1 out"},
        "10701": {"comment":"Thin pixels?"},
        "10703": {"comment":"CURCMD"},
        "10706": {"comment":"+ MODE"},
        "10710": {"comment":"$ED (FILL in MODE 3)?"},
        "10712": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "10714": {"comment":"No: C = x"},
        "10715": {"comment":"HL = x x 2"},
        "10718": {"synopsis":"Splits a 0-511 x in HL: x < 128 gives C = x, TEMPW1 = 0; 128-383 gives C = 128, TEMPW1 = x -\n128; 384-511 gives C = x - 256, TEMPW1 = 256.\nEntry: HL = x.\nExit: carry set; C + TEMPW1 = x.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.","comment":"x 256 or more?"},
        "10723": {"comment":"Under 128?"},
        "10725": {"comment":"Yes: as it is"},
        "10729": {"synopsis":"x is 256 or more.","comment":"x - 256 under 128?"},
        "10731": {"comment":"Yes: 128 to the window"},
        "10733": {"synopsis":"C = the low byte, TEMPW1 = the high byte x 256.","comment":"C = the low byte"},
        "10734": {"comment":"TEMPW1 = H x 256"},
        "10738": {"synopsis":"C = 128, TEMPW1 = x - 128.","comment":"128"},
        "10741": {"comment":"C = 128"},
        "10743": {"comment":"TEMPW1 = x - 128"},
        "10745": {"synopsis":"Stores TEMPW1 and returns with carry.","comment":"TEMPW1"},
        "10748": {"comment":"Carry: thin pixels"},
        "10750": {"synopsis":"Builds at $4D00 an unrolled chain of A pairs RLD / DEC L (C = 1) or RRD / INC L (other C),\nended by RET: ROM0's ROLL_SCROLL_ADDR runs it to shift a row by a nibble.\nEntry: A = the count; C = the direction.\nExit: BC = $00xx; DE, HL kept.\nChanges: AF, B, C."},
        "10752": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "10753": {"comment":"RRD ($ED $67), INC L ($2C)"},
        "10756": {"comment":"Direction 1?"},
        "10759": {"comment":"RLD ($ED $6F), DEC L ($2D)"},
        "10762": {"synopsis":"Writes the chain."},
        "10764": {"comment":"Where the chain is built"},
        "10767": {"synopsis":"One $ED, op, step triple.","comment":"$ED prefix"},
        "10769": {"comment":"RLD or RRD"},
        "10771": {"comment":"INC L or DEC L"},
        "10775": {"comment":"RET ends it"},
        "10780": {"synopsis":"Builds at $4D00 an unrolled chain of A LDI (C = 1) or LDD (other C) instructions, ended by\nRET. The LD C,$C5 at $EA22 hides a second entry at $EA23 (PUSH BC), called by ROM0's\nVERT_MOVE, SCROLL_WIN_M1 and GRAB_BLOCK, which always builds LDIs. ROM0's ROLL_BYTES calls\n$EA1C.\nEntry: A = the count; C = the direction.\nExit: BC, HL kept.\nChanges: AF."},
        "10781": {"comment":"Direction 1?"},
        "10782": {"comment":"LDD"},
        "10784": {"comment":"No: LDD"},
        "10786": {"comment":"Hides $EA23: PUSH BC"},
        "10788": {"comment":"LDI"},
        "10790": {"synopsis":"C = the second byte ($A0 LDI or $A8 LDD): writes A of them."},
        "10791": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "10792": {"comment":"$ED prefix"},
        "10794": {"comment":"Where the chain is built"},
        "10797": {"synopsis":"One $ED, C pair."},
        "10799": {"comment":"LDI or LDD"},
        "10803": {"comment":"RET ends it"},
        "10808": {"synopsis":"DRAW TO x,y,a with an angle (ROM0's DRAW_TO_ARCQ jumps here): stacks the distance to the end\npoint as dx and dy, written straight at STKEND through $CBBC with signs from the steps\n(right and up positive; x from HL with thin pixels, else C), recalls the angle from memory 0\nand goes on as the relative arc.\nEntry: B = |dy|, D = the row step; C or HL = |dx|, E = the x step; Z when THFATT is 0 (thin\npixels).\nExit: as ARC_REL.","comment":"THFATT: Z for thin pixels"},
        "10812": {"comment":"The x step"},
        "10813": {"comment":"Right (1) gives $FF: positive"},
        "10815": {"comment":"E = |dy|"},
        "10816": {"comment":"Keep the row step and |dy|"},
        "10817": {"comment":"Thin: DE = |dx| (16 bits)"},
        "10818": {"comment":"Thin?"},
        "10820": {"comment":"No: DE = C"},
        "10823": {"synopsis":"Stacks dx then dy at STKEND and moves STKEND past them.","comment":"STKEND"},
        "10826": {"comment":"dx at STKEND, sign from A"},
        "10829": {"comment":"Past the value"},
        "10831": {"comment":"D = the row step"},
        "10832": {"comment":"Up ($FF) gives positive"},
        "10833": {"comment":"DE = |dy|"},
        "10835": {"comment":"dy after it"},
        "10838": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "10840": {"comment":"New STKEND"},
        "10843": {"comment":"The angle from memory 0"},
        "10846": {"synopsis":"Draws an arc by dx, dy turning through the angle a (DRAW x,y,a; ROM0's DRAW_CMD_ARGS jumps\nhere):\n1. With the calculator (memories 0-5; ABS $41, SQR $43 and NEGATE $5D among the operations),\n   works out the segment count from the size and angle; a case the $1E conditional jumps\n   pick out draws a straight line (ARC_STRAIGHT).\n2. The count n (CALC_POP_BYTE) becomes (n AND $FC) + 4, 252 when over 255 or when that is\n   256.\n3. A small step (exponent under $81) draws one line (ARC_LINE_OUT).\n4. Each segment's end is turned into a step from XCOORD/YCOORD and drawn with DRAW_REL_STACK\n   (ARC_STEP_DRAW); the last line goes to the exact end (ARC_LAST_LINE).\nEntry: dx, dy and a on the calculator stack.\nExit: HMPR put back ($3FC6).\nError: as DRAW_REL_STACK.\nChanges: all."},
        "10847": {"comment":"-a into memory 5"},
        "10854": {"comment":"Calc $1E: a conditional jump to ARC_STRAIGHT"},
        "10876": {"comment":"Calc $1E: a conditional jump to ARC_CALC_MORE"},
        "10879": {"synopsis":"Calculator bytes: drop two values, end; then a straight line (ARC_LINE_OUT)."},
        "10881": {"comment":"A straight line"},
        "10884": {"synopsis":"Calculator bytes the $1E jump at $EA7C lands on (the decoder reads them as code): $25 $43\n$26 $02 $06 $05 $DD $06 $05 $41 $33 (duplicate, SQR, ...), ended by $33; then CALC_POP_BYTE\ntakes the segment count."},
        "10895": {"comment":"The segment count"},
        "10898": {"comment":"252 when over 255"},
        "10902": {"comment":"A multiple of 4"},
        "10903": {"comment":"Plus 4"},
        "10905": {"comment":"256: 252"},
        "10907": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "10908": {"synopsis":"B = the segment count: sets up the per-segment values in memories 1-5.","comment":"Keep the count"},
        "10979": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "10980": {"comment":"The step's exponent"},
        "10981": {"comment":"Under 1?"},
        "10983": {"comment":"Yes: one line"},
        "10988": {"comment":"XCOORD"},
        "10994": {"comment":"YCOORD"},
        "11002": {"comment":"More segments?"},
        "11004": {"comment":"No: the last line"},
        "11006": {"synopsis":"The next segment: turns memories 1-4 on by one step (a rotation)."},
        "11024": {"synopsis":"Turns the segment's end into dx, dy from XCOORD and YCOORD and draws it (DRAW_REL_STACK);\nloops with B."},
        "11029": {"comment":"XCOORD"},
        "11038": {"comment":"YCOORD"},
        "11044": {"comment":"Keep the count"},
        "11045": {"comment":"Draws the segment"},
        "11051": {"comment":"The next segment"},
        "11053": {"synopsis":"After the segments: drops two values and stacks the step from XCOORD/YCOORD to the end\npoint."},
        "11057": {"comment":"XCOORD"},
        "11062": {"comment":"YCOORD"},
        "11068": {"synopsis":"Draws the line on the calculator stack (DRAW_REL_STACK) and puts HMPR back.","comment":"Draws the line"},
        "11073": {"comment":"HMPR back and return"},
        "11076": {"synopsis":"CALL's body (token $E4): CALL address [, item ...]. When running, each item is stacked with\nFLAGS (its type) under the address, so the address stays on top; TEMPB3 = the item count.\nThen runs the code through CALL_CODE (JUMP_INLINE).\nEntry: the BASIC pointer after CALL.\nExit: as the code leaves it.\nError: 29 for bad syntax.","comment":"The address"},
        "11079": {"comment":"No items yet"},
        "11081": {"synopsis":"Another item after a comma, or the end of the statement.","comment":"The end of the statement?"},
        "11084": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11086": {"comment":"A comma"},
        "11090": {"comment":"The item, either kind"},
        "11094": {"comment":"Count it"},
        "11095": {"comment":"Checking syntax: the next"},
        "11097": {"comment":"FLAGS: bit 6 says number or string"},
        "11101": {"comment":"Item, address: swap, stack B (FLAGS), swap"},
        "11108": {"synopsis":"Stores the count in TEMPB3 and runs the code.","comment":"The item count"},
        "11109": {"comment":"TEMPB3"},
        "11112": {"comment":"Checking syntax: return"},
        "11115": {"comment":"Runs the code, ROM1 out"},
        "11120": {"synopsis":"Sets the numeric variables error, lino and stat to ERRNR, PPC and SUBPPC (SET_VAR_BYTE /\nSET_VAR_WORD). ROM0 calls it (RST $30 at $0F36, MAIN_RESET_RUN) before an ON ERROR handler\nruns.\nExit: through ASSIGN_NUM_TYPE.\nChanges: all.","comment":"ERRNR"},
        "11123": {"comment":"\"error\""},
        "11129": {"comment":"PPC"},
        "11132": {"comment":"\"lino\""},
        "11138": {"comment":"SUBPPC"},
        "11141": {"comment":"\"stat\", then falls into SET_VAR_BYTE"},
        "11144": {"synopsis":"SET_VAR_WORD with HL = A."},
        "11147": {"synopsis":"Assigns HL to the numeric variable whose type byte and name are at DE: stacks HL (STK_HL),\ncopies the 6 bytes to $513F and goes on in ROM0's ASSIGN_NUM_TYPE (JUMP_INLINE) with A = the\ntype byte.\nEntry: HL = the value; DE = the type byte and name.\nExit: as ASSIGN_NUM_TYPE.\nChanges: all.","comment":"Keep the name"},
        "11148": {"comment":"Stacks the value"},
        "11151": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "11152": {"comment":"Where ASSIGN_NUM_TYPE reads it"},
        "11155": {"comment":"A = the type byte"},
        "11156": {"comment":"Type byte and up to 5 letters"},
        "11161": {"comment":"Assigns it, ROM1 out"},
        "11166": {"synopsis":"The variable \"error\": type byte $04 (a 5-letter name), then its letters."},
        "11172": {"synopsis":"The variable \"lino\": type byte $03, then its letters."},
        "11177": {"synopsis":"The variable \"stat\": type byte $03, then its letters."},
        "11182": {"synopsis":"The reset goes on here from ROM0's RESET_WAIT (LMPR = $5F):\n1. IM 1, I = 0. Tests the RAM a page at a time from page 0 (HMPR, CLUT 0 = page x 8 shows\n   the progress): clears the page, then writes $FF and 0 every 256 bytes and reads them\n   back. The first page that fails ends the count; when all 32 pass, a key on bit 0 of port\n   $FEFE held down makes it 16.\n2. PRAMTP = pages - 1; VMPR = that page. SP = $4F00. ALLOCT: 0 for each page, $FF for the\n   missing ones, $40 for pages 0-3, $C0 for the last two (the screen; FISCRNP = their first\n   page + $60). LASTPAGE = RAMTOPP = 3, RAMTOP = $BFFF.\n3. Copies the start-up tables from ROM1: $D2 bytes from $FC69 to $58E1, patches\n   (BYTE_STEP_LIST from $FD3B at $59CE), PROG = $9CD5, CHANS = $5CB6 with $1F bytes from\n   $FC4A, then $44 bytes from $FBDE to $5800, $12 to $5A00 and $1A to $5BC6.\n4. NMIV = NMI_BREAK, ANYIV = INT_DEFAULT; expands the font (FONT_EXPAND); CHARS = $5090, UDG\n   = $5510; goes on at NEW_INIT.\nEntry: none.\nExit: does not return.","comment":"A = 0: the first page"},
        "11185": {"comment":"Interrupt mode 1"},
        "11187": {"synopsis":"Tests page A: pages it in, clears it, then checks every 256th byte.","comment":"Port $F8 with B = 0: CLUT 0"},
        "11190": {"comment":"D = the page"},
        "11191": {"comment":"x 8"},
        "11194": {"comment":"CLUT 0 shows the page under test"},
        "11197": {"comment":"HMPR: the page at $8000"},
        "11199": {"comment":"Clears $8000-$BFFF"},
        "11211": {"comment":"Back to the start"},
        "11214": {"comment":"BC = 256: the step"},
        "11215": {"comment":"64 checks in the page"},
        "11217": {"synopsis":"Writes $FF and 0 at HL and reads each back; a mismatch ends the count.","comment":"Write $FF"},
        "11219": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11220": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "11221": {"comment":"No: RAM ends here"},
        "11223": {"comment":"Write 0"},
        "11224": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11226": {"comment":"0?"},
        "11227": {"comment":"No: RAM ends here"},
        "11229": {"comment":"256 bytes on"},
        "11230": {"comment":"More in the page?"},
        "11233": {"comment":"The next page"},
        "11234": {"comment":"All 32?"},
        "11236": {"comment":"No: test it"},
        "11238": {"comment":"Keyboard row of port $FEFE"},
        "11242": {"comment":"Bit 0: a key held?"},
        "11243": {"comment":"16 pages"},
        "11245": {"comment":"Held: 16"},
        "11247": {"comment":"Otherwise 32"},
        "11248": {"synopsis":"A = the page count: sets PRAMTP and VMPR, then builds ALLOCT from $5100 and the screen\npages.","comment":"B = the page count"},
        "11249": {"comment":"The last page"},
        "11250": {"comment":"E = the last page"},
        "11251": {"comment":"PRAMTP"},
        "11254": {"comment":"VMPR: the screen on the last page"},
        "11256": {"comment":"A stack under $4F00"},
        "11259": {"comment":"ALLOCT"},
        "11262": {"comment":"Keep its start"},
        "11263": {"synopsis":"ALLOCT: 0 for each page there is.","comment":"0: a page there is"},
        "11268": {"comment":"$21 - the page count left over"},
        "11272": {"synopsis":"ALLOCT: $FF for the pages that are not there (to 33 bytes).","comment":"$FF: no page"},
        "11277": {"comment":"Back to ALLOCT"},
        "11278": {"comment":"$40: the system's pages"},
        "11280": {"comment":"Pages 0-3"},
        "11282": {"synopsis":"ALLOCT: $40 for pages 0-3."},
        "11286": {"comment":"L = 4"},
        "11287": {"comment":"3"},
        "11288": {"comment":"LASTPAGE"},
        "11291": {"comment":"RAMTOPP"},
        "11294": {"comment":"L = the last page"},
        "11295": {"comment":"The page before it"},
        "11297": {"comment":"Mode 4 bits"},
        "11299": {"comment":"FISCRNP: the first screen's page and mode"},
        "11302": {"comment":"$C0: a screen page"},
        "11304": {"comment":"The page before the last"},
        "11306": {"comment":"And the last"},
        "11307": {"comment":"RAMTOP = $BFFF"},
        "11313": {"comment":"The table at ROM1 $FC69"},
        "11316": {"comment":"Just past RHTAB"},
        "11319": {"comment":"$D2 bytes"},
        "11323": {"comment":"DE = the patch list's place in ROM1"},
        "11324": {"comment":"Patches from $59CE"},
        "11330": {"comment":"PROG"},
        "11336": {"comment":"CHANS"},
        "11343": {"comment":"The channel table"},
        "11346": {"comment":"$1F bytes"},
        "11350": {"comment":"Start-up values from ROM1 $FBDE"},
        "11353": {"comment":"To $5800"},
        "11356": {"comment":"$44 bytes"},
        "11360": {"comment":"$12 bytes to $5A00"},
        "11367": {"comment":"$1A bytes to $5BC6"},
        "11374": {"comment":"NMIV = NMI_BREAK"},
        "11380": {"comment":"ANYIV = INT_DEFAULT"},
        "11386": {"comment":"Expands the font"},
        "11389": {"comment":"CHARS = $5090"},
        "11395": {"comment":"UDG = $5510"},
        "11401": {"comment":"The rest as NEW"},
        "11403": {"synopsis":"NEW's body (token $AF): when running, disables interrupts and falls into NEW_INIT.\nEntry: A = the character after NEW.\nExit: does not return (stops with error code 80).","comment":"Checking syntax: return"},
        "11407": {"synopsis":"Puts the system back as after a reset (also the reset's last part):\n1. The screen list SCLIST: SCPTR = $5CA0; FISCRNP's screen in CUSCRNP and VMPR, then 15 $FF\n   entries. Frees the other screens' pages (ALLOCT $C0 -> 0, below the first screen).\n2. STREAMS: the nine values from ROM0 $028B, each with 0, then 24 zero bytes.\n3. An empty program ($FF at PROG), NVARS just after it, RESTORE_START; REPDEL $21, REPSPD 3;\n   MEM = $5121; ERRSOUND, SPEEDIC and THFATT $51; THFATP and MODE 0; RESET_VARS, ELINE past\n   SAVARS, CLEAR_ELINE.\n4. Mode 4 (JMODE with 3), the colours and palette (RESET_COLOURS), SP = $4F00 with\n   MAIN_REPORT as the error return (ERRSP).\n5. The line palette table at $5600: 16 entries, lines 0, 11, ..., 165, CLUT 0 set to the\n   default palette's colours 1-16 (the start-up colour bars), ended by $FF.\n6. Stops with error code 80.\nEntry: none.\nExit: does not return.","comment":"SCLIST"},
        "11410": {"comment":"SCPTR"},
        "11413": {"comment":"FISCRNP"},
        "11415": {"comment":"CUSCRNP"},
        "11418": {"comment":"VMPR: the first screen"},
        "11420": {"comment":"16 entries"},
        "11422": {"synopsis":"SCLIST: the first screen, then $FF for the other 15 entries."},
        "11423": {"comment":"The first screen, then $FF"},
        "11428": {"comment":"PRAMTP"},
        "11431": {"comment":"The page below the first screen"},
        "11434": {"comment":"ALLOCT"},
        "11436": {"synopsis":"Frees an ALLOCT entry of $C0 (a screen page).","comment":"A screen page?"},
        "11441": {"comment":"Yes: free it (B = 0)"},
        "11442": {"synopsis":"The page below, down to page 1.","comment":"Down to page 1"},
        "11445": {"comment":"C = 0"},
        "11446": {"comment":"STREAMS"},
        "11449": {"comment":"Start-up values in ROM0"},
        "11452": {"comment":"Nine"},
        "11454": {"synopsis":"STREAMS: a value from ROM0 $028B, then C (0).","comment":"The value"},
        "11458": {"comment":"Then 0"},
        "11462": {"comment":"24 more bytes"},
        "11464": {"synopsis":"The rest of STREAMS: 0.","comment":"0"},
        "11468": {"comment":"HL = PROG, A = its page"},
        "11471": {"comment":"An empty program"},
        "11474": {"comment":"NVARS just past it"},
        "11477": {"comment":"NVARSP"},
        "11480": {"comment":"ELINEP"},
        "11483": {"comment":"RESTORE to the start"},
        "11486": {"comment":"REPDEL $21, REPSPD 3"},
        "11492": {"comment":"MEM = $5121"},
        "11498": {"comment":"A = $51"},
        "11499": {"comment":"ERRSOUND"},
        "11502": {"comment":"SPEEDIC"},
        "11505": {"comment":"THFATT"},
        "11509": {"comment":"THFATP = 0"},
        "11512": {"comment":"MODE = 0"},
        "11515": {"comment":"An empty variables area"},
        "11518": {"comment":"SAVARS"},
        "11522": {"comment":"ELINE just past it"},
        "11525": {"comment":"Empties the edit line"},
        "11528": {"comment":"Mode 4"},
        "11533": {"comment":"Colours and palette"},
        "11536": {"comment":"A fresh stack"},
        "11539": {"comment":"MAIN_REPORT: where errors return"},
        "11543": {"comment":"ERRSP"},
        "11547": {"comment":"The default palette's colour 1"},
        "11550": {"comment":"The line palette table"},
        "11553": {"comment":"B = line 0, C = CLUT 0"},
        "11555": {"synopsis":"One line palette entry: line B, CLUT 0, a colour twice; lines 11 apart to 165.","comment":"The line"},
        "11557": {"comment":"The CLUT entry"},
        "11559": {"comment":"The colour"},
        "11561": {"comment":"Both colours the same"},
        "11565": {"comment":"11 lines on"},
        "11569": {"comment":"Past line 165?"},
        "11573": {"comment":"Ends the table"},
        "11575": {"comment":"Stops with error code 80"},
        "11577": {"synopsis":"Expands the font from ROM1 $FE4E into RAM at $5190 (CHARS + 256, character 32 on): 99\ncharacters of 7 rows of 5 bits each, read as one bit stream (a set bit after the last makes\nthe end of each byte); each row is stored shifted left by 1 (bits 5-1) and an eighth row of\n0 is added. Then sets bit 6 of rows 1-5 of character 127 and applies the patch list at ROM1\n$FE33 from $51F7 (BYTE_STEP_LIST).\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL past the last patch.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, HL'.","comment":"H' = 99 characters, L' = 7 rows"},
        "11581": {"comment":"The packed font"},
        "11584": {"comment":"Character 32 in RAM"},
        "11587": {"comment":"The row"},
        "11588": {"comment":"5 bits"},
        "11590": {"synopsis":"Loads the next source byte with a marker bit after it.","comment":"The next source byte"},
        "11592": {"comment":"The marker bit"},
        "11593": {"synopsis":"Shifts the next bit into A; the marker leaving C means a new byte.","comment":"Next bit; marker out with C = 0?"},
        "11595": {"comment":"Yes: the next byte"},
        "11597": {"comment":"Into the row"},
        "11598": {"comment":"More bits?"},
        "11600": {"comment":"Bits 5-1"},
        "11601": {"comment":"Stores the row"},
        "11603": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "11606": {"comment":"Rows left in the character"},
        "11611": {"comment":"The eighth row: 0"},
        "11614": {"comment":"7 rows again"},
        "11616": {"comment":"Characters left"},
        "11620": {"comment":"Character 127, row 1"},
        "11623": {"synopsis":"Sets bit 6 of B rows from HL.","comment":"One more pixel at the left"},
        "11628": {"comment":"The patch list in ROM1"},
        "11631": {"comment":"Into the font from $51F7"},
        "11634": {"synopsis":"Stores a list of byte, step pairs from DE: each byte at HL, then HL moves on by the step; a\nstep of 0 ends it (after its byte).\nEntry: DE = the list; HL = the first place; B = 0.\nExit: DE past the list; HL at the last place.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.","comment":"The byte"},
        "11636": {"comment":"Stores it"},
        "11637": {"comment":"The step"},
        "11640": {"comment":"On to the next place"},
        "11641": {"comment":"Step 0: the end?"},
        "11645": {"synopsis":"CLS # (ROM0's CLS_CMD jumps here): past the '#', returns when checking syntax, then as\nRESET_COLOURS.","comment":"Past '#'; checking syntax: return"},
        "11648": {"synopsis":"Resets the colours: on stream -2 (SELECT_STREAM_M2) prints the codes $15-$11 each with 0,\nthen $10 with 7 (probably the colour control codes), makes the temporary colours permanent\n(TEMP_TO_PERM), calls $F13A with A = 0, resets the palette (PALETTE_RESET) and clears the\nwhole screen (CLS_ALL).\nExit: as CLS_ALL.\nChanges: all.","comment":"Stream -2"},
        "11651": {"comment":"B = 5, C = $10"},
        "11654": {"synopsis":"Prints code B + $10 and 0, for B = 5 down to 1.","comment":"Code $15 down to $11"},
        "11657": {"comment":"With 0"},
        "11661": {"comment":"Code $10"},
        "11663": {"comment":"With 7"},
        "11666": {"comment":"Temporary colours to permanent"},
        "11673": {"comment":"The default palette"},
        "11676": {"comment":"Clears the screen"},
        "11679": {"synopsis":"PALETTE's body (token $A0):\n- PALETTE alone: PALETTE_RESET.\n- PALETTE n LINE y: removes the line palette change of entry n at y (PAL_FIRST_NUM).\n- PALETTE n, c [LINE y] and PALETTE n, c1, c2 [LINE y]: sets entry n (0-15) to the colours\n  (0-127) in PALTAB, or as a change at line y in the table at $5600 (PAL_SET).\nEntry: A = the character after PALETTE.\nError: stops with error code 23 for n over 15, 24 for a colour over 127, 25 when the line\ntable is full, 30 for a line off the screen.","comment":"The end of the statement?"},
        "11682": {"comment":"No: arguments"},
        "11684": {"comment":"Checking syntax: return"},
        "11687": {"synopsis":"Empties the line palette table ($FF at $5600), copies the 20 default colours from ROM1 $FD51\nto both colour tables at $55D8 and $55EC and, in MODE 3 (MODE = 2), swaps entries 0-3 with\n16-19 in both (PAL_MODE3_SWAP).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Empty line palette table"},
        "11692": {"comment":"The first colour table"},
        "11695": {"comment":"Defaults into it"},
        "11698": {"comment":"And into the second at $55EC"},
        "11701": {"comment":"MODE"},
        "11704": {"comment":"MODE 3?"},
        "11707": {"synopsis":"Swaps palette entries 0-3 with 16-19 in both colour tables ($55D8 and $55EC). ROM1 $D764\ncalls it too.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"The first table's entries 0-3"},
        "11710": {"comment":"With its entries 16-19"},
        "11716": {"comment":"The second's 16-19, with its 0-3 (HL)"},
        "11719": {"synopsis":"Swaps 4 bytes at DE and HL (SWAP5_LP's loop with B = 4).","comment":"4 bytes"},
        "11724": {"synopsis":"Copies the 20 default colours from ROM1 $FD51 to DE.","comment":"20 colours"},
        "11727": {"comment":"The defaults in ROM1"},
        "11733": {"synopsis":"PALETTE with a number: n then LINE (remove a line change) or a comma (colours, PAL_COLOURS).","comment":"n"},
        "11736": {"comment":"LINE?"},
        "11738": {"comment":"No: colours"},
        "11740": {"comment":"y"},
        "11743": {"comment":"A = the line"},
        "11747": {"comment":"0-15, else error 23"},
        "11750": {"comment":"n"},
        "11753": {"comment":"D = the line"},
        "11754": {"comment":"E = n"},
        "11755": {"comment":"The line palette table"},
        "11758": {"synopsis":"Looks for line D in the line palette table (4-byte entries in line order).","comment":"The entry's line"},
        "11760": {"comment":"Line D?"},
        "11763": {"comment":"Past it (or $FF): not there"},
        "11764": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"Past the entry"},
        "11769": {"synopsis":"Line D found: entry n E? Then removes the 4 bytes (moves the rest down).","comment":"The entry number"},
        "11770": {"comment":"n?"},
        "11773": {"comment":"DE = the entry"},
        "11776": {"comment":"HL = the next"},
        "11780": {"comment":"BC = the bytes from there"},
        "11784": {"comment":"Moves the rest down"},
        "11789": {"comment":"Stops with error code 23 (no jump here)"},
        "11791": {"synopsis":"PALETTE n, c1: a second colour, LINE or the end.","comment":"A comma and c1"},
        "11794": {"comment":"Another comma?"},
        "11798": {"comment":"LINE?"},
        "11802": {"comment":"y"},
        "11805": {"comment":"A = the line"},
        "11810": {"synopsis":"One colour and no line: A = $FF (PALTAB).","comment":"Checking syntax: return"},
        "11813": {"comment":"No line: PALTAB"},
        "11815": {"synopsis":"Takes the one colour (0-127, error 24) and uses it twice.","comment":"Keep the line"},
        "11816": {"comment":"0-127, else error 24"},
        "11819": {"comment":"c1"},
        "11822": {"comment":"Twice: c2 = c1"},
        "11825": {"synopsis":"PALETTE n, c1, c2: LINE or the end.","comment":"c2"},
        "11828": {"comment":"LINE?"},
        "11832": {"comment":"Checking syntax: return"},
        "11835": {"comment":"No line"},
        "11840": {"synopsis":"LINE y after the colours: A = the line (PAL_LINE_ROW).","comment":"y"},
        "11843": {"comment":"A = the line"},
        "11846": {"comment":"Keep the line"},
        "11847": {"synopsis":"Takes c2 then c1 (0-127, error 24).","comment":"0-127, else error 24"},
        "11850": {"comment":"c2"},
        "11854": {"comment":"c1"},
        "11857": {"synopsis":"Takes n (0-15, error 23) into E, B = c1, C = c2, A = the line or $FF.","comment":"Keep it"},
        "11858": {"comment":"0-15, else error 23"},
        "11861": {"comment":"n"},
        "11864": {"comment":"E = n"},
        "11865": {"comment":"B = c1"},
        "11867": {"comment":"C = c2"},
        "11868": {"comment":"A = the line or $FF"},
        "11869": {"synopsis":"JPALET's body: with A = $FF sets palette entry E's two colours in PALTAB ($55D8 + E = B,\n$55EC + E = C); otherwise sets them as a change at line A (PAL_LINE_SET).\nEntry: A = $FF or the line; E = the entry; B, C = the colours.\nError: stops with error code 25 when the line table is full.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"No line?"},
        "11871": {"comment":"A line change"},
        "11873": {"comment":"PALTAB"},
        "11878": {"comment":"Entry E"},
        "11879": {"comment":"First colour"},
        "11880": {"comment":"The second table, 20 on"},
        "11883": {"comment":"Second colour"},
        "11885": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 25: the line palette table is full.","comment":"Stops with error code 25"},
        "11887": {"synopsis":"Puts line A, entry E, colours B and C in the table at $5600 (in line order): replaces the\ncolours of the same line and entry, otherwise inserts 4 bytes. Interrupts are off while it\nchanges.","comment":"The line palette table"},
        "11890": {"comment":"D = the line"},
        "11891": {"synopsis":"Finds the first entry with a line not below D.","comment":"The entry's line"},
        "11893": {"comment":"Not below D?"},
        "11896": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"Past the entry"},
        "11901": {"synopsis":"Same line: the same entry number replaces the colours.","comment":"Below D? Insert here"},
        "11903": {"comment":"The entry number"},
        "11904": {"comment":"E?"},
        "11907": {"comment":"Same: new colours"},
        "11910": {"synopsis":"Inserts 4 bytes before the entry at HL: error 25 when the table would reach $200 bytes.","comment":"Back to the entry's line"},
        "11914": {"comment":"BC = the table's size, HL at its end"},
        "11917": {"comment":"4 more bytes"},
        "11921": {"comment":"$200 or more?"},
        "11924": {"comment":"Yes: stops with error code 25"},
        "11926": {"comment":"DE = the place"},
        "11927": {"comment":"Keep the end"},
        "11928": {"comment":"Bytes to move"},
        "11933": {"comment":"DE = the end"},
        "11934": {"comment":"4 bytes up"},
        "11939": {"comment":"No interrupts while it moves"},
        "11940": {"comment":"Opens 4 bytes"},
        "11942": {"comment":"HL = the place"},
        "11943": {"comment":"D = the line, E = n"},
        "11944": {"comment":"The colours"},
        "11945": {"comment":"The line"},
        "11947": {"comment":"The entry number"},
        "11948": {"synopsis":"Stores the colours B, C after the entry's index byte; interrupts back on."},
        "11949": {"comment":"First colour"},
        "11951": {"comment":"Second colour"},
        "11954": {"synopsis":"Counts the line palette table from $5600: BC = its size in bytes with the $FF end; HL at the\n$FF. ROM1 $E13C calls it.\nExit: BC = the bytes; HL = the end.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"The line palette table"},
        "11957": {"synopsis":"PAL_TABLE_SIZE from the entry at HL.","comment":"1 for the $FF"},
        "11960": {"synopsis":"One 4-byte entry, until $FF.","comment":"$FF: the end?"},
        "11963": {"comment":"Past the entry"},
        "11967": {"comment":"4 bytes more"},
        "11973": {"synopsis":"Turns the y of LINE y into the line before its row: scaled as a point (SCALE_COORDS on y,\ny), GET_PLOT_ROW, the extra value dropped, 1 less.\nEntry: y on the calculator stack.\nExit: A = the row - 1.\nError: stops with error code 30 for the top row or a y off the screen.","comment":"y, y: as a point"},
        "11976": {"comment":"Scaled"},
        "11979": {"comment":"A = the row"},
        "11983": {"comment":"Drops the other value"},
        "11987": {"comment":"The line before; row 0?"},
        "11990": {"comment":"Stops with error code 30"},
        "11992": {"synopsis":"BEEP's body (token $AD): BEEP d, p. With the calculator: f = 55 x calc $32((p + 27) / 12),\nso p = 0 gives about 261.6 (calc $32 is probably 2 to the power); puts d in floating form\n(calc $31, probably) and checks its exponent (under $85: d under 16, else error 50) and f's\n($84-$8E, else error 49); cycles = f x d and the period 375000 / f - 15 (GET_UINT16 each),\nthen BEEP_TONE with DE = cycles - 1. No cycles: nothing.\nError: stops with error code 49 or 50 for values out of range, 29 for bad syntax.","comment":"d, p"},
        "11995": {"comment":"p + 27, / 12, calc $32"},
        "12003": {"comment":"x 55"},
        "12006": {"comment":"f, f, d after calc $1C, then calc $31"},
        "12010": {"comment":"The top's exponent"},
        "12011": {"comment":"Under $85?"},
        "12015": {"comment":"Stops with error code 50"},
        "12017": {"synopsis":"Checks the frequency's exponent: $84 to $8E.","comment":"Down to the value below"},
        "12021": {"comment":"Its exponent"},
        "12022": {"comment":"Under $84?"},
        "12026": {"comment":"$8F or more?"},
        "12030": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 49: the frequency is out of range.","comment":"Stops with error code 49"},
        "12032": {"synopsis":"Cycles = f x d; period = 375000 / f - 15 (the 5-byte constant is 375000)."},
        "12033": {"comment":"f x d, then 375000 / f - 15"},
        "12047": {"comment":"The period"},
        "12051": {"comment":"The cycles"},
        "12054": {"comment":"DE = cycles"},
        "12055": {"comment":"HL = the period"},
        "12056": {"comment":"None?"},
        "12058": {"comment":"Cycles - 1"},
        "12059": {"synopsis":"JBEEP's body: a tone on the beeper, bit 4 of port $FE (with BORDCOL and bit 3 set),\ninterrupts off. Each half period is a delay loop timed by H and L / 2 (an odd L enters at\nBEEP_HALF_ODD, 8 T longer); DE counts the cycles down at each falling edge.\nEntry: DE = the cycles; HL = the period (in 8 T units).\nExit: interrupts on; BC kept.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"No interrupts while it times"},
        "12061": {"comment":"The delay with 8 T more"},
        "12064": {"comment":"L / 2; odd?"},
        "12066": {"comment":"Yes: from $EF30"},
        "12068": {"comment":"Even: from $EF32"},
        "12070": {"synopsis":"IX = the delay loop's entry; the border value.","comment":"IX = the delay's entry"},
        "12073": {"comment":"BORDCOL"},
        "12076": {"comment":"Beeper and MIC bits set"},
        "12078": {"comment":"The first edge"},
        "12080": {"synopsis":"Reached by JP (IX): 8 T more, for an odd L, then BEEP_HALF.","comment":"4 T"},
        "12081": {"comment":"4 T more"},
        "12082": {"synopsis":"Reached by JP (IX): the half period's delay, B = L / 2 then H x $7F rounds.","comment":"One more round for H"},
        "12084": {"synopsis":"The delay loop.","comment":"The inner delay"},
        "12087": {"comment":"Then $7F a round"},
        "12089": {"comment":"Rounds left?"},
        "12093": {"synopsis":"Flips the beeper bit; a falling edge counts a cycle.","comment":"Flip the beeper bit"},
        "12095": {"comment":"Out to port $FE"},
        "12097": {"comment":"Keep it in B"},
        "12098": {"comment":"C = H, the rounds"},
        "12099": {"comment":"Bit 4 set: a rising edge?"},
        "12103": {"comment":"Cycles left?"},
        "12105": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "12107": {"comment":"One less"},
        "12108": {"synopsis":"Restores A and B, and delays through IX.","comment":"A = the port value"},
        "12109": {"comment":"B = L / 2"},
        "12110": {"comment":"The delay"},
        "12112": {"synopsis":"A rising edge: no count."},
        "12115": {"synopsis":"All cycles done: BC back, interrupts on."},
        "12118": {"synopsis":"ZAP's body (token $F3): six sweeps of 30 one-cycle tones, the period starting at 255 and\nrising by 2 (SWEEP_TONES).\nChanges: all.","comment":"Checking syntax: return"},
        "12121": {"comment":"6 sweeps"},
        "12123": {"synopsis":"One sweep."},
        "12124": {"comment":"The period's step: +2"},
        "12127": {"comment":"One cycle each"},
        "12129": {"comment":"30 tones"},
        "12136": {"comment":"The next sweep"},
        "12140": {"synopsis":"BOOM's body (token $F5): 78 one-cycle tones, the period from 255 rising by 12.","comment":"Checking syntax: return"},
        "12143": {"comment":"One cycle each"},
        "12145": {"comment":"The period's step: +12"},
        "12150": {"synopsis":"ZOOM's body (token $F6): 78 tones of 6 cycles, the period from 255 falling by 3.","comment":"Checking syntax: return"},
        "12153": {"comment":"6 cycles each"},
        "12155": {"comment":"The period's step: -3"},
        "12158": {"synopsis":"SWEEP_TONES with 78 tones.","comment":"78 tones"},
        "12160": {"synopsis":"Plays A tones of E cycles (BEEP_TONE), the period starting at 255 and moved by BC after\neach.\nEntry: A = the tone count; E = the cycles; BC = the period's step.\nExit: interrupts on.\nChanges: all.","comment":"Period 255"},
        "12162": {"comment":"The count to B'"},
        "12163": {"comment":"H = 0"},
        "12165": {"comment":"D = 0: E cycles"},
        "12168": {"synopsis":"One tone, then the next period."},
        "12169": {"comment":"Keep the cycles and period"},
        "12171": {"comment":"The tone"},
        "12177": {"comment":"The next period"},
        "12179": {"comment":"Tones left?"},
        "12184": {"synopsis":"POW's body (token $F4): 256 one-cycle tones whose periods are the bytes from the address\nSYNTAX_STOP leaves in HL.\nChanges: all.","comment":"Checking syntax: return"},
        "12187": {"comment":"DE = the bytes"},
        "12188": {"comment":"256 tones"},
        "12190": {"synopsis":"One tone with the next byte as the period.","comment":"The period from the next byte"},
        "12196": {"comment":"One cycle"},
        "12199": {"comment":"The tone"},
        "12204": {"comment":"The next"},
        "12208": {"synopsis":"BLOCKS's body (token $A9): BLOCKS n with n 0 or 1 (else error 30) stores n - 1 in BGFLG: 0\ngives $FF, 1 gives 0.\nError: stops with error code 30 for another n.","comment":"n"},
        "12211": {"comment":"0-1, else error 30"},
        "12217": {"comment":"n - 1"},
        "12218": {"comment":"BGFLG"},
        "12222": {"synopsis":"KEY's body (token $DC): KEY n, v stores v (0-255) at RHTAB + n (the keyboard table, n\n0-280).\nError: stops with error code 30 for n over 280 or v over 255.","comment":"n, v"},
        "12225": {"comment":"v"},
        "12229": {"comment":"n"},
        "12233": {"comment":"n over 280?"},
        "12237": {"comment":"Yes: stops with error code 30"},
        "12240": {"comment":"RHTAB, the keyboard table"},
        "12244": {"comment":"Stores v"},
        "12246": {"synopsis":"DEVICE's body (token $F0): DEVICE letter [n] stores the letter (made capital) in SLDEV and n\nin SLNUM. No n (0): T gives 112, N keeps 0, any other letter 1.\nError: stops with error code 29 when no letter follows, 30 for n over 255.","comment":"A letter"},
        "12249": {"comment":"Capital"},
        "12252": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "12253": {"comment":"The number, 0 when none"},
        "12256": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "12257": {"comment":"Checking syntax: return"},
        "12261": {"comment":"C = n"},
        "12264": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "12265": {"comment":"N?"},
        "12267": {"comment":"Yes: as it is"},
        "12269": {"comment":"T?"},
        "12273": {"comment":"T with a number?"},
        "12277": {"comment":"T 0: 112"},
        "12279": {"synopsis":"Another letter: 0 becomes 1.","comment":"0?"},
        "12283": {"comment":"Becomes 1"},
        "12284": {"synopsis":"SLDEV = the letter, SLNUM = C.","comment":"SLDEV, then SLNUM"},
        "12291": {"synopsis":"PAUSE's routine (CMDADDRT's word for token $C2): PAUSE [n]. Reads the optional number,\nrecords the pause for BLITZ (RECORD_GRAPHIC, kind 7, the low byte of n) and falls into\nPAUSE_FRAMES.\nError: 30 when n is not 0-65535; 14 when ESC is pressed while waiting.","comment":"The optional number (syntax: returns from here)"},
        "12294": {"comment":"BC = n, 0-65535"},
        "12297": {"comment":"Kind 7: a pause, for a BLITZ recording"},
        "12302": {"synopsis":"Waits BC frame interrupts, or until a key is pressed; BC = 0 waits for a key only. Each turn\nempties the keyboard queue, halts and tests ESC. BLITZ's kind 7 calls it (ROM0's\nBLITZ_SETTING, BC = the record's byte).\nEntry: BC = the frames.\nExit: BC = 0 when the time ran out; else FLAGS bit 5 cleared.\nError: 14 when ESC is pressed.","comment":"Empty the queue; HL = FLAGS"},
        "12305": {"comment":"Wait for an interrupt"},
        "12306": {"comment":"ESC pressed? Error 14"},
        "12309": {"comment":"LASTSTAT bit 3 set: not the frame interrupt?"},
        "12316": {"comment":"BC = 0: no time limit?"},
        "12320": {"comment":"Count a frame; the last one?"},
        "12324": {"synopsis":"PAUSE_FRAMES's key test: goes on waiting unless FLAGS bit 5 (a new key) was set during the\nframe; then clears it.","comment":"A new key (FLAGS bit 5)?"},
        "12328": {"comment":"Yes: clear it and stop"},
        "12331": {"synopsis":"Sets colour item A to D in the temporary colours. ROM0's COLOUR_ITEM_SET calls it (and\nremakes CEXTAB afterwards). Items, as the tokens PEN-OVER minus $91: $10 PEN (CI_PEN), $11\nPAPER (CI_PAPER), $12 FLASH (CI_FLASH), $13 BRIGHT (CI_BRIGHT), $14 INVERSE (here) and $15\nOVER (CI_OVER).\nINVERSE 0 or 1: INVERT = 0 or $FF and PFLAGT bit 2 = D.\nEntry: A = the item, $10-$15; D = the value.\nError: 23 for a value out of range.\nChanges: AF, BC, E, HL.","comment":"B = the value"},
        "12332": {"comment":"Item $10: PEN?"},
        "12337": {"comment":"$11: PAPER?"},
        "12341": {"comment":"$12: FLASH?"},
        "12344": {"comment":"$13: BRIGHT?"},
        "12347": {"comment":"$14 INVERSE, else $15 OVER"},
        "12350": {"comment":"INVERSE: PFLAGT bit 2"},
        "12352": {"comment":"Only 0 or 1"},
        "12357": {"comment":"INVERT = 0 for 0, $FF for 1"},
        "12362": {"comment":"B = the value in bit 2"},
        "12368": {"synopsis":"COLOUR_ITEM_DO's OVER: values 0-3 are recorded for BLITZ (kind 4) and stored in GOVERT; 0\nand 1 also go to OVERT and PFLAGT bit 0.\nError: 23 for 4 and up.","comment":"OVER: PFLAGT bit 0"},
        "12371": {"comment":"Only 0-3"},
        "12375": {"comment":"Kind 4 for BLITZ, C = the value"},
        "12385": {"comment":"GOVERT = the value"},
        "12388": {"comment":"2 or 3: GOVERT only"},
        "12391": {"comment":"OVERT = the value"},
        "12395": {"synopsis":"Puts the bits of A under the mask C into PFLAGT (MERGE_BITS_C) and returns.","comment":"PFLAGT"},
        "12401": {"synopsis":"COLOUR_ITEM_DO's BRIGHT: outside mode 3 a value of 0 or 1 also clears or sets bits 7 and 3\n(the bright bit of each 4-bit colour) of M23PAPT and M231NKT; then as CI_FLASH with mask $40\n(CI_ATTR_BIT).","comment":"ATTRT/MASKT bit 6"},
        "12403": {"comment":"Mode 3 (MODE 2)?"},
        "12411": {"comment":"Only 0 and 1 change the pen and paper"},
        "12415": {"comment":"Z: BRIGHT 0"},
        "12416": {"comment":"E = M23PAPT"},
        "12420": {"comment":"A = M231NKT"},
        "12425": {"comment":"BRIGHT 1: bits 7 and 3 on"},
        "12428": {"comment":"and in the paper"},
        "12433": {"synopsis":"BRIGHT 0: clears bits 7 and 3 of M231NKT and M23PAPT.","comment":"Bits 7 and 3 off"},
        "12436": {"comment":"and in the paper"},
        "12439": {"synopsis":"Stores the new M23PAPT and M231NKT.","comment":"M23PAPT"},
        "12442": {"comment":"M231NKT"},
        "12446": {"comment":"A = the value"},
        "12447": {"synopsis":"BRIGHT's value rotated once more than FLASH's: bit 0 to bit 6."},
        "12450": {"synopsis":"COLOUR_ITEM_DO's FLASH: mask $80 in ATTRT and MASKT (CI_ATTR_BIT).","comment":"ATTRT/MASKT bit 7"},
        "12452": {"comment":"A = the value"},
        "12453": {"synopsis":"FLASH and BRIGHT: B = the value rotated right (bit 0 to the mask's bit); accepts 0, 1 and 8\n(16 is taken as 8); 8 sets the mask's bit in MASKT (the attribute bit left as it is) instead\nof in ATTRT.\nError: 23 for any other value.","comment":"B = the value rotated into place"},
        "12456": {"comment":"Value 16?"},
        "12460": {"comment":"As 8: one more step right"},
        "12463": {"synopsis":"Checks the value of FLASH or BRIGHT: 8, 0 and 1 go on to CI_ATTR_STORE.","comment":"8?"},
        "12467": {"comment":"0 or 1?"},
        "12471": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 23 (\"Invalid colour\" in ERRMSGS_TABLE): a colour item's value out of\nrange.","comment":"Stops with error code 23"},
        "12473": {"synopsis":"Stores B's bits under the mask C in ATTRT and B rotated right 3 times in MASKT, so a value\nof 8 sets the MASKT bit and clears the ATTRT one.","comment":"ATTRT"},
        "12477": {"comment":"ATTRT bits from B; HL = MASKT"},
        "12480": {"comment":"B rotated right 3 times"},
        "12484": {"comment":"MASKT bits from it"},
        "12486": {"synopsis":"COLOUR_ITEM_DO's PEN: mask 7 in ATTRT (the value itself), then CI_COLOUR.","comment":"ATTRT bits 0-2"},
        "12490": {"synopsis":"COLOUR_ITEM_DO's PAPER: mask $38 in ATTRT, B = the value x 8; then CI_COLOUR.","comment":"ATTRT bits 3-5"},
        "12492": {"comment":"B = the value x 8"},
        "12497": {"synopsis":"PEN and PAPER (C = 7 or $38): a value 0-15 is put in both nibbles of a byte, which becomes\nM231NKT (the pen, recorded for BLITZ as kind 5) or M23PAPT (the paper), in mode 3's bit\norder in mode 3 (MODE 2); 8-15 set ATTRT bit 6. Values 16 and 17 go to CI_COLOUR_16. Then\nATTRT, MASKT and PFLAGT are set (CI_COLOUR_ATTR).\nError: 23 for 18 and up.","comment":"ATTRT"},
        "12501": {"comment":"16 or more?"},
        "12505": {"comment":"The value in both nibbles"},
        "12510": {"comment":"E = the byte"},
        "12511": {"comment":"Values 8-15?"},
        "12514": {"comment":"Yes: ATTRT bit 6 (bright) on"},
        "12516": {"synopsis":"Turns the byte E into mode 3's bit order when MODE is 2 (as M3_COLOUR_FORM).","comment":"Mode 3 (MODE 2)?"},
        "12524": {"comment":"Mode 3's bit order"},
        "12531": {"synopsis":"Stores the byte A as the pen (C bit 0 set: M231NKT, recorded for BLITZ as kind 5) or the\npaper (M23PAPT).","comment":"PEN (C = 7)?"},
        "12535": {"comment":"M231NKT = the pen"},
        "12538": {"comment":"Kind 5 for BLITZ, C = the byte"},
        "12548": {"synopsis":"M23PAPT = A, then CI_COLOUR_ATTR.","comment":"M23PAPT = the paper"},
        "12553": {"synopsis":"PEN or PAPER 16 or 17: B becomes the mask C (all the item's bits) unless ATTRT's bits under\nC OR'd with C leave bits 5 and 2 both set; then CI_COLOUR_ATTR. 18 and up stop with error\n23.","comment":"18 or more: error 23"},
        "12557": {"comment":"A = ATTRT"},
        "12560": {"comment":"Bits 5 and 2 both set with the mask?"},
        "12566": {"comment":"No: B = all the mask bits"},
        "12567": {"synopsis":"B = A."},
        "12568": {"synopsis":"Sets the attribute variables for PEN or PAPER: ATTRT's bits under C from B; MASKT's bits\nunder C set for a value over 15, clear otherwise; PFLAGT bit 4 (PEN) or bit 6 (PAPER) set\nfor a value over 16, clear otherwise.\nEntry: B = the attribute bits; C = the mask; D = the value; HL = ATTRT.","comment":"ATTRT bits from B"},
        "12572": {"comment":"MASKT: set for a value over 15"},
        "12577": {"comment":"C = $10 (PEN) or $40 (PAPER)"},
        "12582": {"comment":"PFLAGT: set for a value over 16"},
        "12584": {"synopsis":"A = $FF when D is over A, else 0; then MERGE_BITS_C.\nEntry: A = the limit; D = the value; C = the mask; HL = the variable.","comment":"Carry: D over the limit"},
        "12585": {"comment":"A = $FF or 0"},
        "12586": {"synopsis":"Puts A's bits under the mask C into the byte at HL, keeping the others; moves HL on.\nEntry: A = the bits; C = the mask; HL = the byte.\nExit: A = C; HL + 1.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"A's bits where C is set"},
        "12590": {"comment":"A = the mask"},
        "12593": {"synopsis":"BORDER's routine (CMDADDRT's word for token $9E): BORDER n with n 0-15, then SET_BORDER_A.\nError: 23 for n over 15.","comment":"One number (syntax: returns from here)"},
        "12596": {"comment":"0-15, else error 23"},
        "12602": {"synopsis":"Sets the border to colour A (0-15): port $FE gets bits 0-2 of the colour, bit 3 of it in bit\n5 and bit 3 set, and BORDCOL bits 0-5 the same; BORDCR = the colour x 8 (the paper) with ink\n7 for colours whose bit 2 is clear, ink 0 otherwise; M23LSC = the colour in both nibbles (L)\nand the contrasting pen, $FF or 0 (H), in mode 3 in its bit order (M3_COLOUR_FORM). ROM1\n$ED96 calls it with A = 0.\nEntry: A = the colour.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"C = L = the colour"},
        "12604": {"comment":"B = the colour x 4"},
        "12607": {"comment":"Bit 3 of the colour to bit 5"},
        "12611": {"comment":"Bit 3 (MIC) on"},
        "12614": {"comment":"BORDCOL bits 0-5 from it"},
        "12623": {"comment":"The border"},
        "12625": {"comment":"A = the colour x 8: the paper"},
        "12627": {"comment":"H = 0: a dark pen"},
        "12629": {"comment":"Colour bit 2 set?"},
        "12633": {"comment":"No: H = $FF and ink 7"},
        "12637": {"synopsis":"Stores BORDCR and makes L the colour in both nibbles; in mode 3 (MODE 2) L takes mode 3's\nbit order and H is $FF unless that byte is $FF.","comment":"BORDCR"},
        "12640": {"comment":"L = the colour in both nibbles"},
        "12647": {"comment":"Mode 3 (MODE 2)?"},
        "12654": {"comment":"Mode 3's bit order"},
        "12657": {"comment":"All set: a pen of 0"},
        "12660": {"comment":"Else $FF"},
        "12662": {"synopsis":"H = A (mode 3's pen byte for M23LSC)."},
        "12663": {"synopsis":"M23LSC = HL.","comment":"M23LSC: L the paper, H the pen"},
        "12667": {"synopsis":"Turns L into mode 3's bit order (M3_COLOUR_FORM) and stores HL in M23LSC. ROM1 $D757 calls\nit while changing the mode.\nEntry: HL = the lower screen's colours."},
        "12672": {"synopsis":"Rearranges the bits of the colour byte L (a colour in both nibbles, as mode 4 keeps it) into\nthe order mode 3 uses: L = ((L rotated left twice XOR L) AND $CC XOR L) rotated left once.\nROM1 $D743 converts M23PAPP and M231NKP with it.\nEntry: L = the byte.\nExit: A = L = the new byte.\nChanges: AF, L."},
        "12682": {"synopsis":"WINDOW's routine (CMDADDRT's word for token $EC): WINDOW alone sets the upper window to the\nwhole screen (WINDOW_FULL); WINDOW l,r,t,b sets UWLHS, UWRHS, UWTOP and UWBOT, checked\nagainst WINDMAX (its low byte the last row, its high byte the last column), and puts SPOSNU\nat the window's top left.\nError: 54 (\"Invalid WINDOW\") when b is past the last row, t over b, r past the last column\nor l not left of r; 30 for a number over 255.","comment":"No numbers?"},
        "12687": {"comment":"Four numbers (FOUR_NUM)"},
        "12690": {"comment":"Syntax: returns from here"},
        "12693": {"comment":"b (the bottom row)"},
        "12696": {"comment":"Past the last row (WINDMAX)?"},
        "12702": {"comment":"B = b"},
        "12704": {"comment":"t (the top row)"},
        "12708": {"comment":"t = b?"},
        "12711": {"comment":"t over b?"},
        "12713": {"synopsis":"C = t; then r, checked against WINDMAX's high byte, and l, which must be under r.","comment":"C = t"},
        "12715": {"comment":"r (the right column)"},
        "12718": {"comment":"Past the last column?"},
        "12725": {"comment":"l (the left column)"},
        "12728": {"comment":"L = r"},
        "12729": {"comment":"l not left of r?"},
        "12732": {"synopsis":"Stores the upper window: UWRHS = L, UWLHS = A, UWTOP and UWBOT from the stack; SPOSNU = (top\nrow, left column).\nEntry: A = the left column; L = the right column; the stack: top row (low), bottom row\n(high).","comment":"H = l"},
        "12733": {"comment":"UWRHS, UWLHS"},
        "12736": {"comment":"L = t, H = b"},
        "12737": {"comment":"UWTOP, UWBOT"},
        "12740": {"comment":"SPOSNU: row t, column l"},
        "12746": {"synopsis":"WINDOW with no numbers: rows 0 to WINDMAX's low byte, columns 0 to its high byte.","comment":"Syntax: returns from here"},
        "12749": {"comment":"L = the last row, H = the last column"},
        "12752": {"comment":"Top 0"},
        "12755": {"comment":"Top 0, bottom the last row"},
        "12756": {"comment":"Right: the last column; left 0"},
        "12759": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 54 (\"Invalid WINDOW\" in ERRMSGS_TABLE).","comment":"Stops with error code 54"},
        "12761": {"synopsis":"OUT's routine (CMDADDRT's word for token $E0): OUT port,value writes the value (0-255) to\nthe 16-bit port (OUT (C),A with the port in BC).\nError: 30 for a value over 255 or a port over 65535.","comment":"Two numbers (syntax: returns from here)"},
        "12764": {"comment":"The value, 0-255"},
        "12768": {"comment":"BC = the port"},
        "12772": {"comment":"Out to port BC"},
        "12775": {"synopsis":"STOP's routine (CMDADDRT's word for token $B1): stops with error code 16 (\"STOP statement\").","comment":"Syntax: returns from here"},
        "12778": {"comment":"Stops with error code 16"},
        "12780": {"synopsis":"RANDOMIZE's routine (CMDADDRT's word for token $C7): SEED = n, or for n = 0 (or no number)\nthe low word of FRAMES.\nError: 30 for n over 65535.","comment":"The optional number (syntax: returns from here)"},
        "12783": {"comment":"HL = n"},
        "12786": {"comment":"n = 0?"},
        "12790": {"comment":"Yes: the frame counter instead"},
        "12793": {"synopsis":"SEED = HL.","comment":"SEED"},
        "12797": {"synopsis":"DUMP's routine (CMDADDRT's word for token $BF): steps past an optional $FF $70 (a function\ntoken) and, when running, calls the dump vector DMPV with A = $AF (DUMP_GRAPHICS).\nError: 29 for $FF followed by another token.","comment":"A function token?"},
        "12801": {"comment":"The token after $FF"},
        "12802": {"comment":"Only $70; else error 29"},
        "12807": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "12808": {"synopsis":"Ends DUMP's syntax check (SYNTAX_STOP) and falls into DUMP_GRAPHICS.","comment":"Syntax: returns from here"},
        "12811": {"synopsis":"JGDUMP's body: calls DMPV (when set) with A = $AF. The operand $AF hides JTDUMP's entry\n$F20C, XOR A: DMPV is called with A = 0. With DMPV's high byte 0 nothing is done.\nEntry: none (A is set here).","comment":"A = $AF; $F20C (JTDUMP): XOR A, A = 0"},
        "12813": {"comment":"DMPV: the dump vector"},
        "12816": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the vector HL unless its high byte is 0 (not set), when it just returns; called, so\nthe vector returns to the caller. ROM1 $DCC1, $DD8B, $F553 and DUMP use it.\nEntry: HL = the vector.","comment":"High byte 0: not set?"},
        "12819": {"comment":"Run it"},
        "12820": {"synopsis":"SCREEN$'s routine (ROM0's function table, a string result): SCREEN$(row,column) gives the\ncharacter at that cell of the screen as a 1-character string, or an empty one (five zero\nbytes stacked by STK_A) when the cell matches no character.\nError: 32 (\"Off screen\", ROM1 $CFA4) when the row is past UWBOT + 2 or the column past\nUWRHS.","comment":"(row,column) (syntax: returns from here)"},
        "12824": {"comment":"L = the column limit"},
        "12829": {"comment":"H = the row limit"},
        "12835": {"comment":"D = the row, E = the column; else error 32"},
        "12838": {"comment":"Which character?"},
        "12841": {"comment":"Found: a 1-byte string at TEMPW1"},
        "12844": {"comment":"Not found: an empty string"},
        "12848": {"synopsis":"JMCHAR's body: finds which character is shown at row D, column E of the screen (positions as\nin the upper screen: DEVICE is 0 meanwhile). The cell's 8 pixel rows are read into the\nbuffer at $5188 as bit patterns, set where a pixel differs from the cell's first one (modes\n3 and 4 through CELL_PATTERN, shifted for the 6-pixel cells of mode 3; modes 1 and 2\ninverted when the first pixel is set), then compared with the 96 characters of the main set\n(from CHARS + 256, codes $20-$7F) and the 41 from UDG - 128 (codes $80-$A8).\nEntry: D = the row; E = the column.\nExit: found: carry reset, A = the code, also at TEMPW1, HL = TEMPW1, BC = 1. Not found:\ncarry set.\nChanges: all.","comment":"DEVICE kept, 0 meanwhile"},
        "12856": {"comment":"DE = the cell in the screen"},
        "12860": {"comment":"DEVICE back"},
        "12862": {"comment":"HL = the cell"},
        "12863": {"comment":"The 8-byte buffer"},
        "12866": {"comment":"CELL_ADDR's flags kept"},
        "12867": {"comment":"Modes 1 and 2?"},
        "12876": {"comment":"The cell's pattern (modes 3, 4)"},
        "12879": {"comment":"Not a 6-pixel cell?"},
        "12882": {"comment":"8 rows; keep bits 6-1"},
        "12888": {"comment":"Even column: shift right"},
        "12890": {"synopsis":"Mode 3, a 6-pixel cell in an odd column: each row rotated left, bits 6-1 kept.","comment":"Rotate the row left"},
        "12892": {"comment":"The 6 pixels only"},
        "12899": {"synopsis":"Mode 3, a 6-pixel cell in an even column: each row rotated right, bits 6-1 kept.","comment":"Rotate the row right"},
        "12901": {"comment":"The 6 pixels only"},
        "12908": {"synopsis":"Modes 1 and 2: the cell's 8 screen bytes into the buffer, inverted when the first byte's bit\n7 (the cell's first pixel) is set."},
        "12909": {"comment":"8 rows, C = 0"},
        "12912": {"comment":"The first byte"},
        "12915": {"comment":"Its first pixel set?"},
        "12918": {"comment":"Then invert: C = $FF"},
        "12919": {"synopsis":"One row of CELL_READ_M12: the screen byte XOR C to the buffer; HL to the next pixel row\n(NEXT_PIXEL_ROW).","comment":"The row"},
        "12922": {"comment":"Inverted or not, to the buffer"},
        "12924": {"comment":"The next pixel row"},
        "12930": {"synopsis":"Looks for the buffer's pattern among the 96 characters from CHARS + 256, then among the 41\nfrom UDG - 128.","comment":"CHARS + 256: code $20"},
        "12934": {"comment":"96 characters"},
        "12939": {"comment":"Found?"},
        "12941": {"comment":"UDG - 128: code $80"},
        "12948": {"comment":"41 characters"},
        "12953": {"comment":"Not there either: carry"},
        "12954": {"comment":"Codes from $80"},
        "12956": {"synopsis":"Turns the index into the character code (+ $20) and keeps it at TEMPW1 as a 1-byte string\n(HL = TEMPW1, BC = 1).","comment":"The code"},
        "12958": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "12961": {"comment":"TEMPW1 = the code"},
        "12966": {"synopsis":"Looks for the 8-byte pattern of the buffer at $5188 in a table of A character patterns, 8\nbytes each: rows 3 and 4 are compared first, then all 8. The entry $F2B6 (the operand of the\nCP $19 at $F2B5) is ADD HL,DE: the next pattern.\nEntry: HL = the first pattern; A = the count.\nExit: found: carry reset, A = its index. Not found: carry set.\nChanges: AF, AF', BC, DE, HL.","comment":"B = the count"},
        "12967": {"comment":"Kept in A'"},
        "12968": {"comment":"C = the buffer's row 4"},
        "12974": {"comment":"A = its row 3"},
        "12975": {"comment":"HL at row 3"},
        "12978": {"comment":"8 bytes a pattern"},
        "12981": {"comment":"$F2B6: ADD HL,DE, the next pattern"},
        "12983": {"comment":"Row 3 the same?"},
        "12986": {"synopsis":"The next pattern of FONT_SEARCH; carry when none is left.","comment":"Another pattern? (to $F2B6)"},
        "12988": {"comment":"None: carry"},
        "12990": {"synopsis":"Row 3 matched: compares row 4, then all 8 rows from row 0.","comment":"Row 4 the same?"},
        "12994": {"comment":"A = row 3 again"},
        "12999": {"comment":"HL at row 0"},
        "13002": {"comment":"The buffer, 8 rows"},
        "13007": {"synopsis":"Compares one row of the pattern with the buffer; a difference goes on with the next pattern.","comment":"The same row?"},
        "13011": {"comment":"No: HL back at its row 3"},
        "13013": {"comment":"A = its row 3"},
        "13019": {"synopsis":"The next row of FONT_CMP_LOOP; after 8 the index = the count - the patterns left.","comment":"Next row"},
        "13025": {"comment":"A = the count"},
        "13026": {"comment":"Index = count - patterns left"},
        "13028": {"synopsis":"LIST_DONE's body (after LIST found the first line): clears the indents (CLR_LIST_INDENT) and\nlists lines from HL, each followed by a new line, while their number is not over LAST; past\nLAST, when DFLAG bit 4 is set, it goes on until the print position reaches WINDBOT.\nEntry: HL = the first line.","comment":"No indents yet"},
        "13031": {"synopsis":"Lists the line at HL (LIST_PROG_LINE), stops at the end of the program, ends it with A = CR,\nand reads the next line's number.","comment":"List it; the end of the program?"},
        "13035": {"comment":"The CR"},
        "13036": {"comment":"The next line's number, high byte"},
        "13040": {"comment":"Past $BFFF: on to the next page"},
        "13044": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "13050": {"comment":"LAST"},
        "13054": {"comment":"Over LAST?"},
        "13059": {"comment":"DFLAG bit 4: fill the window?"},
        "13065": {"comment":"WINDBOT"},
        "13069": {"comment":"Above it: list on"},
        "13076": {"synopsis":"Lists one program line at HL (ROM0's LIST_LINE_R1 jumps here; ROM0's ED_FETCH_LINE calls it\nto copy a line into the edit line): the line number right-aligned in 5 columns\n(PRINT_BC_DEC's entry $F5B4), on the upper screen the row's LPT byte set ($5B), then the\nline cursor (DRAW_LINE_MARK) for the line EPPC or a space, then the text (LIST_TEXT).\nEntry: HL = the line (paged in).\nExit: carry at the end of the program ($FF); else A = CR, HL past the line.\nChanges: all.","comment":"High byte of the number"},
        "13080": {"comment":"The end marker $FF?"},
        "13084": {"comment":"BC = the number"},
        "13088": {"comment":"$5ABC = the running indent"},
        "13094": {"comment":"Carry reset"},
        "13096": {"comment":"EPPC"},
        "13099": {"comment":"Z: this line; carry: after it"},
        "13106": {"synopsis":"$5B86 (BCREG) = 1 for a line after EPPC, else 0; then the number is printed.","comment":"BCREG = 0 or 1"},
        "13109": {"comment":"The number, 5 columns"},
        "13112": {"comment":"The upper screen (DEVICE 0)?"},
        "13118": {"comment":"E = SPOSNU row - WINDTOP + $52"},
        "13129": {"comment":"DE = LPT + the row"},
        "13131": {"comment":"Set: a line starts here"},
        "13133": {"synopsis":"HL past the line number and length to the text; the line EPPC gets the line cursor and FLAGS\nbit 0 set, any other a space.","comment":"Past the length: the text"},
        "13136": {"comment":"The line EPPC?"},
        "13139": {"comment":"The line cursor"},
        "13142": {"synopsis":"Lists the text at HL with FLAGS bit 0 set (LIST_TEXT). ED_REDRAW_LINE calls it through BC\nfor the line being edited.\nEntry: HL = the text."},
        "13143": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 0 on"},
        "13151": {"synopsis":"A space after the number of a line other than EPPC."},
        "13154": {"synopsis":"Lists a line's text from HL: $5AC0 = 0, the indent for the first statement (LIST_INDENT_TOK)\nwhen LISTFLG is set, INQUFG = 0; then LIST_CHAR_LOOP.\nEntry: HL = the text.","comment":"The line's own indent ($5AC0) = 0"},
        "13158": {"comment":"LISTFLG: an indented listing?"},
        "13162": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "13166": {"comment":"Indent for it"},
        "13171": {"comment":"INQUFG = 0: not in quotes"},
        "13175": {"synopsis":"Prints one item of the text: the '?' marker first where XPTR points, the cursor where KCUR\nis (CURSOR_IF_KCUR); skips a hidden number, keeps the position in LSPTR, returns at CR. In\nan indented listing (LISTFLG) a ':' outside quotes, unless FLAGE bit 5 is set, starts a new\nrow instead (LIST_NEW_ROW); a '\"' flips INQUFG bit 0.\nEntry: DE = the text.\nExit: A = CR; HL past it.","comment":"XPTR: the error mark here?"},
        "13181": {"comment":"Then the '?'"},
        "13184": {"comment":"The cursor here?"},
        "13188": {"comment":"Past a hidden number; A = the character"},
        "13193": {"comment":"LSPTR = its address"},
        "13197": {"comment":"The end of the line?"},
        "13201": {"comment":"A ':'?"},
        "13206": {"comment":"LISTFLG: indented?"},
        "13213": {"comment":"INQUFG bit 0: in quotes?"},
        "13220": {"comment":"FLAGE bit 5?"},
        "13228": {"comment":"$5ABD kept, 0 meanwhile"},
        "13236": {"comment":"The lower screen (DEVICE 1)?"},
        "13240": {"comment":"No: a CR"},
        "13244": {"comment":"Yes: TAB 0 ($17, 0, 0)"},
        "13250": {"synopsis":"An indented listing's ':': prints A (CR, or the last byte of TAB 0), 6 spaces (under the\nline number, ROM1 $DE76), puts $5ABD back and indents for the next statement\n(LIST_INDENT_TOK).","comment":"CR or TAB 0"},
        "13251": {"comment":"6 spaces"},
        "13257": {"comment":"$5ABD back"},
        "13261": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "13265": {"comment":"Indent for it"},
        "13270": {"synopsis":"A '\"' flips INQUFG bit 0 (counts up).","comment":"A '\"'?"},
        "13274": {"comment":"INQUFG: in or out of quotes"},
        "13278": {"synopsis":"Prints the item (RST $10) and goes on with LIST_CHAR_LOOP.","comment":"Print it"},
        "13281": {"synopsis":"Moves LPT's 30 bytes (a byte a screen row, set where a listed line starts) with the window:\nD = 1 (ROM0's SCROLL_WIN_UP1) moves them up by A rows (LPT_SHIFT_UP); D = 0\n(SCROLL_WIN_DOWN) down by A rows, clearing the A bytes at the top.\nEntry: A = the rows; D = 1 up, 0 down.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"L = the rows"},
        "13282": {"comment":"C = 30 - rows: the bytes moved"},
        "13286": {"comment":"B = H = 0"},
        "13290": {"comment":"Up?"},
        "13293": {"comment":"LPT's last byte"},
        "13297": {"comment":"HL = it - the rows"},
        "13301": {"comment":"Move them down"},
        "13303": {"comment":"B = the rows"},
        "13305": {"synopsis":"Clears B bytes of LPT downwards from DE: the rows that came in at the top.","comment":"Cleared"},
        "13310": {"synopsis":"Moves LPT up by L rows, lowers LNPTR (the line cursor's row) by as many and clears the rows\nat the bottom.","comment":"LPT"},
        "13313": {"comment":"HL = LPT + the rows"},
        "13314": {"comment":"Move them up"},
        "13316": {"comment":"B = the rows"},
        "13317": {"comment":"LNPTR - the rows"},
        "13324": {"synopsis":"Clears B bytes of LPT from DE upwards: the rows that came in at the bottom.","comment":"Cleared"},
        "13329": {"synopsis":"The indent of an indented listing (LISTFLG = the step) for a statement starting with token\nA. $5ABE is the running indent of blocks and $5AC0 the line's own; $5ABF and $5AC1 (copied\nfrom them first) are this statement's.\n1. DO, IF ($D7), DEF PROC and FOR add the step to $5ABE (INDENT_OPEN): the next statements\n   move in.\n2. LOOP, END PROC, END IF and NEXT take it off $5ABF and $5ABE (INDENT_CLOSE).\n3. LOOP IF, EXIT IF and ELSE ($D9) take it off $5ABF only (INDENT_MID); ELSE ($DA) off\n   $5AC1.\n4. IF ($D8) and ON add it to $5AC0.\nThen INDENT_SPACES prints $5ABF + $5AC1 spaces.\nEntry: A = the token.\nChanges: AF, B, HL; what ROM1 $DE76 changes.","comment":"The indents"},
        "13333": {"comment":"$5ABF = $5ABE"},
        "13337": {"comment":"$5AC1 = $5AC0"},
        "13341": {"comment":"DO?"},
        "13345": {"comment":"IF ($D7)?"},
        "13349": {"comment":"DEF PROC?"},
        "13353": {"comment":"FOR?"},
        "13357": {"comment":"LOOP?"},
        "13361": {"comment":"END PROC?"},
        "13365": {"comment":"END IF?"},
        "13369": {"comment":"NEXT?"},
        "13373": {"synopsis":"The end of a block: one step off this statement's indent ($5ABF) and the running one ($5ABE\n= $5ABF).","comment":"$5ABF - the step"},
        "13376": {"comment":"$5ABE = $5ABF"},
        "13381": {"synopsis":"Tests for EXIT IF, ELSE ($D9) and LOOP IF; then, with HL at $5AC0, ELSE ($DA).","comment":"EXIT IF?"},
        "13385": {"comment":"ELSE ($D9)?"},
        "13389": {"comment":"LOOP IF?"},
        "13393": {"comment":"HL = $5AC0"},
        "13395": {"comment":"ELSE ($DA)?"},
        "13399": {"synopsis":"One step off this statement's indent only ($5ABF, or $5AC1 for ELSE $DA).","comment":"The byte after HL - the step"},
        "13404": {"synopsis":"Tests for IF ($D8) and ON, which open the line's own indent ($5AC0).","comment":"IF ($D8)?"},
        "13408": {"comment":"ON?"},
        "13412": {"synopsis":"Adds the step (LISTFLG) to the indent at HL ($5ABE or $5AC0), then INDENT_SPACES.","comment":"+ the step"},
        "13417": {"comment":"Hides $F46A: LD A,6, then CP $AF ($DC46's entry)"},
        "13419": {"comment":"No effect here"},
        "13421": {"synopsis":"Prints $5ABF + $5AC1 spaces (ROM1 $DE76), at most the window's width - 5 and none in a\nwindow under 10 columns. The entry $F46A (inside the CP $3E at $F469: LD A,6, then CP $AF),\nwhich ROM1 $DC46 calls, adds 6 (the line number's columns).\nEntry: A = 0 here, 6 from $F46A.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "13422": {"comment":"+ $5ABF"},
        "13428": {"comment":"+ $5AC1"},
        "13429": {"comment":"None?"},
        "13431": {"comment":"WINDRHS, WINDLHS"},
        "13434": {"comment":"The width"},
        "13436": {"comment":"Under 10 columns?"},
        "13439": {"comment":"At most width - 5"},
        "13444": {"comment":"Cut down"},
        "13445": {"synopsis":"Prints B spaces (ROM1 $DE76).","comment":"B spaces"},
        "13448": {"synopsis":"Takes the step (LISTFLG) off the byte after HL, not below 0.\nEntry: HL = the byte before it.\nExit: HL at the byte.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.","comment":"The byte"},
        "13453": {"comment":"- the step"},
        "13456": {"comment":"Not below 0"},
        "13457": {"comment":"Else 0"},
        "13460": {"synopsis":"Draws the line being edited again in place (ROM0's CALL_R1_F494, when DFLAG bit 3 is set\nbefore a key is read).\n1. Sets up the device (DEVICE_COLOURS), keeps the print position and WINDTOP (in TEMPB2),\n   clears DFLAG bits 5 and 3, and makes ED_REDRAW_ERR the error return (ERRSP).\n2. Lists the text: the edit line (ED_LINE_START) through LIST_LINE_TEXT with\n   CALL_BC_LISTING, unless it is empty; an INPUT line (FLAGE bit 5) with LIST_LINE_TEXT\n   directly. Then the cursor when it is at the end.\n3. Pads with spaces up to where the last drawing ended (OLDPOS, its row moved as the window\n   moved: ROW_SCROLL_ADJ), keeps the new end in OLDPOS, puts ERRSP back and the print\n   position (ROM1 $DC62), and clears XPTR's high byte.","comment":"Set up the device"},
        "13463": {"comment":"DE = the print position"},
        "13467": {"comment":"TEMPB2 = WINDTOP"},
        "13473": {"comment":"DFLAG bits 5 and 3 off"},
        "13480": {"comment":"ERRSP kept"},
        "13484": {"comment":"An error goes to ED_REDRAW_ERR"},
        "13492": {"comment":"DE = the line, Z for the edit line"},
        "13495": {"comment":"OLDPOS kept"},
        "13500": {"comment":"BC = LIST_LINE_TEXT"},
        "13503": {"comment":"An INPUT line (FLAGE bit 5)?"},
        "13510": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "13515": {"comment":"No indents"},
        "13518": {"comment":"List it"},
        "13521": {"comment":"Z: no second listing"},
        "13522": {"synopsis":"An INPUT line: lists it (BC = LIST_LINE_TEXT through JP_BC).","comment":"List it"},
        "13525": {"synopsis":"After the text: the cursor if KCUR is at the end, then the position reached and OLDPOS moved\nwith the window."},
        "13526": {"comment":"The cursor at the end?"},
        "13529": {"comment":"Set up the device again"},
        "13532": {"comment":"DE = where the text ended"},
        "13535": {"comment":"HL = OLDPOS"},
        "13536": {"comment":"Its row moved with the window"},
        "13541": {"synopsis":"Prints spaces until the print position reaches the old end (BC), then goes on at $F4FE\n(inside the LD HL at $F4FD).","comment":"BC = the old end"},
        "13542": {"comment":"DE = the position"},
        "13547": {"comment":"Reached it? (to $F4FE)"},
        "13552": {"comment":"A space"},
        "13559": {"synopsis":"ED_REDRAW_LINE's error return (its address is at ERRSP): sounds the lower screen's beep or\nleaves the editor (ED_LOWER_BEEP), takes the print position as the end and finishes as\nED_REDRAW_LINE does.","comment":"Beep, or out of the editor"},
        "13562": {"comment":"DE = the position"},
        "13565": {"comment":"Skips $F4FE: POP DE (the end), POP HL (the error return)"},
        "13568": {"comment":"ERRSP back"},
        "13572": {"comment":"OLDPOS = the end"},
        "13576": {"comment":"The first position"},
        "13577": {"comment":"Its row moved too"},
        "13580": {"comment":"The print position back"},
        "13583": {"comment":"XPTR's high byte = 0"},
        "13588": {"synopsis":"Adds to the row H how far WINDTOP has moved since ED_REDRAW_LINE kept it in TEMPB2.\nEntry: H = the row.\nExit: H moved.\nChanges: AF, B, H.","comment":"TEMPB2: WINDTOP before"},
        "13592": {"comment":"WINDTOP now"},
        "13596": {"comment":"+ the row"},
        "13599": {"synopsis":"ROM0's ED_ROW_OUTPUT's body (the output routine while ED_CURSOR_UPDN draws the line): at the\nposition KPOS (SPOSNL equal to it) makes the character being printed the cursor's (KCUR =\nLSPTR) and draws the cursor; then prints A (ED_ROW_OUT_CHAR).\nEntry: A = the character.","comment":"SPOSNL"},
        "13603": {"comment":"KPOS"},
        "13607": {"comment":"At KPOS?"},
        "13611": {"comment":"KCUR = LSPTR: this character"},
        "13618": {"comment":"Draw the cursor"},
        "13622": {"synopsis":"Prints A through ROM1 $E013 (CALL_R1_E013).","comment":"Print it"},
        "13625": {"synopsis":"When DE is KCUR and the page in HMPR is KCURP's, keeps the print position (SPOSNL) in KPOS\nand draws the cursor (DRAW_CURSOR); otherwise returns.\nEntry: DE = the text position.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.","comment":"KCUR here?"},
        "13632": {"comment":"HMPR"},
        "13635": {"comment":"KCURP's page?"},
        "13642": {"comment":"KPOS = SPOSNL"},
        "13648": {"synopsis":"Draws the cursor: calls the vector at $5AFE (RURV) when set, then prints the character at\n$5A01 (or at $5A02 when KLFLAG bit 3 is set) inverse (PRINT_MARKER_A).","comment":"The vector at $5AFE, if set"},
        "13654": {"comment":"The two cursor characters"},
        "13657": {"comment":"KLFLAG bit 3?"},
        "13662": {"comment":"The first"},
        "13665": {"comment":"Or the second"},
        "13668": {"synopsis":"Draws the line cursor LNCUR at the print position and sets LNPTR to its row (SPOSNU's row).\nROM0's LCUR_SET_ROW jumps here. The operand of the CP $3E at $F56D hides the entry $F56E: LD\nA,'?', the error mark LIST_CHAR_LOOP prints at XPTR.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"LNPTR = the row"},
        "13674": {"comment":"LNCUR"},
        "13677": {"comment":"Hides $F56E: LD A,'?' (the error mark)"},
        "13680": {"synopsis":"Prints A inverse as a plain character: PFLAGT bit 2 set and INVERT, INQUFG and BGFLG $FF\nmeanwhile, all four put back afterwards.\nEntry: A = the character.\nKeeps: DE, HL.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"B = the character"},
        "13682": {"comment":"PFLAGT kept"},
        "13687": {"comment":"Bit 2 on: inverse"},
        "13689": {"comment":"INVERT kept"},
        "13693": {"comment":"INQUFG kept"},
        "13697": {"comment":"BGFLG kept"},
        "13701": {"comment":"All three $FF"},
        "13714": {"comment":"Print it"},
        "13718": {"comment":"BGFLG back"},
        "13722": {"comment":"INQUFG back"},
        "13726": {"comment":"INVERT back"},
        "13730": {"comment":"PFLAGT back"},
        "13736": {"synopsis":"Prints A in decimal without leading zeros (PRINT_BC_DEC with BC = A). ROM0's REPORT_LINE and\nERR_PRINT_LINE call it.\nEntry: A = the number.","comment":"BC = A"},
        "13739": {"synopsis":"Prints BC in decimal, without leading zeros; a number $FF00 or more (an edit line's number)\nprints as 0. The LD ($201E),HL at $F5B3 hides the entry $F5B4, LD E,$20, which prints\nleading zeros as spaces (5 columns; LIST_PROG_LINE uses it). The digits come from\nsubtracting the words at ROM1 $FE46 (-10000, -1000, -100, -10, then 0 for the last digit).\nROM0's PRINT_REPORT, ERR_PRINT_LINE and ED_AUTO_NUMBER call it.\nEntry: BC = the number.\nKeeps: HL.\nChanges: AF, BC, E.","comment":"No leading zeros"},
        "13741": {"comment":"$FFxx?"},
        "13745": {"comment":"Then BC = 0"},
        "13747": {"comment":"Skips $F5B4: LD E,$20 (leading spaces)"},
        "13750": {"synopsis":"Keeps HL and BC; HL = the table of powers of ten at ROM1 $FE46.","comment":"The number on the stack"},
        "13752": {"comment":"The negated powers of ten"},
        "13755": {"synopsis":"Takes the next power from the table; the 0 that ends it prints the last digit.","comment":"BC = -power"},
        "13759": {"comment":"HL = the number left"},
        "13761": {"comment":"The end word (0)?"},
        "13765": {"comment":"Count from 0"},
        "13766": {"synopsis":"Subtracts the power until the number goes below 0; A = the digit + 1.","comment":"One more"},
        "13768": {"comment":"Still 0 or more?"},
        "13770": {"comment":"Add the last one back"},
        "13772": {"comment":"A = the digit; 0?"},
        "13775": {"synopsis":"A digit other than a leading zero: E = '0' from now on, so later zeros print.","comment":"E = '0'"},
        "13777": {"synopsis":"Prints the digit + E (a leading zero: nothing for E = 0, a space for E = $20); then the next\npower.","comment":"The character; 0: nothing"},
        "13781": {"comment":"HL = the table pointer again"},
        "13782": {"comment":"The last power done?"},
        "13786": {"comment":"Drop the number"},
        "13787": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "13789": {"synopsis":"The table UMSGS points to after boot (JPOMSG's messages; ROM0's PRINT_UMSG prints one): 9\nmessages, numbered from 0, each ended by a byte with bit 7 set (ROM1 $DD5A counts them). A\nbyte whose low 7 bits are under $20 stands for that entry of the word list at ROM1 $F819 (in\nthe same form, read by $DD6D), so \"Nu\" $1E \"ric\" $8E reads \"Numeric array: \". Message 0 is\nthe start-up line ($7F is the font's character 127); the next are \"scroll?\", a space, the\ntape prompt and the headers of a file's kind (\"Basic: \" to \"Screen: \"). ERRMSGS_TABLE\nfollows directly.","comment":"UMSGS 0: \"   MILES GORDON TECHNOLOGY plc       $7F 1990  SAM Coup\""},
        "13842": {"comment":"UMSGS 1: \"scroll?\""},
        "13849": {"comment":"UMSGS 2: \" \""},
        "13850": {"comment":"UMSGS 3: \"Start tape and then press a key\""},
        "13880": {"comment":"UMSGS 4: \"Basic: \""},
        "13887": {"comment":"UMSGS 5: \"Numeric array: \""},
        "13894": {"comment":"UMSGS 6: \"String array: \""},
        "13896": {"comment":"UMSGS 7: \"Code: \""},
        "13901": {"comment":"UMSGS 8: \"Screen: \""},
        "13905": {"synopsis":"The table ERRMSGS points to after boot: BASIC's error messages, message n for error code n\n(0 \"OK\" to 55; ROM0's REPORT_TEXT finds it through ROM1 $DD4C), in UMSGS_TABLE's form: bit 7\nends a message, a byte under $20 (low 7 bits) is a word from the list at ROM1 $F819. It runs\nto ROM1 $F818; the word list follows it.","comment":"Error 0: \"OK\""},
        "13907": {"comment":"Error 1: \"Out of memory\""},
        "13916": {"comment":"Error 2: \" not found\""},
        "13922": {"comment":"Error 3: \"DATA has all been read\""},
        "13944": {"comment":"Error 4: \"Subscript wrong\""},
        "13959": {"comment":"Error 5: \"NEXT without FOR\""},
        "13964": {"comment":"Error 6: \"FOR without NEXT\""},
        "13969": {"comment":"Error 7: \"FN without DEF FN\""},
        "13978": {"comment":"Error 8: \"RETURN without GOSUB\""},
        "13990": {"comment":"Error 9: \"Missing LOOP\""},
        "13992": {"comment":"Error 10: \"LOOP without DO\""},
        "13996": {"comment":"Error 11: \"No POP data\""},
        "14005": {"comment":"Error 12: \"Missing DEF PROC\""},
        "14010": {"comment":"Error 13: \"No END PROC\""},
        "14015": {"comment":"Error 14: \"BREAK - CONTINUE to repeat\""},
        "14035": {"comment":"Error 15: \"BREAK into program\""},
        "14046": {"comment":"Error 16: \"STOP statement\""},
        "14049": {"comment":"Error 17: \"STOP in INPUT\""},
        "14057": {"comment":"Error 18: \"Invalid file name\""},
        "14060": {"comment":"Error 19: \"Loading error\""},
        "14067": {"comment":"Error 20: \"Invalid device\""},
        "14073": {"comment":"Error 21: \"Invalid stream number\""},
        "14079": {"comment":"Error 22: \"End of file\""},
        "14084": {"comment":"Error 23: \"Invalid colour\""},
        "14086": {"comment":"Error 24: \"Invalid palette colour\""},
        "14089": {"comment":"Error 25: \"Too many palette changes\""},
        "14098": {"comment":"Error 26: \"Parameter error\""},
        "14106": {"comment":"Error 27: \"Invalid argument\""},
        "14113": {"comment":"Error 28: \"Number too large\""},
        "14120": {"comment":"Error 29: \"Not understood\""},
        "14132": {"comment":"Error 30: \"Integer out of range\""},
        "14149": {"comment":"Error 31: \"Statement doesn't exist\""},
        "14165": {"comment":"Error 32: \"Off screen\""},
        "14171": {"comment":"Error 33: \"No room for line\""},
        "14184": {"comment":"Error 34: \"Invalid screen mode\""},
        "14192": {"comment":"Error 35: \"Invalid BLITZ code\""},
        "14203": {"comment":"Error 36: \"Stored area too big\""},
        "14216": {"comment":"Error 37: \"Invalid PUT block\""},
        "14226": {"comment":"Error 38: \"PUT mask mismatch\""},
        "14243": {"comment":"Error 39: \"Missing END IF\""},
        "14250": {"comment":"Error 40: \"Invalid variable name\""},
        "14259": {"comment":"Error 41: \"BASIC stack full\""},
        "14275": {"comment":"Error 42: \"String too long\""},
        "14278": {"comment":"Error 43: \"Invalid screen number\""},
        "14284": {"comment":"Error 44: \"Screen is already open\""},
        "14287": {"comment":"Error 45: \"Stream is already open\""},
        "14290": {"comment":"Error 46: \"Current screen\""},
        "14300": {"comment":"Error 47: \"Stream is not open\""},
        "14310": {"comment":"Error 48: \"Invalid CLEAR address\""},
        "14324": {"comment":"Error 49: \"Invalid Note\""},
        "14326": {"comment":"Error 50: \"Note too long\""},
        "14329": {"comment":"Error 51: \"FPC error\""},
        "14333": {"comment":"Error 52: \"Too many definitions\""},
        "14336": {"comment":"Rest of error 52's message, 'Too many definitions'"},
        "14343": {"comment":"Error 53: 'No DOS'"},
        "14349": {"comment":"Error 54: 'Invalid WINDOW'"},
        "14356": {"comment":"Error 55: 'Missing disk', the table's last"},
        "14361": {"synopsis":"The 32 words the messages share, bit-7 ended, numbered $00-$1F. A message byte whose low 7\nbits are below $20 stands for the word of that number: ROM1 $DD5A, which copies entry A of a\nbit-7-ended list at DE to the buffer at HL, calls itself with DE = MSG_WORDS for such a byte\n(ROM1 $DD6D), so words are expanded wherever a message (ERRMSGS) uses one. Word $1F 'ar'\nends at $38C7; the byte after it is the keyword list's spacer.","comment":"Word $00"},
        "14369": {"comment":"Word $01"},
        "14378": {"comment":"Word $02"},
        "14386": {"comment":"Word $03"},
        "14391": {"comment":"Word $04"},
        "14407": {"comment":"Word $05"},
        "14415": {"comment":"Word $06"},
        "14419": {"comment":"Word $07"},
        "14425": {"comment":"Word $08"},
        "14430": {"comment":"Word $09"},
        "14435": {"comment":"Word $0A"},
        "14439": {"comment":"Word $0B"},
        "14442": {"comment":"Word $0C"},
        "14448": {"comment":"Word $0D"},
        "14453": {"comment":"Word $0E"},
        "14461": {"comment":"Word $0F"},
        "14465": {"comment":"Word $10"},
        "14469": {"comment":"Word $11"},
        "14474": {"comment":"Word $12"},
        "14479": {"comment":"Word $13"},
        "14485": {"comment":"Word $14"},
        "14494": {"comment":"Word $15"},
        "14502": {"comment":"Word $16"},
        "14507": {"comment":"Word $17"},
        "14511": {"comment":"Word $18"},
        "14517": {"comment":"Word $19"},
        "14519": {"comment":"Word $1A"},
        "14524": {"comment":"Word $1B"},
        "14528": {"comment":"Word $1C"},
        "14530": {"comment":"Word $1D"},
        "14532": {"comment":"Word $1E"},
        "14534": {"comment":"Word $1F"},
        "14536": {"comment":"Spacer: the search from $F8C7 ($C585) passes this end first"},
        "14537": {"synopsis":"The keywords, bit-7 ended, 196 entries from PI to INK; '-' marks an unused code. Entry n (PI\nis 1) is the code $FF, n + $3A for n below $4A (the functions and operators PI-'>=', $FF\n$3B-$FF $83) and the one-byte token n + $3B from there (USING $85 ... DIR $90 ... ZOOM $F6,\nthen unused $F7-$FE). INK, the last, would be $FF: ROM1 $C5AD turns it into PEN ($A1).\nReaders: ROM1 $C585 tokenises a line by searching it with JT_018A (ROM1 $D6B0), HL = $F8C7\nand A = $C5 (the count, which runs out after INK); the listing prints entry A with ROM1\n$DD5A from $F8C9 ($DD04) or from later entries ($F92A SIN, $F9A3 MOD, $F9BC USING, $FA2F\nPALETTE, $FACB FOR, $FB67 OUT; ROM1 $DCCA-$DD13); BOOT's code (ROM1 $D96A) compares 4 bytes\nwith 'BOOT' at $FB94.","comment":"$FF $3B"},
        "14539": {"comment":"$FF $3C"},
        "14542": {"comment":"$FF $3D"},
        "14547": {"comment":"$FF $3E"},
        "14551": {"comment":"$FF $3F"},
        "14557": {"comment":"$FF $40"},
        "14561": {"comment":"$FF $41"},
        "14565": {"comment":"$FF $42"},
        "14567": {"comment":"$FF $43"},
        "14570": {"comment":"$FF $44"},
        "14576": {"comment":"$FF $45"},
        "14582": {"comment":"$FF $46"},
        "14586": {"comment":"$FF $47"},
        "14590": {"comment":"$FF $48"},
        "14596": {"comment":"$FF $49, unused"},
        "14597": {"comment":"$FF $4A"},
        "14602": {"comment":"$FF $4B"},
        "14608": {"comment":"$FF $4C"},
        "14615": {"comment":"$FF $4D"},
        "14619": {"comment":"$FF $4E, unused"},
        "14620": {"comment":"$FF $4F"},
        "14625": {"comment":"$FF $50"},
        "14632": {"comment":"$FF $51, unused"},
        "14633": {"comment":"$FF $52, unused"},
        "14634": {"comment":"$FF $53"},
        "14637": {"comment":"$FF $54"},
        "14640": {"comment":"$FF $55"},
        "14643": {"comment":"$FF $56"},
        "14646": {"comment":"$FF $57"},
        "14649": {"comment":"$FF $58"},
        "14652": {"comment":"$FF $59"},
        "14654": {"comment":"$FF $5A"},
        "14657": {"comment":"$FF $5B"},
        "14660": {"comment":"$FF $5C"},
        "14663": {"comment":"$FF $5D"},
        "14666": {"comment":"$FF $5E"},
        "14669": {"comment":"$FF $5F"},
        "14672": {"comment":"$FF $60"},
