        "15323": {"comment":"Would be $FF: ROM1 $C5AD makes INK PEN ($A1)"},
        "15326": {"synopsis":"The start-up key definitions, copied to $5800 (68 bytes) by the reset at ROM1 $EC56; DKDEF =\n$5800 and DKLIM = $5880 come from SYSVAR_INIT_5BC6. The list KEYDEF_FIND reads: each entry\nis the key's code, a length word and the text (tokens and characters); a code $FF ends it.\nThe editor (ED_KEY_DEFN) puts the text in at the cursor; one that ends with ':' leaves the\nline open, any other ends it as ENTER does.","comment":"Key $C0: LIST"},
        "15330": {"comment":"Key $C1: RENUM:"},
        "15335": {"comment":"Key $C2: PRINT:"},
        "15340": {"comment":"Key $C3: MODE:"},
        "15345": {"comment":"Key $C4: RUN"},
        "15349": {"comment":"Key $C5: CONTINUE"},
        "15353": {"comment":"Key $C6: CLS #"},
        "15358": {"comment":"Key $C7: LOAD \"\""},
        "15364": {"comment":"Key $C8: LOAD \"\" CODE"},
        "15372": {"comment":"Key $C9: BOOT"},
        "15376": {"comment":"Key $FC: {$06}:"},
        "15381": {"comment":"Key $FD: {$14}{$01}:"},
        "15387": {"comment":"Key $FE: {$14}{$00}:"},
        "15393": {"comment":"End of the list"},
        "15394": {"synopsis":"The start-up values of the system variables $5A00-$5A11 (LNCUR to LPTPRTI), 18 bytes the\nreset copies at ROM1 $EC60, straight after KEYDEF_DEFAULTS.","comment":"LNCUR = $3E"},
        "15395": {"comment":"$5A01 = $80"},
        "15396": {"comment":"$5A02 = $81"},
        "15397": {"comment":"$5A03 = $31"},
        "15398": {"comment":"$5A04 = $30"},
        "15399": {"comment":"$5A05 = $23"},
        "15400": {"comment":"SLDEV = 'T'"},
        "15401": {"comment":"SLNUM = $70"},
        "15402": {"comment":"$5A08 = $11"},
        "15403": {"comment":"LINIPTR = $5600"},
        "15405": {"comment":"XCMDP = $FF, $0000"},
        "15408": {"comment":"PRRHS = 79"},
        "15409": {"comment":"AFTERCR = $0A"},
        "15410": {"comment":"LPTPRTI = $01E9"},
        "15412": {"synopsis":"The start-up values of the system variables $5BC6-$5BDF (BASSTK to MNIP), 26 bytes the reset\ncopies at ROM1 $EC6A after SYSVAR_INIT_5A00. Its last four bytes, MNOP and MNIP, are the\nfirst four of CHANNEL_TABLE (channel K's routines), so the table proper ends at $3C49.","comment":"BASSTK = $4AFF"},
        "15414": {"comment":"HEAPEND = $4000"},
        "15416": {"comment":"HPST = $4000"},
        "15418": {"comment":"FPSBOT = $4D00"},
        "15420": {"comment":"DKDEF = $5800: KEYDEF_DEFAULTS copy"},
        "15422": {"comment":"DKLIM = $5880"},
        "15424": {"comment":"PATOUT = $DC77 (ROM1)"},
        "15426": {"comment":"ERRMSGS = $F651 (ROM1)"},
        "15428": {"comment":"UMSGS = $F5DD (ROM1)"},
        "15430": {"comment":"RHTAB = $58E0: KEYMAP_PLANE0 copy - 1"},
        "15432": {"comment":"CMDADDRT = $FD65: COMMAND_TABLE"},
        "15434": {"synopsis":"The start-up channel list, copied to CHANS ($5CB6, 31 bytes) by the reset at ROM1 $EC4F.\nEach channel is 5 bytes: the output routine's word, the input routine's word (ROM0\naddresses) and the letter: K, S, R, P, $, B; a $0D follows (probably the end marker). K and\nS share their routines; R, P, $ and B take input through $3F12, which stops with error code\n20. The first four bytes are also MNOP and MNIP's start-up values (SYSVAR_INIT_5BC6).","comment":"K: out $01CC (to ROM1 $DC00), in CHAN_KS_INPUT"},
        "15438": {"comment":"Channel letter 'K'"},
        "15439": {"comment":"S: out $01CC (to ROM1 $DC00), in CHAN_KS_INPUT"},
        "15443": {"comment":"Channel letter 'S'"},
        "15444": {"comment":"R: out CHAN_R_OUTPUT, in $3F12 (error 20)"},
        "15448": {"comment":"Channel letter 'R'"},
        "15449": {"comment":"P: out $01CC (to ROM1 $DC00), in $3F12 (error 20)"},
        "15453": {"comment":"Channel letter 'P'"},
        "15454": {"comment":"$: out $01AF (to a string), in $3F12 (error 20)"},
        "15458": {"comment":"Channel letter '$'"},
        "15459": {"comment":"B: out JSENDA, in $3F12 (error 20)"},
        "15463": {"comment":"Channel letter 'B'"},
        "15464": {"comment":"After the last channel (probably the end marker)"},
        "15465": {"synopsis":"The start-up key map, 3 planes of 70 codes ($D2 bytes) copied to $58E1 by the reset (ROM1\n$EC31); RHTAB = $58E0. ROM1 $D59A reads the code for key E (from 1) in plane D at RHTAB + E\n+ $46 * D; ROM1 $EFD0 (KEY) writes one. This is plane 0: lower-case letters, digits and the\ncodes $C0-$C9 the editor treats as defined keys (KEYDEF_DEFAULTS). Planes 1 and 2 follow\n(KEYMAP_PLANE1, KEYMAP_PLANE2); plane 3 is set sparsely by KEYMAP_P3_FILL."},
        "15535": {"synopsis":"Plane 1 of the start-up key map (KEYMAP_PLANE0), copied to RHTAB + $47: the capitals and\nshifted symbols of plane 0's keys."},
        "15605": {"synopsis":"Plane 2 of the start-up key map (KEYMAP_PLANE0), copied to RHTAB + $8D: further symbols,\ndigits and codes $80 and up."},
        "15675": {"synopsis":"Plane 3's start-up codes, written by ROM1 $ED72 at the reset (DE = here, HL = $59CE, ROM1\n$EC3C): pairs of a code and the distance to the next one's byte; a distance of 0 ends it.\n$59CE is RHTAB + 3 * $46 + 28, so plane 3 gets codes for keys 28, 31, 32, 40, 41, 48, 49,\n50, 59, 66 and 68.","comment":"Key 28: $13"},
        "15677": {"comment":"Key 31: $89"},
        "15679": {"comment":"Key 32: $8A"},
        "15681": {"comment":"Key 40: $88"},
        "15683": {"comment":"Key 41: $8B"},
        "15685": {"comment":"Key 48: $10"},
        "15687": {"comment":"Key 49: $8F"},
        "15689": {"comment":"Key 50: $8C"},
        "15691": {"comment":"Key 59: $8D"},
        "15693": {"comment":"Key 66: $11"},
        "15695": {"comment":"Key 68: $8E, the last"},
        "15697": {"synopsis":"The start-up colours, 20 bytes that ROM1 $EDCC copies to DE; PALETTE's code (ROM1 $EDAC)\ncopies them twice, to $55D8 and $55EC (40 bytes). Each copy is 16 palette colours and 4 more\nthat MODE 2 swaps into entries 0-3 (ROM1 $EDB5, through ROM0's $1899 swap).","comment":"Entries 0-3"},
        "15701": {"comment":"Entries 4-7"},
        "15705": {"comment":"Entries 8-11"},
        "15709": {"comment":"Entries 12-15"},
        "15713": {"comment":"MODE 2's four colours"},
        "15717": {"synopsis":"The statement table CMDADDRT points to ($FD65, SYSVAR_INIT_5BC6): one word for each token\n$90 (DIR) to $F6 (ZOOM), 103 words. STMT_DISPATCH_DE reads it with ROM1 paged in: a word\nwith bit 15 set is a ROM1 routine and runs with ROM1 in, any other a ROM0 routine run with\nROM1 out. Unimplemented statements point to STOP_ERR29.","comment":"DIR: STOP_ERR29"},
        "15719": {"comment":"FORMAT: STOP_ERR29"},
        "15721": {"comment":"ERASE: STOP_ERR29"},
        "15723": {"comment":"MOVE: STOP_ERR29"},
        "15725": {"comment":"SAVE: ROM1 $E019"},
        "15727": {"comment":"LOAD: ROM1 $E019"},
