        "15921": {"comment":"ZOOM: ROM1 $EF76"},
        "15923": {"synopsis":"The font's eighth rows, written by ROM1 $ED72 after FONT_PACKED is unpacked (ROM1 $ED6C: DE\n= here, HL = $51F7, the eighth byte of ','): pairs of a row byte and the distance to the\nnext; a distance of 0 ends it. Sets the descenders of ',', ';', '_', 'g', 'j', 'p', 'q' and\n'y'; the $00 for 'K' is a step, the distance to '_' being over 255.","comment":"',': $08"},
        "15925": {"comment":"';': $08"},
        "15927": {"comment":"'K': $00"},
        "15929": {"comment":"'_': $FF"},
        "15931": {"comment":"'g': $1C"},
        "15933": {"comment":"'j': $10"},
        "15935": {"comment":"'p': $20"},
        "15937": {"comment":"'q': $02"},
        "15939": {"comment":"'y': $1C, the last"},
        "15941": {"comment":"$5A: no code found that reads it"},
        "15942": {"synopsis":"-10000, -1000, -100 and -10, the words ROM1 $F5B8 adds to count a number's digits when it\nprints BC in decimal; a low byte of 0 ends the list, and that end is FONT_PACKED's first two\nbytes ($0000).","comment":"-10000"},
        "15944": {"comment":"-1000"},
        "15946": {"comment":"-100"},
        "15948": {"comment":"-10"},
        "15950": {"synopsis":"The character set, packed: 99 characters (codes 32-130) of 7 rows of 5 bits, read from bit 7\nof each byte on, 434 bytes to the ROM's end. ROM1 $ED3D unpacks it at the reset to 8 bytes\nper character at $5190 (CHARS = $5090), each row in bits 5-1 and an empty eighth row;\nFONT_DESC_FILL then fills the descenders. Its first two bytes also end DEC_POWERS."}
      }
    }
  },
